vents{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/e1e5bdf26b0229513cc532a9f8ae0f216b1fe40c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:55:32Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:41:29Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(scrollbarwrapper): cut the comments the guideline already carries\n\nThe block above the standard properties repeated, word for word, what the\nguideline page now tells consumers. The one about the WebKit fallback keeps\nthe clause a future edit could silently undo -- that the selectors are flat\non purpose -- and drops the diagnosis, which belongs in the pull request.","tree":{"sha":"764f0019eec0e36de8800b52cca82cf7f026545c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/764f0019eec0e36de8800b52cca82cf7f026545c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/e1e5bdf26b0229513cc532a9f8ae0f216b1fe40c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/e1e5bdf26b0229513cc532a9f8ae0f216b1fe40c","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKGUxZTViZGYyNmIwMjI5NTEzY2M1MzJhOWY4YWUwZjIxNmIxZmU0MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/03f2f0ed1caafc67f1c53e6b26eea174bacecc87","sha":"03f2f0ed1caafc67f1c53e6b26eea174bacecc87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/03f2f0ed1caafc67f1c53e6b26eea174bacecc87"}],"sha":"e1e5bdf26b0229513cc532a9f8ae0f216b1fe40c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/e1e5bdf26b0229513cc532a9f8ae0f216b1fe40c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/03f2f0ed1caafc67f1c53e6b26eea174bacecc87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:56:42Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:41:29Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(scrollbarwrapper): scope the WebKit scrollbar rules to engines that use them\n\nSetting scrollbar-width or scrollbar-color on an element makes Chromium\nignore that element''s ::-webkit-scrollbar rules, and this component sets\nboth on every element. The forty lines of WebKit pseudo-element styling\nbelow them have therefore had no effect for some time: measured on a\nrunning page, a scroller renders the engine''s own thin bar at 11px and\nnever the 8px those rules name.\n\nTwo things kept that invisible. The rules were nested inside the\nuniversal selector, which compiles to a descendant combinator, so they\ncould never have reached the root scroller in any engine. And the width\nthey name reads like a fact about the library, which is where a\nconsumer''s temptation to compensate for a fixed number comes from.\n\nPut them behind @supports not (scrollbar-width: thin), where they are\nwhat they actually are -- a fallback for engines without the standard\nproperties -- and write the selectors flat so that fallback also covers\nthe root. No change on any engine that supports the standard properties,\nwhich is every current one. The guideline gains a line saying the bar''s\nwidth belongs to the engine and to reserve room with scrollbar-gutter\nrather than a pixel value.","tree":{"sha":"54ec7f52e5f32dcff39729a00cf8c5acb89f4aee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/54ec7f52e5f32dcff39729a00cf8c5acb89f4aee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/03f2f0ed1caafc67f1c53e6b26eea174bacecc87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"pub