n-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"docs(CUI-61): state the dual-entry rule rather than naming one component","tree":{"sha":"d3baec8c8c54160ad4c10ab9ded9c4e8cee1b757","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/d3baec8c8c54160ad4c10ab9ded9c4e8cee1b757"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/1cc129166889bcacfdd0b255f0730fcb9f4e0708","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/1cc129166889bcacfdd0b255f0730fcb9f4e0708","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDFjYzEyOTE2Njg4OWJjYWNmZGQwYjI1NWYwNzMwZmNiOWY0ZTA3MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/559e88af27d724b432640f2c0eda04fa57d77d0f","sha":"559e88af27d724b432640f2c0eda04fa57d77d0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/559e88af27d724b432640f2c0eda04fa57d77d0f"}],"sha":"1cc129166889bcacfdd0b255f0730fcb9f4e0708","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/1cc129166889bcacfdd0b255f0730fcb9f4e0708"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/b6f21f7a2ba885c907c1e76fce74c7035eb4c664/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:50:33Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:50:33Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"bugfix(tablev2): let a table that never scrolls reach its own right edge\n\nThe scrollbar gutter was reserved unconditionally, on the head row and on\nthe body''s scroll container alike, so a table too short to scroll still\ngave a scrollbar''s width away. Its rows stopped there with it: the\nseparator under each row and the inset marker on a selected one are meant\nto run to the container''s edge, and did not.\n\nReserve it only when the body overflows. The head row sits outside the\nscroll container, so both read one flag and reserve together or not at\nall, which is what the unconditional reservation was bought to guarantee.\nThe flag is the two heights react-window already lays out with --\nrows.length * itemSize against the available height -- rather than a DOM\nread: the scroll container re-renders on every scroll frame, so measuring\nthere would force a layout on each one. It replaces the previous reading\nof react-window''s render indices, which reported how many rows had been\nrendered rather than whether the body overflowed.\n\nThis brings back, narrowed, the trade ac2e2cae removed: the columns shift\nby the gutter when a table becomes scrollable. Head and body now move\ntogether so nothing misaligns, and the reservation is no longer a pixel\nwidth measured in JS and forced with !important.\n\nThe form keeps its unconditional reservation -- there the gutter lands in\npadding nobody sees, and it buys fields that do not slide left when the\nform starts scrolling.","tree":{"sha":"d528d3fcc976c46ab1eaa0dab5fb73aedf99d372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/d528d3fcc976c46ab1eaa0dab5fb73aedf99d372"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/b6f21f7a2ba885c907c1e76fce74c7035eb4c664","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.