://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/b5e9e938da5bb7b0c5e62b9e9aaab58a769b92c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:23:12Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:18:11Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"docs(CUI-60): title each story after the component it documents\n\nSix sidebar titles named something that is not exported: a stale Barchartv2, a\nspaced Constrained Text, a lowercase statusIcon, NoResult for\nUnsuccessfulResult, Radio for RadioGroup, and Templates/Layout for Layout2 while\na different Layout is still exported. With no component manifest the title is\nwhat a reader and an agent see, so each now matches its export. Deep links to\nthe old paths break; the one inbound link in the repo moves with them.\n\nSelectInput documented the same Select as the entry beside it, reading as two\ncomponents. It is titled for what it shows instead: Select composed in a form.\n\ninput.stories.tsx ended in 137 commented-out lines carrying a second meta\ntitled Components/Input/Input. It rendered nothing, but it reads as a real title\nto anyone scanning the file, so it goes.\n\nText and Spacing Utils keep their names: each covers several exports, and naming\neither after one of them would narrow a cluster page into a component page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09e9fb6113a056fd6f745091a089a06574ad7fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/09e9fb6113a056fd6f745091a089a06574ad7fe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/b5e9e938da5bb7b0c5e62b9e9aaa