"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/db41d58ee9fc91895b96a5c0b54c4fcb1f6e1cfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:33:40Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:33:40Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"CUI-58: restyle option group headings after design review\n\nDrop the uppercase, smaller-font heading for a bold one at the option\nfont size, indent a group''s options past its heading, and move the\nseparator from below the heading to above it.\n\nThe menu''s max-height was computed from an r32 row while the options are\ndrawn at r40, so itemsPerScrollWindow never held -- the four and a half\nrows it promised showed 3.6. Both now use r40, and the default rises\nfrom 4 to 7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"512a59167103994047309bc85d3d695eeabc41d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/512a59167103994047309bc85d3d695eeabc41d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/db41d58ee9fc91895b96a5c0b54c4fcb1f6e1cfb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/db41d58ee9fc91895b96a5c0b54c4fcb1f6e1cfb","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKGRiNDFkNThlZTlmYzkxODk1Yjk2YTVjMGI1NGM0ZmNiMWY2ZTFjZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3","sha":"90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3"}],"sha":"db41d58ee9fc91895b96a5c0b54c4fcb1f6e1cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/db41d58ee9fc91895b96a5c0b54c4fcb1f6e1cfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/4554d1ab1435a769576ae1433605048f630aaa0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:41:22Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:41:22Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(CUI-59): type the theme without constraining what may be mounted\n\nDefaultTheme does two jobs in styled-components: it describes what a component\nreads from context, and it constrains what ThemeProvider accepts. Declaring the\nstyled-system scales on it as required did the first job and broke the second,\nsince themes are authored flat -- mounting one stopped compiling across the\napplications that consume this library, most of it test setup and one an\napplication shell.\n\nThe scales are optional in the augmentation, so a flat theme still mounts.\nCoreUIProvidedTheme stays strict for Box, which takes it as an explicit generic\nand never reads DefaultTheme. Nothing is lost: no consumer reads a scale off the\ntheme, while reading a token off it is now checked everywhere the package is\ninstalled -- including the applications that never wrote the augmentation by\nhand and have had it typed as `any` until now.\n\nCoreUiThemeProvider is exported from the stable entry point too. It is not the\nsuccessor to an earlier provider, so next.ts was never its home, and it is the\nonly thing that installs the scales the styled-system props look up.\n\nThemeColors stays as a deprecated alias of ThemeColorToken. Neither entry point\nexported it, but the module it lives in is reachable by path.","tree":{"sha":"ab559665c3b080e6fec34df51dfae139a28cbf16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/ab559665c3b080e6fec34df51dfae139a28cbf16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/co