ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/049efb32fc705b8971eb871d7b4f06de427f9407/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:48:52Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:58:18Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): the Heatmap guideline states all three sort orders\n\nThe page named sortOrder and described only the default, which left a\nreader to find the other two in the type. Documenting the status\nshorthand honestly turned out to be the whole point.\n\n''status'' does not sort. It returns [''Success'', ''Warning'', ''Failed'']\nfiltered by what the grid happens to hold, so it is a whitelist: any\nvalue named otherwise keeps its colour on the cells and loses its legend\nentry, which leaves it neither readable nor filterable on a grid whose\nown guideline says two sections earlier that colour is the only channel.\n\nThat catches the absence value as well, and a status history always has\none, since collection has gaps. So the shorthand is not \"for grids that\nspell their values that way\", it is for charts with exactly three\noutcomes and no fourth. Heatmaps take the comparator.","tree":{"sha":"cc426b2829317e593571b000bc832db0204fdb69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/cc426b2829317e593571b000bc832db0204fdb69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/049efb32fc705b8971eb871d7b4f06de427f9407","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/049efb32fc705b8971eb871d7b4f06de427f9407","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDA0OWVmYjMyZmM3MDViODk3MWViODcxZDdiNGYwNmRlNDI3Zjk0MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07","sha":"38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07"}],"sha":"049efb32fc705b8971eb871d7b4f06de427f9407","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/049efb32fc705b8971eb871d7b4f06de427f9407"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/28891f7c893d0dc7d62bece80a02909335a51e6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:50:57Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:50:57Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"docs(color): correct why the token is preferred, and lead with the rule\n\nThe page claimed that passing theme.statusCritical snapshots the colour and\nmisses a rebrand. Measured under a switched theme, both forms render the same\nvalue: theme.x comes from useTheme() and is already the mounted theme''s. The\nreal difference is that only the token name is checkable, which is all the\nnarrowing is about.\n\nThe override advice also opened on an analogy rather than the instruction, so it\nnow says use a token, and here is what to do when a value genuinely sits outside\nthe palette.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e52b93cbd9734e972cc971329ee03bb460ed449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/2e52b93cbd9734e972cc971329ee03bb460ed449"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/28891f7c893d0dc7d62bece80a02909335a51e6e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/28891f7c893d0dc7d62bece80a02909335a51e6e","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDI4ODkxZjdjODkzZDBkYzdkNjJiZWNlODBhMDI5MDkzMzVhNTFlNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2","sha":"c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2"}],"sha":"28891f7c893d0dc7d62bece80a02909335a51e6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/28891f7c893d0dc7d62bece80a02909335a51e6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:45:39Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:45:39Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"docs(color): say how to use a colour outside the palette\n\nThe narrowed props tell you a raw colour is rejected but not what to do when one\nis genuinely warranted, so the error reads as a wall. styled() is the override,\nits CSS is unchecked, and it beats a token passed as a prop on the same element.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a136f78c2ebb84308a2a613e3f88da0d156b0116","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/a136f78c2ebb84308a2a613e3f88da0d156b0116"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKGM4YTQ3ZjRkMmYwMjRmMWMxNTczM2Y3ODIzMWFlMDQ5ZTczZGMzYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256","sha":"d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256"}],"sha":"c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/c8a47f4d2f024f1c15733f78231ae049e73dc3b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:17:58Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:17:58Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(CUI-59): type the theme so a mistyped Box colour fails to compile\n\nBox composed styled-system''s prop types at their defaults, so every colour and\nscale prop accepted any string. The lookup happens at runtime against\ntheme.colors, so a typo resolved to nothing and the style silently disappeared.\nMirror image: CoreUiThemeProvider installs colors, space and fontSizes, but no\ntype said so, and reading them back from a styled component was an error.\n\nBox''s colour props now take a theme token or one of the three CSS keywords that\ndefer to the context. No raw colour: outside the theme it cannot follow a theme\nswitch or a rebrand. fontSize narrows to the scale''s keys along the way. The\nspace props are deliberately untouched — the scale is an array, so narrowing\nwould reduce it to bare indices and reject the rem values and multi-value\nshorthands in use.\n\nCoreUITheme stays the flat token record it is: themes are authored in that shape\nand branded by spreading one, so a colors field folded into it could be carried\nover stale. The scales live in CoreUIProvidedTheme, which is what DefaultTheme\nis now augmented with — declared from theme.ts so the augmentation ships in\ndist and a consumer stops hand-writing its own.\n\nThe tests that mounted a bare theme through styled-components'' ThemeProvider\nmove to CoreUiThemeProvider; without the scales, token lookups inside them never\nresolved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f57163a9fc70f6103cc7422ae7db1b17306ff42f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/f57163a9fc70f6103cc7422ae7db1b17306ff42f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKGQ2MTYwMTJlYzE1MjA2MzQwODA1YmNhNWZiMDQyZmJkNDlkYjgyNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a","sha":"dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a"}],"sha":"d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/d616012ec15206340805bca5fb042fbd49db8256"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:09:36Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:09:36Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): the scrolling grid keeps room for a cell''s focus ring\n\nA cell paints its hover and focus ring outside its own box, and the\nscroller clips at its padding box, so the ring on any cell along an edge\nwas cut — top and bottom by the hidden vertical overflow, the leading and\ntrailing columns by the horizontal one.\n\nPadding gives it that room, and gives the outermost tiles a little air\nfrom the gutter and the frame besides.","tree":{"sha":"f131aff1ec4ac7c7f8bee04bc5b428f110973224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/f131aff1ec4ac7c7f8bee04bc5b428f110973224"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDM4ZDFlNDBkYTM0ZmE3MDEyMjA3NzM2YjhlY2NlOGJhZTQzNzRjMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f","sha":"6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f"}],"sha":"38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/38d1e40da34fa7012207736b8ecce8bae4374c07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:09:11Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:09:11Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): a Heatmap row owns its cells again\n\nTooltip does not wrap its children transparently: it puts a container\nand a reference div around them. The role sat on the Cell, two levels\nunder, so what each row actually owned was an anonymous div and the\ngridcells were buried beneath it — the one arrangement ARIA does not\nallow, since a row''s required owned elements are its cells.\n\nThe role moves to a wrapper above the Tooltip. That wrapper is the grid\nitem now, which is why it is display: grid — TooltipContainer is\ninline-block, and behind an ordinary block it would shrink to fit a cell\nthat has no width of its own, collapsing every tile to nothing.\n\nThe gap that let this through is worth as much as the fix. The suite\ncounted six gridcells and found them by name, and both stayed true with\nthe cells buried, because neither says anything about who owns them.\nThere is a test for the ownership itself now; it fails on the old shape,\nwith the three nulls of the intervening divs.\n\nEmpty cells were always correct, having no tooltip to be wrapped in —\nwhich is how the grid came to be right for its holes and wrong for every\npainted cell.","tree":{"sha":"547d68bc3a5cc6e6c286baff8ec236dae07c07a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/547d68bc3a5cc6e6c286baff8ec236dae07c07a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDZiZjVkMjYzOTM3OTMyYTk5MjQxMDQyMjJjNjA4NTg4OWU0MDM4M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/93c1e407876662c2753af08920fd1dc0d9c42ae2","sha":"93c1e407876662c2753af08920fd1dc0d9c42ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/93c1e407876662c2753af08920fd1dc0d9c42ae2"}],"sha":"6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/6bf5d263937932a9924104222c6085889e40383f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:00:11Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:26:51Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"CUI-58: add an option-group primitive to Selectv2\n\nA category heading previously had to be faked as a disabled option with a\nsentinel value, which made it indistinguishable from a genuinely unavailable\noption. Select.Group publishes its label to the options nested under it, and the\nmenu renders a heading row per group.\n\nThe virtualised menu list is flattened back to one row per rendered item, since\nreact-window sizes every row alike and would otherwise clip a whole group into a\nsingle option''s height. That also rules out the heading row as the target of an\noption''s aria-describedby, since react-window unmounts it once it scrolls out of\nthe window, so the description points at a hidden element that stays mounted for\nevery group.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dafc4c49027c1a19454f740a441eadef2317a2aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/dafc4c49027c1a19454f740a441eadef2317a2aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDkwZjMxODU3NTNjNjExYjZhY2ViMDc1OTE5ZWU3ZjgxOGFhMmI4YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a","sha":"dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/dc160b1640aa2c3bd76551a5a142ad51754a937a"}],"sha":"90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/90f3185753c611b6aceb075919ee7f818aa2b8b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/93c1e407876662c2753af08920fd1dc0d9c42ae2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:33:38Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T13:33:38Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): the Heatmap gives up its labels and legend before its cells\n\nA narrowing frame used to take it out of the cells alone: the label gutter held\na fixed `labelWidth` and the legend held its column, so the tiles were the only\nthing left to squeeze, and they reached `cellMinWidth` and scrolled while both\nneighbours still had room to give.\n\nReverse the order, cheapest first. The row labels truncate — they keep the whole\nname in a tooltip, so nothing is lost. The legend then drops under the grid and\nturns horizontal, which costs nothing at all. Only then do the cells narrow, and\npast their floor the grid scrolls as before.\n\n`labelWidth` becomes a cap rather than a width, so the gutter also stops leaving\ndead space beside short labels. Two lengths carry the policy: `LABEL_MIN_WIDTH`,\nhow far the labels give way, and `PREFERRED_CELL_WIDTH`, the cell width they give\nway to protect — measured against `cellMinWidth` instead, the cells would always\nreach the floor first and the gutter would only yield once scrolling had started.\n\nWhich way the legend went is measured rather than predicted: the break depends on\nhow many columns the axis has, so there is no breakpoint to write. Reading it back\ncannot oscillate, since going under only makes the legend wider.\n\nAlso fixes two things the responsive work made visible: an x-axis tick wrapped to\ntwo lines inside its single-column cell, and the title was a size and a weight\nabove the `ChartTitle` that `ChartHeader` gives every other chart.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3d74709531c723b868dfef3cf263df301daabd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/e3d74709531c723b868dfef3cf263df301daabd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/93c1e407876662c2753af08920fd1dc0d9c42ae2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY