:"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/df821038373ddd258cc205ff54dbc4aa531af8b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:49:05Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:49:05Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): the Heatmap guideline covers how many slots fit\n\nThe page already asks the reader to decide how wide a slot is, and to say\nwhich rule aggregated it. It said nothing about how many of those slots\nthe frame can hold, which is the decision that comes next and the one the\ncomponent now has an opinion about.\n\nIt sits under the aggregation section rather than beside the time axis,\nbecause it is the same question: slot width decides what a cell hides,\nthe floor decides how much of the grid you can see without scrolling for\nit. Raising the floor to give each slot more room trades one way of\nlosing the pattern for another.","tree":{"sha":"c55f5ad3865c89786031b7f5197b8f82f1be1e76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/c55f5ad3865c89786031b7f5197b8f82f1be1e76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/df821038373ddd258cc205ff54dbc4aa531af8b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/df821038373ddd258cc205ff54dbc4aa531af8b9","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKGRmODIxMDM4MzczZGRkMjU4Y2MyMDVmZjU0ZGJjNGFhNTMxYWY4Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f","sha":"7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f"}],"sha":"df821038373ddd258cc205ff54dbc4aa531af8b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/df821038373ddd258cc205ff54dbc4aa531af8b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:48:53Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:48:53Z","email":"clement.dorosario@scality.com","name":"Clément Do Rosario"},"message":"improvement(charts): tighten the Heatmap props, and let a long axis scroll\n\nFour things Jean-Marc asked for.\n\nlabelWidth was typed string and interpolated into grid-template-columns,\nwhere a length CSS cannot parse does not fail alone — it invalidates the\nwhole declaration, repeat() included, and the grid collapses. It is a\nCSS length now, and it no longer goes near the template: the gutter cell\ncarries its own width, so a bad value costs one label. cellHeight,\ncellGap and cellMinWidth take the same type, and each says what it\nexpects and what it defaults to.\n\nsortOrder and labelMap are read only alongside colorSet — without one\nthere is no legend of ours to order, and the ChartLegendWrapper the\ncaller put above owns it. That was true and unwritten; it is written on\nboth props now.\n\nA cell announced itself as its row and its value, leaving a screen reader\nto count columns to find out when it happened. It carries its slot too,\nfrom the same formatSlot the tooltip uses, so the two cannot drift. And\nthe grid says it is one: role=\"grid\", rows, gridcells — the empty ones\nincluded, or the columns stop lining up for anyone stepping through them.\n\nThen the part that was not asked for as such. Columns share the width\navailable, so a long axis in a narrow frame kept dividing until the cells\nwere slivers a couple of pixels wide: present, aligned, and saying\nnothing. cellMinWidth is a floor, 12px by default, and past it the grid\nscrolls sideways instead.\n\nScrolling is what made the rest of the layout move. The labels sit\noutside the scrolling area rather than pinned inside it, which is worth\nspelling out because pinning is the obvious thing to try and it costs\nthree problems: something opaque to paint, therefore a background the\ncomponent has to be told about, therefore a hover ring bleeding past the\nbox that paints it. Outside, they simply do not move, and the scrollbar\ncovers the tiles alone rather than promising that the labels move too.\nRows became subgrid to keep the two columns level — the scroller takes\nthe rows it is placed in rather than sizing its own — and overflow-y is\nhidden, because a horizontal scrollbar shortens the box by just enough to\nsummon a vertical one.\n\nThe row labels lost role=\"rowheader\" on the way out of the grid: a\nrowheader has to be owned by the row holding its cells. Each row carries\nan aria-label instead, each cell still names its row, and the visible\ncolumn is aria-hidden so none of it is announced twice.","tree":{"sha":"4d9a61f1ce9fa6228a2fd71c2e2fc30eddcf6b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/4d9a61f1ce9fa6228a2fd71c2e2fc30eddcf6b2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294465750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clement-scality","id":294465750,"login":"clement-scality","node_id":"U_kgDOEY0w1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clement-scality","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f","node_id":"C_kwDOClq30NoAKDc5NjVkNzY2MmIwZWYzYzI3OGNkZjc1NTU5NzEwNDBkZmU3ZjhmOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scality/core-ui/commit/1542adbc0606454859ca769d1872ff5999207f27","sha":"1542adbc0606454859ca769d1872ff5999207f27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/1542adbc0606454859ca769d1872ff5999207f27"}],"sha":"7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/7965d7662b0ef3c278cdf7555971040dfe7f8f8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146718185?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JeanMarcMilletScality","id":146718185,"login":"JeanMarcMilletScality","node_id":"U_kgDOCL696Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/commits/34f5d8665b4bb24d1f6ca8f1ba3d99fa8ccc24c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:23:53Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:23:53Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"improvement(constrainedtext): take an explicit alignment and the Text styling props\n\nAlignment could only be inherited from the container or forced to centre, so a\ncaller had no way to state it. Add `align: ''start'' | ''center'' | ''end''`, keeping\n`centered` as a deprecated alias; with neither set the rule stays `inherit`.\n\nAccept the Text props natively and forward them to the internal wrapper, so\n`variant` and its neighbours no longer need a second Text nested inside `text`\nwhile `color` arrives as a prop.\n\nRemoving the file''s `// @ts-nocheck` surfaced an import of `utility-types`,\nwhich is not a dependency of this package and had no other importer. It is\nreplaced with a native indexed access type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d31b7f347341c81ed70f25410c37c1717a4d00d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/trees/d31b7f347341c81ed70f25410c37c1717a4d00d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/core-ui/git/commits/34f5d8665b4bb24d1f6ca8f1ba3d99fa8ccc24c9","verification":{"p