ps://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.tr-064/commits/110a12d854ace0b44eccaf8a81bb1d8103a96148/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:16:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:16:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v5.1.2\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) The mesh topology shows the signal strength of a WLAN device: four bars and the value in dBm (`rx_rcpi`/`tx_rcpi` of the mesh list), the signal to noise and the rating of the FRITZ!Box itself (\"too far away from the access point\", `client_position`) in the tooltip and in the new column \"Signal\" of the table\n- (@GermanBluefox) A device which is not connected any more shows when it was connected last (`last_connected`)\n- (@GermanBluefox) The manufacturer of a device is taken from the FRITZ!Box (`device_manufacturer`, which it knows from LLDP or the DHCP request) and only looked up in the IEEE registries if the box does not name one\n- (@GermanBluefox) The data rates of the mesh topology were shown as download and upload the wrong way round for every link whose first node is the access point - the FRITZ!Box reports `rx`/`tx` from the view of its own node 1, which is not always the upstream side\n- (@GermanBluefox) A click on the missed calls of the tiles (\"FRITZ!Box\" widget of vis-2 and of `ioBroker.devices`) asks whether the counter is reset and sets `calllists.missed.count` to 0. The counter belongs to the adapter, not to the FRITZ!Box - it counts every missed call since the installation, including the complete call list which is read on the first start. The adapter now confirms a written counter right away instead of at the next poll","tree":{"sha":"0d191b96b0871a2c7ee8f836c32dd090729b9196","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.tr-064/git/trees/0d191b96b0871a2c7ee8f836c32dd090729b9196"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.tr-064/git/commits/110a12d854ace0b44eccaf8a81bb1d8103a96148","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.tr-064/commit/110a12d854ace0b44eccaf8a81bb1d8103a96148","node_id":"C_kwDOCmpHGdoAKDExMGExMmQ4NTRhY2UwYjQ0ZWNjYWY4YTgxYmIxZDgxMDNhOTYxNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.tr-064/commit/b52c68ac1415920e213fe9eddb51cc2101496539","sha":"b52c68ac1415920e213fe9eddb51cc2101496539",