633735803bb9efd9261d4be1b18e950","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/14792b917633735803bb9efd9261d4be1b18e950","node_id":"C_kwDOCnS6t9oAKDE0NzkyYjkxNzYzMzczNTgwM2JiOWVmZDkyNjFkNGJlMWIxOGU5NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4","sha":"e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4"}],"sha":"14792b917633735803bb9efd9261d4be1b18e950","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/14792b917633735803bb9efd9261d4be1b18e950"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10495949?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sholzer","id":10495949,"login":"sholzer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk1OTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:39:10Z","email":"sarah.holzer@pimcore.com","name":"Sarah Holzer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:39:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[GraphQL] Allow disabling the GraphQL adapter via configuration (#1158)\n\n* Allow disabling the GraphQL adapter via configuration (#1104)\n\nDatahub is a requirement of other bundles, for example the Data Importer, so it\nis installed on systems that do not want to expose GraphQL at all.\n`pimcore_data_hub.graphql.enabled` (default true) switches the adapter off.\n\nThis is a system level switch, not a permission: it applies to every user,\nadmins included. `plugin_datahub_adapter_graphql` stays assignable and simply\ngrants nothing while the adapter is off.\n\n`supported_types` keeps its meaning - which adapter bundles are installed - and\nis left untouched. The extension resolves the switch against it once and exposes\nthe result as `pimcore_data_hub.enabled_adapter_types`, which\nAdapterAvailabilityService answers from. Only GraphQL, the adapter this bundle\nships itself, carries a switch; adapter types of other bundles are available as\nsoon as they are installed.\n\nEnforced at every entry point:\n\n- the `/pimcore-graphql-webservices/{clientname}` endpoint and the GraphQL\n  Playground answer with 404,\n- configurations of a disabled type are dropped from the Studio listing and\n  cannot be read, created, updated, cloned, imported, exported or deleted,\n- the Data Hub context permission is withheld when no adapter type is enabled at\n  all, which is what removes the entry from every perspective.\n\nExisting configurations are left untouched in the settings store and become\navailable again once the adapter is re-enabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Offer only the adapter types the server enables (#1104)\n\nThe adapter type dropdown was built from the frontend adapter registry filtered\nby permissions alone, so a Data Hub admin - who passes every permission check -\nwas still offered GraphQL on a system where it is switched off, and the create\nrequest then failed at the backend.\n\nA settings provider publishes the enabled types as `data_hub_enabled_adapters`,\nwhich is the channel Studio already uses to hand system level facts to the\nfrontend. A server that does not report them at all leaves every registered\nadapter available, so an older backend behaves as it did before the setting\nexisted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Document disabling the GraphQL adapter (#1104)\n\nDescribes the switch, what it takes away, and how it differs from the\n`plugin_datahub_adapter_graphql` permission it is easily confused with.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"db22b789c67e4dad9dd4feb185e31de92bd32b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/trees/db22b789c67e4dad9dd4feb185e31de92bd32b76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/commits/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4","verification":{"payload":"tree db22b789c67e4dad9dd4feb185e31de92bd32b76\nparent 6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9\nauthor Sarah Holzer <sarah.holzer@pimcore.com> 1790923150 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790923150 +0200\n\n[GraphQL] Allow disabling the GraphQL adapter via configuration (#1158)\n\n* Allow disabling the GraphQL adapter via configuration (#1104)\n\nDatahub is a requirement of other bundles, for example the Data Importer, so it\nis installed on systems that do not want to expose GraphQL at all.\n`pimcore_data_hub.graphql.enabled` (default true) switches the adapter off.\n\nThis is a system level switch, not a permission: it applies to every user,\nadmins included. `plugin_datahub_adapter_graphql` stays assignable and simply\ngrants nothing while the adapter is off.\n\n`supported_types` keeps its meaning - which adapter bundles are installed - and\nis left untouched. The extension resolves the switch against it once and exposes\nthe result as `pimcore_data_hub.enabled_adapter_types`, which\nAdapterAvailabilityService answers from. Only GraphQL, the adapter this bundle\nships itself, carries a switch; adapter types of other bundles are available as\nsoon as they are installed.\n\nEnforced at every entry point:\n\n- the `/pimcore-graphql-webservices/{clientname}` endpoint and the GraphQL\n  Playground answer with 404,\n- configurations of a disabled type are dropped from the Studio listing and\n  cannot be read, created, updated, cloned, imported, exported or deleted,\n- the Data Hub context permission is withheld when no adapter type is enabled at\n  all, which is what removes the entry from every perspective.\n\nExisting configurations are left untouched in the settings store and become\navailable again once the adapter is re-enabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Offer only the adapter types the server enables (#1104)\n\nThe adapter type dropdown was built from the frontend adapter registry filtered\nby permissions alone, so a Data Hub admin - who passes every permission check -\nwas still offered GraphQL on a system where it is switched off, and the create\nrequest then failed at the backend.\n\nA settings provider publishes the enabled types as `data_hub_enabled_adapters`,\nwhich is the channel Studio already uses to hand system level facts to the\nfrontend. A server that does not report them at all leaves every registered\nadapter available, so an older backend behaves as it did before the setting\nexisted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Document disabling the GraphQL adapter (#1104)\n\nDescribes the switch, what it takes away, and how it differs from the\n`plugin_datahub_adapter_graphql` permission it is easily confused with.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv1GOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZEgQAD/ta0EADct9FakuQUP/Smmi\nBq7iofMXD+gd0n/j3z0VzRa2FuRvhd0uqHd2qK936V14rLjpgWSAL3sw7Osi+C1k\n/Spj3NvuM1sr4MEVqqmvZOGW7bGTRyU4iESjktRzmWYHb9u/gFnYSoj/No9OoehY\nc+XZQbmbO/Zmb5MP7Q3dYpE1SYBlDYte5q64hHOfd1e3lJUMCp09M8xHLRq/liEv\nGRlMjpFCQpT3EbNSo84f1FBmULHdEdhjuwwDJ2/dzbrCTSTMj79+KhYxhaG9fvA8\n1gHL69T2v4wEegd63wc21yyScCso3LJRwWyIj/XjKCm+In5VcOoYcVsybflAfa3/\nmoCDx87D24VAYRAvRR8H15RnDwp5qhULWNBNgDFEwn3y+Y4dTBa4GavPw0gLQY17\nIxB4AV/GtjLog9gu1ZuMppD6JqW7Hotd68MmUyNG/FrQBIIFn/nI06EWPM8L1Asa\nRSkjOgv6RofRQI4QyXFYvhe+lY54IL39TnNBHqOJCd51WNON7rT6iOUnpfeOU6qH\n7BBtDCbabHuqvfI1VdSRe2nB4Iek92LQZAZhlEFuAJ4jWfsvw4VvtUl79dG8C2ls\n3uFxEbE21SMrU/BrzaFCMdGBLIG5HOnooGKQDCXAQJy1aRM1fVa7LuK7mtzj/eWC\n2c9yWdnCHxG3VX79obfG\n=+UC1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T06:39:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4","node_id":"C_kwDOCnS6t9oAKGU2NTdhZTYwNzBjMTUzODEwMDZjZGU5NjdlZGY1MzM0Njc3Zjk1YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9","sha":"6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9"}],"sha":"e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/e657ae6070c15381006cde967edf5334677f95b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10495949?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sholzer","id":10495949,"login":"sholzer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk1OTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:30:01Z","email":"sarah.holzer@pimcore.com","name":"Sarah Holzer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:30:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Improvement] Lay the schema definition modal out as two resizable panes (#1153)\n\n* [Improvement] Lay the schema definition modal out as two resizable panes\n\nThe class attribute rail and its panel sat in the ContentLayout sidebar\nslot, which docks to the right edge and resizes from its own left edge.\nThe modal wants the rail first, then the panel, then the available fields\ntree, with a divider between the two panes — which is what SplitLayout\nalready is.\n\nThe sidebar is now a pane: pinned open, sized by the split rather than by\nitself, and with its rail tooltips pointing inwards. The divider between\nthe panes is SplitLayout''s, so it is drawn at rest and draggable from\neither side without the modal positioning it. Read-only configurations\ngive the whole width to the field tree.\n\nAlso drops a dead `.pimcore-content-layout__content` rule; no such class\nis rendered, so the padding it set never applied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Improvement] Take the sidebar props from a 2026.3 canary\n\nThe modal needs `collapsible`, `resizable` and `tooltipPlacement`, which\nlanded in studio-ui-bundle after 2026.2 and are not in any stable release\nyet. The published 2026.3 canary carries them, and a caret range on it\nresolves to 2026.3.0 once that ships, so the manifest need not be touched\nagain then.\n\nNothing else moves: the lockfile change is the package''s own entry, with\nno transitive dependency affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"469b8ebb267058355bda7f1ca4c24bfb26638ed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/trees/469b8ebb267058355bda7f1ca4c24bfb26638ed0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/commits/6502a1481e61b3d62287786be98675cdda255cc9","verification":{"payload":"tree 469b8ebb267058355bda7f1ca4c24bfb26638ed0\nparent 8d88c2650ae6d6b9a3a702c5e6ea0fa9df6a68a6\nauthor Sarah Holzer <sarah.holzer@pimcore.com> 1790922601 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790922601 +0200\n\n[Improvement] Lay the schema definition modal out as two resizable panes (#1153)\n\n* [Improvement] Lay the schema definition modal out as two resizable panes\n\nThe class attribute rail and its panel sat in the ContentLayout sidebar\nslot, which docks to the right edge and resizes from its own left edge.\nThe modal wants the rail first, then the panel, then the available fields\ntree, with a divider between the two panes — which is what SplitLayout\nalready is.\n\nThe sidebar is now a pane: pinned open, sized by the split rather than by\nitself, and with its rail tooltips pointing inwards. The divider between\nthe panes is SplitLayout''s, so it is drawn at rest and draggable from\neither side without the modal positioning it. Read-only configurations\ngive the whole width to the field tree.\n\nAlso drops a dead `.pimcore-content-layout__content` rule; no such class\nis rendered, so the padding it set never applied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Improvement] Take the sidebar props from a 2026.3 canary\n\nThe modal needs `collapsible`, `resizable` and `tooltipPlacement`, which\nlanded in studio-ui-bundle after 2026.2 and are not in any stable release\nyet. The published 2026.3 canary carries them, and a caret range on it\nresolves to 2026.3.0 once that ships, so the manifest need not be touched\nagain then.\n\nNothing else moves: the lockfile change is the package''s own entry, with\nno transitive dependency affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv09pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABoAQAIVqfOsSrqTmEh18taJ5jBYa\nGZG082PDrstQHPPQg3W7i2g7vJhEfV2v+XDz2ZX7CLPvlX2jC74zXCvusUZShZSf\nHHclJDhxI3dXZtME9XA2kjMTzAgRRD+W8XAdSTuNJqgUd2K6RQhorksXeHiXbXmK\nJeSYYRRXpe38dZVbtncl5q2gjlgkOjwSsSW3Ynw+Re7rhnSmvez9JABrISfTZMrt\nKk74aUBizXgnnnc6v1PGG5g2HAOobulFLzqoEOZmjS5dXJBRoMHT9CV21VTgGGnA\nMYXOQw8xHlZiAGizIFkCy2gQEWUqBENeS7xTM4vPXdjSwzztcNZ+mMlRMv9eAZre\n+C2tHa+qJ68BlMUsWtfMwSNOi/03sqiZJzBGilgCPEWU9BJeaCK/P2c/rhcAlMdC\nynd2ZfeqSdX5WMRZhAkYzEdFGsSKl4KICihHS+cKThJzT9nxkDZfwWEkTI/qAjK3\nzYatWJIT1b/QGBewVtHZITvGd2OqSWKWoS/e+ln68YZj0TgOy2t8zvoykgywmWAZ\nwQMinMW8u+qZGcaIVW30U+y5guaINBBvKx7lbDf41wnV0/UgGKqJS