 build","tree":{"sha":"d6e760878d7b256c62a191ac9c4919868c10ca48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/trees/d6e760878d7b256c62a191ac9c4919868c10ca48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/commits/bca080a9435c2e81f835f9e907581a2cd1c4921c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/bca080a9435c2e81f835f9e907581a2cd1c4921c","node_id":"C_kwDOCnS6t9oAKGJjYTA4MGE5NDM1YzJlODFmODM1ZjllOTA3NTgxYTJjZDFjNDkyMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/data-hub/commit/b1d88c8f095926594ad995d174f39d59d509f684","sha":"b1d88c8f095926594ad995d174f39d59d509f684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/b1d88c8f095926594ad995d174f39d59d509f684"}],"sha":"bca080a9435c2e81f835f9e907581a2cd1c4921c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/bca080a9435c2e81f835f9e907581a2cd1c4921c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/998558?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blankse","id":998558,"login":"blankse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5ODU1OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blankse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/commits/b1d88c8f095926594ad995d174f39d59d509f684/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T09:12:14Z","email":"blank@data-factory.net","name":"Sebastian Blank"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T09:12:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Improvement]: Add missing DocumentElementType Renderlet (#1005)\n\n* Add missing DocumentElementType Renderlet\n\nAdds a RenderletType GraphQL type and its query field config generator,\nmodeled on the existing RelationsType, exposing the editable''s\n_editableType/_editableName/id/type/subtype and its single relation\ntarget. Registers the generator service and baselines the new static()\nusage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Refactor RenderletType to satisfy SonarCloud quality gate\n\nExtract a resolveRenderlet() helper for the simple editable fields so the\nrepeated instanceof checks no longer live inside getInstance(), reducing its\ncognitive complexity below the threshold. Drop the unused resolver parameters\nfrom those fields and wrap the relation resolver signature to stay within the\nline-length limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix RenderletType relation resolution and type field\n\nAddress code review feedback on the new Renderlet document element type:\n\n- relation: call load() before getO(). getO() does not lazy-load and $o is\n  stripped from the serialized document in the core cache, so cache-hit\n  documents resolved relation to null despite a valid target.\n- relation: filter unpublished targets, mirroring Relation::getElement().\n  getO() does no publish check and nothing downstream compensated.\n- type: expose the target''s real element type via getData()[''type''] instead\n  of Renderlet::getType(), which is hardcoded to ''renderlet'' and duplicated\n  _editableType.\n- doc: add Renderlet to the supported page element types list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Split long lines to satisfy SonarCloud (php:S103)\n\nBoth lines exceeded the 120-character limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Add RenderletType regression tests and upgrade note\n\nCover the review fixes with container-independent unit tests:\n- relation resolves after load() (cache-hit documents where __sleep()\n  stripped $o)\n- unpublished relation targets are filtered out and not hydrated\n- type exposes the target''s element type instead of the hardcoded\n  ''renderlet''\n\nAnnounce the new document_editableRenderlet type in the 2026.3.0\nupgrade notes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Avoid reflection accessibility bypass in RenderletTypeTest (php:S3011)\n\nConstruct the Service via its real constructor with stubbed dependencies\nand use class-scoped closures instead of ReflectionProperty/\nnewInstanceWithoutConstructor. Track the load() state via an object\ninstead of a by-ref capture (php:S1481 false positive).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Reference RenderletType explicitly in scoped closure (php:S2037)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: blankse <998558+blankse@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ji Jia Jia <kingjia90@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"605c768f4a716ecec82a641ac6ce857f3e50c093","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/trees/605c768f4a716ecec82a641ac6ce857f3e50c093"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/data-hub/git/commits/b1d88c8f095926594ad995d174f39d59d509f684","verification":{"payload":"tree 605c768f4a716ecec82a641ac6ce857f3e50c093\nparent a4e1c5293549923c718a24e7652407d5c354bef5\nauthor Sebastian Blank <blank@data-factory.net> 1786353134 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786353134 +0200\n\n[Improvement]: Add missing DocumentElementType Renderlet (#1005)\n\n* Add missing DocumentElementType Renderlet\n\nAdds a RenderletType GraphQL type and its query field config generator,\nmodeled on the existing RelationsType, exposing the editable''s\n_editableType/_editableName/id/type/subtype and its single relation\ntarget. Registers the generator service and baselines the new static()\nusage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Refactor RenderletType to satisfy SonarCloud quality gate\n\nExtract a resolveRenderlet() helper for the simple editable fields so the\nrepeated instanceof checks no longer live inside getInstance(), reducing its\ncognitive complexity below the threshold. Drop the unused resolver parameters\nfrom those fields and wrap the relation resolver signature to stay within the\nline-length limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix RenderletType relation resolution and type field\n\nAddress code review feedback on the new Renderlet document element type:\n\n- relation: call load() before getO(). getO() does not lazy-load and $o is\n  stripped from the serialized document in the core cache, so cache-hit\n  documents resolved relation to null despite a valid target.\n- relation: filter unpublished targets, mirroring Relation::getElement().\n  getO() does no publish check and nothing downstream compensated.\n- type: expose the target''s real element type via getData()[''type''] instead\n  of Renderlet::getType(), which is hardcoded to ''renderlet'' and duplicated\n  _editableType.\n- doc: add Renderlet to the supported page element types list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Split long lines to satisfy SonarCloud (php:S103)\n\nBoth lines exceeded the 120-character limit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Add RenderletType regression tests and upgrade note\n\nCover the review fixes with container-independent unit tests:\n- relation resolves after load() (cache-hit documents where __sleep()\n  stripped $o)\n- unpublished relation targets are filtered out and not hydrated\n- type exposes the target''s element type instead of the hardcoded\n  ''renderlet''\n\nAnnounce the new document_editableRenderlet type in the 2026.3.0\nupgrade notes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Avoid reflection accessibility bypass in RenderletTypeTest (php:S3011)\n\nConstruct the Service via its real constructor with stubbed dependencies\nand use class-scoped closures instead of ReflectionProperty/\nnewInstanceWithoutConstructor. Track the load() state via an object\ninstead of a by-ref capture (php:S1481 false positive).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Reference RenderletType explicitly in scoped closure (php:S2037)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: blankse <998558+blankse@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ji Jia Jia <kingjia90@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeZXuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAISMQADFVr4isQe9nZcqfQP1dkvUo\nxYMN4pQdNtT7KabsvsDxKfPy7lytGmrMp/ADIuy9Y0i4NOesonuAR7WnG7OJy3p/\nWAUjZnytvLP5PQYZD0RUS9ZbccGvC3/hDjo9TCoWQapz7WC7duKfCJcUDGqrDPeA\nFcNd6Sgfve+Lw6pN/vZboghjpM3OGBeE6SCDF5jG6naAyUZMkdG6m52K3JbqRZ8S\nAAMNPT30MZYVEkX0QjcudHidHCZF0lAnwvSjn2ynm3x6ljWFATo2iobu5wxa507s\n/HrJb2E00K5arBOEG0AgJcUwxgIOuceBpwc2VbBAq2NyqcaHOzh7R9/yDupxnGIg\nj1KhHdFzQz/4fXJ5E5RYLgHtQJrVsMJTIrZe1XfMVUkZ6WhAGzAcNU+vwUS5jYwy\n5XsskW2RQRq+jMr6HzeNQ3E6lLQ2khDDnAIuv29xIutXmjl5971vrfTwPTWj0W5o\nJer5fXwcdv/I1Rct47ViwZ0TZeqe1EVUwtM1My8TMAmPvxmrJd9OXKTRLlEz6RIs\nKAEaFujCjEXC2VLThyncFlspqS4/gM+80bXU8GktQz5Lty0cRz4QzxdXNGEE5J69\nTEbiuLdnAwAlKAKzOgQtgDHxSGtn0CqMRVR6PVhy9xDJAqkJCXG/l2fuJZ3wTQ2P\nvCwREeVyD3QNv5chQJ+C\n=pNSc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T09:12:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/