hub.io/commits/c8e135597c9ea972de6529b6050baa03d77147c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/cd0395940e5489985c7a85fe9015d1ff50faa8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:26:57Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:26:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/playwright (#48)\n\n* docs: mark MFE Slices 10–17 done, close Q22 as D104\n\n- Slices 10–14 and the Slice 16 strip merged in PR #45, Slice 15 in PR #46;\n  README status block, slice table and slice headers now say so\n- D104: Slices 16 and 17 done on the maintainer''s call. Q22 closes without a\n  written issue list; Slice 16''s footer-down check never ran and moves to\n  Slice 9''s failure-isolation specs\n- Q22 moved to questions-closed-q18-q21.md, with the links to it repointed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: make \"Try again\" recover a remote whose load failed (D106)\n\nThree caches held a failed remote load, and a retry has to get past all of\nthem: React.lazy''s (already handled by a new lazy per attempt), the\nmodule @module-federation/vite compiles `import(''homepage/Homepage'')` into\n(its pending promise is created once per page), and the browser''s module\nmap (a failed module fetch is remembered for its URL).\n\nOn a retry, MfeRemoteMount now calls reloadRemote instead of the import:\nit re-registers the remote with `force: true` at\n`remoteEntry.js?mf-retry=<attempt>` and loads it through the federation\nhost. The four shell wrappers pass the new `exposedModule` prop.\n@module-federation/runtime is pinned at 2.9.0 to match the plugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add Playwright and the e2e project''s boundary tags\n\n- @playwright/test 1.63 as a root dev dependency, with `e2e:build` and\n  `e2e` scripts (their files land in the next commit)\n- `type:e2e` / `scope:e2e` tags, and a constraint that lets the suite\n  import no workspace code: it tests what shipped\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the Playwright E2E suite over the composed production build (Slice 9)\n\nRuns against a local production build of the shell and all four remotes,\non its own ports (3100, 4274-4277) so a running dev server is never\nreused. `E2E_BASE_URL` points it at a deployed site for Slice 8.\n\nCovers the composed happy path, design-system styles inside each remote\n(on utilities only that remote''s lib uses), failure isolation per remote,\nthe footer-down look (D104), bounded retry, and load vs render failures.\nEvery spec was seen failing against a deliberately broken build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: run the Playwright E2E suite on every pull request\n\nA second job beside `gates`: installs Chromium, builds the E2E stack with\n`pnpm e2e:build` (never `pnpm build`, which bakes the dev origins), runs\nthe suite, and uploads the report on failure. Slice 8''s deploy jobs will\ndepend on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record Slice 9 as built, D105–D106, and close Q23\n\n- D105: the E2E stack''s own ports, R3 living in the shell''s stylesheet,\n  and style checks on utilities only one lib uses\n- D106: the retry fix and the three caches it gets past; closes Q23\n- Slice 9 built (24/24, 28 files, negative-control table); Slice 8 gains\n  a CloudFront error-caching verification for the `?mf-retry=` URL\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5312be20666b6d1ee4e34aae68022166b200258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/a5312be20666b6d1ee4e34aae68022166b200258"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/cd0395940e5489985c7a85fe9015d1ff50faa8ad","verification":{"payload":"tree a5312be20666b6d1ee4e34aae68022166b200258\nparent 8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790234817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790234817 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/playwright (#48)\n\n* docs: mark MFE Slices 10–17 done, close Q22 as D104\n\n- Slices 10–14 and the Slice 16 strip merged in PR #45, Slice 15 in PR #46;\n  README status block, slice table and slice headers now say so\n- D104: Slices 16 and 17 done on the maintainer''s call. Q22 closes without a\n  written issue list; Slice 16''s footer-down check never ran and moves to\n  Slice 9''s failure-isolation specs\n- Q22 moved to questions-closed-q18-q21.md, with the links to it repointed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: make \"Try again\" recover a remote whose load failed (D106)\n\nThree caches held a failed remote load, and a retry has to get past all of\nthem: React.lazy''s (already handled by a new lazy per attempt), the\nmodule @module-federation/vite compiles `import(''homepage/Homepage'')` into\n(its pending promise is created once per page), and the browser''s module\nmap (a failed module fetch is remembered for its URL).\n\nOn a retry, MfeRemoteMount now calls reloadRemote instead of the import:\nit re-registers the remote with `force: true` at\n`remoteEntry.js?mf-retry=<attempt>` and loads it through the federation\nhost. The four shell wrappers pass the new `exposedModule` prop.\n@module-federation/runtime is pinned at 2.9.0 to match the plugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add Playwright and the e2e project''s boundary tags\n\n- @playwright/test 1.63 as a root dev dependency, with `e2e:build` and\n  `e2e` scripts (their files land in the next commit)\n- `type:e2e` / `scope:e2e` tags, and a constraint that lets the suite\n  import no workspace code: it tests what shipped\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the Playwright E2E suite over the composed production build (Slice 9)\n\nRuns against a local production build of the shell and all four remotes,\non its own ports (3100, 4274-4277) so a running dev server is never\nreused. `E2E_BASE_URL` points it at a deployed site for Slice 8.\n\nCovers the composed happy path, design-system styles inside each remote\n(on utilities only that remote''s lib uses), failure isolation per remote,\nthe footer-down look (D104), bounded retry, and load vs render failures.\nEvery spec was seen failing against a deliberately broken build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: run the Playwright E2E suite on every pull request\n\nA second job beside `gates`: installs Chromium, builds the E2E stack with\n`pnpm e2e:build` (never `pnpm build`, which bakes the dev origins), runs\nthe suite, and uploads the report on failure. Slice 8''s deploy jobs will\ndepend on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record Slice 9 as built, D105–D106, and close Q23\n\n- D105: the E2E stack''s own ports, R3 living in the shell''s stylesheet,\n  and style checks on utilities only one lib uses\n- D106: the retry fix and the three caches it gets past; closes Q23\n- Slice 9 built (24/24, 28 files, negative-control table); Slice 8 gains\n  a CloudFront error-caching verification for the `?mf-retry=` URL\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtNDBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAON4QAKG2AuzqUwYfzBUubMvuHT+c\n06JWuaqEVuPo0MnCqf6GF8nbrc88X7t/VA5/ZAb2LVfL1wgnKQ4aJ+ETDD3mudsv\nZDBHdrn2NEfrrFOr3/ZixIrthgOYmjV8HA2/VuV4UoHQWNgOYEsWQrHdDYwIWHXw\nQal07jMstlnpeUiqjazYIsxKJiEofcF4M/Fc3r8Yy0ZvBfTLcz+FaMBYUtEz2k0T\noNt5VZR6Z2Z8PeqvstMliSvuwMhQOt3rhy9DWiIRw4y6ue/jd4k8HbkQhphEUMAz\nKNzj6dsvPzt7T+Wcd6j3Ug/t9xp4Unc8O80sYuDV9WMDqmFySnnNYkOlJuoYaqz2\nDvFgeU+X6+aaW5P78xB+ypVn35bMeOEND/x3vGD4f2PLbVhygfRc5OvJlFmuLOc2\n11XRE/6ZbowZ/L1q+9aKQwEZEJeVWhpDkxTcfbGRxadtseH6/j9pwavFS3Qt2VtA\nY8+tgPsDWWel3EtQLxeM+HRmpjxVcDPTXP8aQficHxCss1tPNbP6UN2GKb1SCQ1I\nb6JJ9o09eLq2AKQqfknuoX5B1TI4m/9mfpbJnzPhBz+JXsqB/2DcV8mjqeYIwcPt\ntlWCiWmnHArxD9iv23yoNJ/8VrGZyPY2pSSzZbKgrlr7Q3/XPQ+1888I+yktxIoO\n+Dm6c0DXQ7LFVQ1zkB9D\n=TZI8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T07:26:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/cd0395940e5489985c7a85fe9015d1ff50faa8ad","node_id":"C_kwDOCok6WdoAKGNkMDM5NTk0MGU1NDg5OTg1YzdhODVmZTkwMTVkMWZmNTBmYWE4YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b","sha":"8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b"}],"sha":"cd0395940e5489985c7a85fe9015d1ff50faa8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/cd0395940e5489985c7a85fe9015d1ff50faa8ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:39:35Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:39:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/enhancements fixes (#47)\n\n* feat: update the Experience bullets from the resume and scope the admin platform''s design system to the department\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: move the header''s section nav onto shadcn NavigationMenu\n\nAdd shadcn''s navigation-menu to ui-primitives (arrow functions, cn from\nshared-utils, and Tabler''s chevron in place of lucide-react), plus radix-ui\nand class-variance-authority. Wrap it as NavMenu in ui-components with the\ndesign''s plain text-link styling, and render HeaderNav through it — the\nlinks gain a list structure and arrow-key focus movement. HeaderNavLink is\nretired; its path-prefix spec moves into HeaderNav''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: move the shadcn primitives from Radix to Base UI\n\nRegenerate navigation-menu on Base UI (shadcn base-vega style, Tabler\nicons from the CLI), swap radix-ui for @base-ui/react, and drop the\nviewport prop NavMenu no longer needs. Keep TanStack Start''s server-fn\ncompiler off Base UI''s pre-bundles in the shell, pin the shell to port\n3000 with strictPort, and record why @base-ui/react is not a federation\nshared dependency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the Experience accordion on shadcn Accordion\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Accordion primitive with theme keyframes driven by\nBase UI''s --accordion-panel-height, and an Accordion wrapper in\nui-components that draws the design''s +/- ring and hover tint. The\nExperience section renders through it, with the row split into header and\nbody files; the hand-rolled entry and its open-state toggle are retired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: move the mobile menu onto a shadcn Sheet and add the Button primitive\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Button and Sheet primitives, and a MenuSheet wrapper\nthat draws the header''s ink panel below the bar. The header''s two-bar toggle\nbecomes the sheet''s trigger (Base UI supplies aria-expanded/aria-controls),\nand the sheet is non-modal so the toggle stays reachable while open. Escape,\nan outside press and a link tap close it. The hand-rolled overlay is retired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: teach cn the theme''s radius tokens\n\ntailwind-merge cannot read the theme, so rounded-pill was not grouped with a\nshadcn primitive''s rounded-md and both stayed on the element, leaving the\ncorner to stylesheet order. Register the --radius-* names alongside the\nfont sizes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw the portfolio chips on shadcn Badge\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Badge primitive and rebuild MetaChip on it, with an\ninverse tone for chips on dark cards. Add TagChip, an outline Badge that can\nrender as the list item itself, and move the Technologies list and the work\ncard''s Live chip onto them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw every pill with shadcn Button variants, centred on cap-height\n\nPillLink styles its anchor with buttonVariants (Base UI''s Button forces\nrole=\"button\", so it never renders an <a>) and gains accent and outline-ink\nvariants for ink surfaces. The contact block''s LinkedIn pill and the detail\npage''s closing pills move onto it. Labels are trimmed to cap-height inside a\nfixed height, so the space above the capitals equals the space below the\nbaseline and icons line up with the capitals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: give the About and Contact eyebrows the accent rule the other sections use\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the shadcn Skeleton primitive and a theme-toned LoadingSkeleton\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw a region skeleton while a remote''s lazy import is pending\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: give each federated remote its loading skeleton\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8127cb8a263fe9315335a304d61bb446398660b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/b8127cb8a263fe9315335a304d61bb446398660b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/8aba011ec40a373fb4cdc3e453d48323c4fb199b","verification":{"payload":"tree b8127cb8a263fe9315335a304d61bb446398660b\nparent 6073c9f00763af4c3cf0804f0ab5920fc0603cb5\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790203175 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790203175 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/enhancements fixes (#47)\n\n* feat: update the Experience bullets from the resume and scope the admin platform''s design system to the department\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: move the header''s section nav onto shadcn NavigationMenu\n\nAdd shadcn''s navigation-menu to ui-primitives (arrow functions, cn from\nshared-utils, and Tabler''s chevron in place of lucide-react), plus radix-ui\nand class-variance-authority. Wrap it as NavMenu in ui-components with the\ndesign''s plain text-link styling, and render HeaderNav through it — the\nlinks gain a list structure and arrow-key focus movement. HeaderNavLink is\nretired; its path-prefix spec moves into HeaderNav''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: move the shadcn primitives from Radix to Base UI\n\nRegenerate navigation-menu on Base UI (shadcn base-vega style, Tabler\nicons from the CLI), swap radix-ui for @base-ui/react, and drop the\nviewport prop NavMenu no longer needs. Keep TanStack Start''s server-fn\ncompiler off Base UI''s pre-bundles in the shell, pin the shell to port\n3000 with strictPort, and record why @base-ui/react is not a federation\nshared dependency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the Experience accordion on shadcn Accordion\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Accordion primitive with theme keyframes driven by\nBase UI''s --accordion-panel-height, and an Accordion wrapper in\nui-components that draws the design''s +/- ring and hover tint. The\nExperience section renders through it, with the row split into header and\nbody files; the hand-rolled entry and its open-state toggle are retired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: move the mobile menu onto a shadcn Sheet and add the Button primitive\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Button and Sheet primitives, and a MenuSheet wrapper\nthat draws the header''s ink panel below the bar. The header''s two-bar toggle\nbecomes the sheet''s trigger (Base UI supplies aria-expanded/aria-controls),\nand the sheet is non-modal so the toggle stays reachable while open. Escape,\nan outside press and a link tap close it. The hand-rolled overlay is retired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: teach cn the theme''s radius tokens\n\ntailwind-merge cannot read the theme, so rounded-pill was not grouped with a\nshadcn primitive''s rounded-md and both stayed on the element, leaving the\ncorner to stylesheet order. Register the --radius-* names alongside the\nfont sizes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw the portfolio chips on shadcn Badge\n\nAdd shadcn''s base-vega Badge primitive and rebuild MetaChip on it, with an\ninverse tone for chips on dark cards. Add TagChip, an outline Badge that can\nrender as the list item itself, and move the Technologies list and the work\ncard''s Live chip onto them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw every pill with shadcn Button variants, centred on cap-height\n\nPillLink styles its anchor with buttonVariants (Base UI''s Button forces\nrole=\"button\", so it never renders an <a>) and gains accent and outline-ink\nvariants for ink surfaces. The contact block''s LinkedIn pill and the detail\npage''s closing pills move onto it. Labels are trimmed to cap-height inside a\nfixed height, so the space above the capitals equals the space below the\nbaseline and icons line up with the capitals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: give the About and Contact eyebrows the accent rule the other sections use\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the shadcn Skeleton primitive and a theme-toned LoadingSkeleton\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw a region skeleton while a remote''s lazy import is pending\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: give each federated remote its loading skeleton\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtFUnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXsYQABDllm677aFrkGkfHGLbCR6m\n54Bp+9PLB9eEHKrusx4x/Nz0Jwd3DEwpb0jrJhy2vM6vm0WAcMkgJimFk5Hx5plR\nnocG1Z8/xv8hptY4EV+zWR7AGDB7HtjUr82BLUDDpG2DrRZtMMyJleuUZjLQ5kNL\nlkVYAk3FeVMWwRZr/9PgTcwnJYkB3UJodzMIGVQP7VuJEBg0lvyyoHWAC+m9muVB\nDL0GC4/5/ZSe/5OyJMogitTgObIo5ve3MjILu4wZWn0whjiDbtOUI4XTKIU4YeVY\nI6tlx5sLmh4l0YaixRLYyEXJoSpJeDryZ3ZOSqareBsmL85PcMr8FrOxIrNLZNkd\niTuZ8pyzGsxveoSGmruQVpj5Cz3KwTmCwSqsCH3C17TUuF4BmeZUmUqVl4YE+0aL\nQtGv2C+98csQEtMT4MWLZ/fUu2PQ1L/jj4LqUJGN38ZgJeHJeEtLDggvcqcHUkED\nco0R60F+YesXJP