wNzNjOWYwMDc2M2FmNGMzY2YwODA0ZjBhYjU5MjBmYzA2MDNjYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2","sha":"ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2"}],"sha":"6073c9f00763af4c3cf0804f0ab5920fc0603cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/6073c9f00763af4c3cf0804f0ab5920fc0603cb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:26:09Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:26:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/new skin (#45)\n\n* docs: record D76-D81 and the design source move for the 2026-09-22 redesign\n\nTwo new design exports replace the look of every surface in the plan. The six\ndecisions that had to be settled before any slice could be written:\n\n- D76 — the _design/ exports supersede the live v3 site as the design source,\n  site-wide. Content stays on 39bbe56 (D53). Retires the invented Header and\n  Footer of D59/D70.\n- D77 — the eight ported items survive; the design''s six-project list is read\n  as a card-grid layout spec. The ported slug wins in all four conflicts.\n- D78 — the HTML description and the videos are kept, as blocks the design\n  does not draw. This is what leaves D69 and its sanitizer with a subject.\n- D79 — the footer remote keeps the strip only; the dark blocks above it\n  belong to their pages. Four remotes survive; the cost is stated.\n- D80 — the redesign runs before deployment and E2E. Slices 8 and 9 keep\n  their numbers: renumbering would rewrite 97 references across 40 files,\n  most of them in source.\n- D81 — SITE_SECTIONS becomes the design''s five anchors and --spacing-header\n  splits into two tokens that are not derivable from each other.\n\ndesign-sources.md is mostly content moved out of README.md so the index can\nstay under its 200-line cap. Its new material is a finding and two defects:\n\n- _design/ is gitignored (.gitignore:9, added in 7b3bf60 when it was a scratch\n  directory), so every design link resolves on one machine and nowhere else.\n  Three options recorded; the plan does not resolve it unilaterally.\n- the exports contradict themselves on the years figure, and both hero images\n  are explicit placeholders. Raised as Q21 and Q18 rather than filled in.\n\nopen-questions.md goes from none open to four (Q18-Q21), each blocking one\nfield or region rather than a whole slice. The seventeen closed rows carry\nover intact; a sentence claiming twenty-one closed questions is corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add slices 10-16, the redesign''s seven build steps\n\nThe build instructions derived from D76-D81. They run after slices 5-7 and\nbefore 8-9 (D80).\n\n- 10 design foundation — solo. Nine palette tokens, three typefaces, the inset\n  rounded frame, five shared components justified by counted call sites.\n  --color-page and --color-ink both change value, so every existing component\n  shifts appearance without being edited.\n- 11 content model — solo. The new field set, and the per-file ownership table.\n  This slice exists because the 5-7 wave collided on shared-types and\n  shared-fixtures after the plan claimed they were disjoint; freezing the whole\n  content model before any agent starts is that correction applied.\n- 12 header — the only slice permitted to touch SITE_SECTIONS (D81). Records\n  that the two exports draw different bars, which makes the variant a new prop\n  crossing the federation boundary.\n- 13 homepage A — specs strip, hero, Work grid. Three breakpoints, not two.\n- 14 homepage B — Experience, Skills, About, Contact. The accordion opens index\n  0 on load, and gets real button semantics as a recorded divergence from the\n  export''s div-with-click-handler.\n- 15 portfolio detail — twelve regions, plus the two blocks D78 keeps that the\n  design does not draw. Both flagged invented, control by control.\n- 16 footer strip — its real content is the degradation D79 created: a downed\n  footer leaves the dark block ending on a bare rule.\n\nEach slice restates its binding decisions with a line of local meaning. Those\nare copies and they drift; decisions.md remains the source of truth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the design foundation and re-skin the shell onto it\n\nReplaces the v3 palette with the 2026-09-22 design exports'' token set (D76)\nand moves every surface the shell owns onto it. The exports are a\nspecification, not source: they are inline-styled <x-dc> templates, and\nnothing of that shape is copied -- every literal is re-expressed as a theme\ntoken.\n\nThe theme retires --color-page (there is no white in the new design) and\nsplits --spacing-header into --spacing-nav (56px) and --spacing-anchor (84px)\nper D81. Those are different numbers, and the single token that served both is\nwhy a section heading landed flush against the nav''s bottom rule. The old\ntoken stays defined, now inert.\n\nFive components join libs/ui/components because each has three or more call\nsites across the two exports -- D29''s threshold met by inspection, not\nanticipation. Eyebrow takes a surface rather than a colour so that mint on\npaper has no name: the design uses #3FD9A4 only inside ink sections, and a\nprop that cannot express the wrong pairing beats a comment saying not to.\nSectionHeading takes its two halves separately because the split point is\neditorial and a parser would guess it.\n\nThe shell''s content region loses its max-width and padding: the design''s\nsections run edge to edge and carry their own, because the alternating surface\nand ink backgrounds have to touch the card''s sides. The card''s overflow-hidden\nis what clips every dark section to the corner radius.\n\nlibs/ui/components gains a @portfolio/shared-utils dependency. Slice 10''s file\nlist said it needed none; all five components merge a className through cn,\nwhich lives there. It surfaced as an Nx project-reference sync failure rather\nthan a missing import (D83).\n\nThe Card primitive still names bg-page, now a dead token. ProfileCard\noverrides it through cn and is its only consumer, so it is harmless -- left in\nplace because D25 forbids hand-editing generated shadcn output.\n\nRefs D76, D81, D83, D84.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: load the webfonts from a link tag, not a CSS import\n\nCarlito, JetBrains Mono and Inter come from the Google Fonts CDN, which is\nwhat the design exports themselves reference (Q20 -> D82).\n\nThe first implementation put an @import url(...) at the top of\nlibs/ui/theme/src/theme.css, so that one declaration would cover the shell and\nthe four standalone remote dev surfaces. Vite''s CSS pipeline silently dropped\nit: the served stylesheet carried no @import and no @font-face, the page made\nzero requests to either font origin, and it rendered in system fallbacks --\nwith typecheck, lint, 161 specs and the file-size gate all green. A font that\nnever arrives is a page in a different face, not a broken one, so nothing in\nthe build could see it. It was caught by reading document.fonts and the\nresource timings in the running page.\n\nSo the request is a <link> in the shell''s document head, and in each remote''s\nindex.html for its standalone surface. That is also the faster shape: a CSS\n@import cannot begin its request until the importing sheet has been fetched\nand parsed, which serializes two round trips before any text can paint in the\nright face.\n\nThe four index.html files repeat the same three lines. There is no shared HTML\nlayer between the remotes, and introducing one to save twelve lines would\ncouple four independently deployed apps.\n\napps/shell/src/styles.css changes only in its comment, which had been left\nasserting that the theme carries the font @import -- pointing the next reader\nstraight at the mechanism that failed.\n\nSlice 8 inherits the CSP: style-src must allow fonts.googleapis.com and\nfont-src fonts.gstatic.com, or this regresses in production exactly as\nsilently.\n\nRefs D82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: clear the fixed header''s overlap and offset the anchor links\n\nThe nav bar is pinned flush to the top of the viewport (D84), which made two\nexisting measurements wrong.\n\nThe Header remote''s row carried h-header, D43''s single 4rem token. With the\nbar''s own padding that made the bar 97px while the spacer holding content down\nis 56px, so 41px of the page sat underneath it. Invisible only because the\nhomepage hero is currently a flat block; it would have clipped the hero''s\nspecs strip the moment Slice 13 landed. The row now sizes from its padding,\nwhich is 57px, and content clears the bar by 27px.\n\nBoth homepage sections carried scroll-mt-header, and a utility class beats the\ntheme''s [id] { scroll-margin-top } base rule -- so anchors resolved to 64px and\nnot the 84px the design states. A bar 56px tall wants more than 56px of scroll\nmargin or the heading lands flush against its bottom rule, which is why D81\nsplit the token in the first place. Clicking a nav link now lands the section\nat 84px.\n\nThe two remote loading placeholders reserved the old 64px; they reserve the\nreal bar''s height now, so hydration does not shift the page. The\nmfe-loading-placeholder spec passes the class as an arbitrary string and is\nretargeted so no file names a token that is about to go; its assertion is\nunchanged.\n\nThat leaves --spacing-header with zero readers. D81 assigned its removal to\nSlice 12 on the reasoning that the readers were spread across the three-way\nSITE_SECTIONS contract; they were not, they were four spacing call sites, and\nthese are all four. The token is left defined and inert rather than deleted:\nunder independent deployment a header remote built before this change still\nasks for h-header, and the class only generates while some source names it.\nDeleting it degrades an old remote to content height rather than a wrong one,\nwhich is Slice 8''s problem to weigh, not this commit''s.\n\nMobile still overlaps by 25px: at 375px the interim nav wraps to two lines and\nthe bar is 81px. Slice 12 closes it -- the design''s mobile nav is a 44px\nhamburger, not wrapped links.\n\nRefs D81, D84.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D82-D84 and what building Slice 10 found wrong in the plan\n\nThree of the four decisions here are corrections to the plan found by building\nagainst it rather than by reading it, which is the pattern the README already\nwarns about after the 5-7 wave.\n\nD82 closes Q20: the three typefaces come from the Google Fonts CDN, via a\n<link>. It is written up at length because the failure it records has no\nsignal -- an @import in the theme was silently dropped by Vite and the site\nrendered in system faces with every gate green. Q20''s own wording said \"a\n<link> in the shell''s document head\"; the implementation talked itself out of\nit for a real reason and lost an afternoon to it.\n\nD83 records that this slice''s file list was wrong about\nlibs/ui/components/package.json. It claimed nothing new was needed; all five\ncomponents merge a className through cn, which lives in a package\nui-components did not depend on.\n\nD84 records the nav bar being flush to the viewport top rather than floating\nat the frame inset as both exports draw it.\n\ndesign-sources.md gains the Design -> code delta table plan-design-links.md\nrequires and the plan did not have. Without it, a divergence reads as a defect\n-- and Slice 12 would have rebuilt the export''s floating bar from the design,\nsilently reverting D84. The table says so explicitly.\n\nSlice 10 gains a \"What this slice leaves open\" section: the 25px mobile header\noverlap, the five components carrying R3''s exposure until something mounts\nthem, and --spacing-header''s now-zero readers.\n\nThe README''s status table is corrected -- it still read \"Slices 3-7 built,\nawaiting review\" and named only PR #42 as merged, while #43 and #44 are both\nin this branch''s history.\n\nparallelization.md carries the slices 10-16 dependency graph, the second\nwave''s seam table and its per-slice file estimates. That work predates this\nsession and was sitting uncommitted; it is included here at the maintainer''s\ninstruction. One detail in it is already stale: its slice 10 row does not\nmention the shared-utils dependency, which D83 now records.\n\nRefs D76, D81, D82, D83, D84. Closes Q20.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: close Q18, Q19 and Q21 as D85-D87 before the redesign wave\n\nAll four questions raised on 2026-09-22 by reading the new design exports are\nnow closed, and three of them closed by measuring the repo against the export\nrather than by the agent sent to build against it. That ordering is the whole\npoint: the README''s warning after the 5-7 wave is that plan corrections keep\narriving from builders, and these three would each have arrived that way.\n\nD85 makes the detail and homepage heroes typographic. The question offered\n\"crop an existing screenshot\" as the cheap option and it was not available:\nthe widest asset in the repo is 1.80 -- a 540x300 card thumbnail -- against\n16/7''s 2.29, and four of the eight items are mobile-screenshot-only with no\ncroppable candidate at all. The region and its ratio survive; only the fill\nchanges, so hero and heroCaption come off PortfolioItem entirely.\n\nD86 derives the gallery''s span and ratio from the authored dimensions and\nbuckets them to the design''s two. Three of Q19''s own premises were wrong: it\nis 35 gallery images and not 43 (the other eight are thumbnail), its warning\nthat derivation breaks the design''s rhythm is backwards (the design is 12\nportrait tiles to 8 landscape, the catalogue 26 to 9), and the authored\nwidth/height are display dimensions rather than intrinsic -- but they preserve\nthe ratio exactly, which is all derivation needs.\n\nD87 replaces both of the design''s years figures. 2011 to 2026 is 15 years, not\nthe 14 the question computed; 10+ anchors on no row in the experience list;\n13+ anchors cleanly on the 2013 Cricket Manager title. So the strip reads 15+\nyears shipping and the About stat reads 13+ years in lead & architect roles,\nboth derivable from the table printed directly beneath them.\n\nTwo of these change what a slice builds, not just what it knows -- D85 removes\ntwo fields from Slice 11''s deliverable and D86 turns Slice 15''s gallery from\nauthored data into derived presentation -- so the binding blocks of slices 11,\n13, 14 and 15 are rewritten, and Slice 11''s field table and Slice 15''s Hero and\nGallery sections with them.\n\nQ18/Q19/Q21 go to a third closed-questions file: appending them to the second\nwould have taken it to ~558 lines, over the 500-line cap. Q20 stays where it\nclosed so its existing links keep resolving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the shared UiIcon and the design''s second breakpoint\n\nUiIcon is the sixth shared component (D93), added by the coordinator ahead\nof the redesign wave rather than reported-and-waited: four slices need it —\n12 for the mobile overlay and the detail bar, 13 for the hero CTA and every\nWork card, 14 for the Experience accordion, 15 for the link pills.\n\nIt extends D75 rather than reopening it — Tabler, not a second icon\nlibrary — and keeps SocialIcon''s decorative contract, so the accessible name\nstays on the element around it.\n\n--breakpoint-wide corrects Slice 10, whose comment read \"the frame''s inset\nand its one breakpoint\". The homepage export distinguishes three bands and\ngives the middle one its own hero lede layout, so collapsing to two is a\nvisible regression at tablet width that fails by looking fine (D97).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the content model, the header and the homepage on the new design\n\nSlices 11-14 of the MFE plan, committed as one change because nothing\nsmaller compiles (D92): Slice 11 removes projectGroups, cardId and\nhero.links, Slice 12 re-points SITE_SECTIONS, and Slices 13-14 are what\nmakes the homepage read the new shape.\n\nThe content model gains the design''s per-item fields and the homepage''s\nfour lower panels. SITE_SECTIONS becomes the design''s five anchors, with\nSECTION_IDS so no file outside the fixture writes one of those strings\n(D96). The header renders two variants -- five anchors on the homepage,\nbrand + back-link on a detail page, since those anchors point at sections a\ndetail page does not have -- chosen by the host route rather than inferred.\n\nEight of the thirteen decisions this work produced are corrections to the\nplan rather than discoveries about the code (D88-D100): an omitted year\nfield, a skills section the field list never mentioned, a file split the\n200-line cap would not hold, a variant spec pointed at a component that\ntakes children, and a theme that claimed the design had one breakpoint when\nit has two. Most were found by running the gates the slices prescribed.\n\nDeliberate divergences from the export, each recorded: the menu control is\na button with aria-expanded, the accordion is a button with aria-controls,\nwhite-space:nowrap is dropped from the two clamped headings because it\noverflows by construction, and the hero region is typographic because no\nasset in the repo reaches 16/7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D88-D100 and what building slices 11-14 found wrong in the plan\n\nEight of the thirteen decisions are corrections to the plan rather than\ndiscoveries about the code -- the same ratio the 5-7 wave produced, and the\npattern the README warns about after it. Most were found by running the\ngates the slices themselves prescribed, not by reading the plan:\n\n- Slice 11 called itself additive while removing three fields; the\n  consumers'' typecheck is what disproved it (D92).\n- Its field table omitted year, which the design reads twice (D89), and\n  never mentioned skillGroups at all (D88).\n- Its file table could not hold the 200-line cap once the new fields went\n  in, so four modules split (D91).\n- Slice 12 pointed its variant spec at a component that takes children and\n  cannot pass a prop (D95).\n- The theme claimed the design had one breakpoint; it has two, and the\n  middle band has its own hero layout (D97).\n\nD100 records the anchor contract''s third leg as verified in the browser --\nall five nav anchors scrolling, four landing at exactly 84px -- which is the\ngate Slice 12 could not finish while the homepage remote was throwing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: group lib source into section folders\n\nEvery lib under libs/ except ui/primitives now keeps its source in folders\nnamed after sections, one level deep: a component plus the subcomponents,\nconsts and specs that exist only to build it. A file used by two or more\nsections gets its own folder (header''s anchor-href). index.ts and\ntest-setup.ts stay at the src root.\n\nui/primitives stays flat because shadcn writes its output to src/ and\nmoving a generated file breaks re-running `shadcn add` (D25).\n\nRelative imports are rewritten to match, and the plan docs and app\nREADMEs that cite lib file paths point at the new locations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: move E2E ahead of deployment and add Slice 17 for UI/navigation fixes\n\nD101: Slice 9 runs before Slice 8. E2E tests a local production build,\nnot a deployment, so every deploy is gated on it from the first one.\nBoth slices add their jobs to the existing ci.yml rather than creating\na second workflow.\n\nD102: the remaining UI and navigation issues become Slice 17, ahead of\nE2E so the suite doesn''t pin down the broken behaviour. Its issue list\nis Q22, still open. Its placement after 15 and 16 is proposed.\n\nAlso regroups Slice 15''s file list into section folders (~26 -> ~31\nfiles) and updates the README''s fixture glob for the nested layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: fill the footer strip, fix the hero break, add experience row hover, run sections full-bleed with capped copy, update hero specs strip, add AWS and smooth anchor scroll\n\n- Footer: build the design''s strip (copyright, circular marks, role line);\n  it was rendering ink-on-ink. Drop the contact block''s bottom padding so\n  the rule-to-strip gap is the export''s 1.5rem.\n- Hero: force the break after \"Building the\" (a \\n in headline.lead) so\n  \"front-end\" no longer splits at its hyphen at desktop width.\n- Experience: pointer cursor, plus a hover/focus state on the rows (accent\n  name and ring, half-strength surface tint).\n- Layout: drop the 1400px card and dark inset; section backgrounds run\n  full-bleed and copy is held to the 1400px column by a new px-page\n  utility, including the portfolio detail page. Body is paper.\n- Smooth scrolling for in-page anchors, off under reduced motion.\n- Content: AWS under Platform & Quality; React, Design System and Figma\n  in the Cosmikata stack; \"Atlanta\" in the specs strip; \"13+ years\n  shipping\" (D103, superseding D87''s strip figure).\n- Plan: Slice 16 marked strip-built; D103 recorded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: teach cn the theme font-size tokens so text-chip survives a text color\n\ntailwind-merge read unknown text-<name> classes as colors, so text-chip was\ndropped whenever a chip also set text-ink / text-paper and every MetaChip\nrendered at 16px instead of 0.58rem. Register the six --text-* sizes from\nlibs/ui/theme with extendTailwindMerge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: trim MetaChip''s label to cap height so its caps sit centred\n\nThe all-caps label left the font''s descent as dead space under the text\n(~6px above, ~9px below). The label span now uses text-box trim-both cap\nalphabetic, with padding at 0.47rem to keep the pill''s height; browsers\nwithout text-box keep py-1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: right-align the header nav at desktop width\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b0bc145e5c0fe850ebd56e990ad124668f4a09d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/8b0bc145e5c0fe850ebd56e990ad124668f4a09d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b0bc145e5c0fe850ebd56e990ad124668f4a09d\nparent d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790177169 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790177169 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/new skin (#45)\n\n* docs: record D76-D81 and the design source move for the 2026-09-22 redesign\n\nTwo new design exports replace the look of every surface in the plan. The six\ndecisions that had to be settled before any slice could be written:\n\n- D76 — the _design/ exports supersede the live v3 site as the design source,\n  site-wide. Content stays on 39bbe56 (D53). Retires the invented Header and\n  Footer of D59/D70.\n- D77 — the eight ported items survive; the design''s six-project list is read\n  as a card-grid layout spec. The ported slug wins in all four conflicts.\n- D78 — the HTML description and the videos are kept, as blocks the design\n  does not draw. This is what leaves D69 and its sanitizer with a subject.\n- D79 — the footer remote keeps the strip only; the dark blocks above it\n  belong to their pages. Four remotes survive; the cost is stated.\n- D80 — the redesign runs before deployment and E2E. Slices 8 and 9 keep\n  their numbers: renumbering would rewrite 97 references across 40 files,\n  most of them in source.\n- D81 — SITE_SECTIONS becomes the design''s five anchors and --spacing-header\n  splits into two tokens that are not derivable from each other.\n\ndesign-sources.md is mostly content moved out of README.md so the index can\nstay under its 200-line cap. Its new material is a finding and two defects:\n\n- _design/ is gitignored (.gitignore:9, added in 7b3bf60 when it was a scratch\n  directory), so every design link resolves on one machine and nowhere else.\n  Three options recorded; the plan does not resolve it unilaterally.\n- the exports contradict themselves on the years figure, and both hero images\n  are explicit placeholders. Raised as Q21 and Q18 rather than filled in.\n\nopen-questions.md goes from none open to four (Q18-Q21), each blocking one\nfield or region rather than a whole slice. The seventeen closed rows carry\nover intact; a sentence claiming twenty-one closed questions is corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add slices 10-16, the redesign''s seven build steps\n\nThe build instructions derived from D76-D81. They run after slices 5-7 and\nbefore 8-9 (D80).\n\n- 10 design foundation — solo. Nine palette tokens, three typefaces, the inset\n  rounded frame, five shared components justified by counted call sites.\n  --color-page and --color-ink both change value, so every existing component\n  shifts appearance without being edited.\n- 11 content model — solo. The new field set, and the per-file ownership table.\n  This slice exists because the 5-7 wave collided on shared-types and\n  shared-fixtures after the plan claimed they were disjoint; freezing the whole\n  content model before any agent starts is that correction applied.\n- 12 header — the only slice permitted to touch SITE_SECTIONS (D81). Records\n  that the two exports draw different bars, which makes the variant a new prop\n  crossing the federation boundary.\n- 13 homepage A — specs strip, hero, Work grid. Three breakpoints, not two.\n- 14 homepage B — Experience, Skills, About, Contact. The accordion opens index\n  0 on load, and gets real button semantics as a recorded divergence from the\n  export''s div-with-click-handler.\n- 15 portfolio detail — twelve regions, plus the two blocks D78 keeps that the\n  design does not draw. Both flagged invented, control by control.\n- 16 footer strip — its real content is the degradation D79 created: a downed\n  footer leaves the dark block ending on a bare rule.\n\nEach slice restates its binding decisions with a line of local meaning. Those\nare copies and they drift; decisions.md remains the source of truth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the design foundation and re-skin the shell onto it\n\nReplaces the v3 palette with the 2026-09-22 design exports'' token set (D76)\nand moves every surface the shell owns onto it. The exports are a\nspecification, not source: they are inline-styled <x-dc> templates, and\nnothing of that shape is copied -- every literal is re-expressed as a theme\ntoken.\n\nThe theme retires --color-page (there is no white in the new design) and\nsplits --spacing-header into --spacing-nav (56px) and --spacing-anchor (84px)\nper D81. Those are different numbers, and the single token that served both is\nwhy a section heading landed flush against the nav''s bottom rule. The old\ntoken stays defined, now inert.\n\nFive components join libs/ui/components because each has three or more call\nsites across the two exports -- D29''s threshold met by inspection, not\nanticipation. Eyebrow takes a surface rather than a colour so that mint on\npaper has no name: the design uses #3FD9A4 only inside ink sections, and a\nprop that cannot express the wrong pairing beats a comment saying not to.\nSectionHeading takes its two halves separately because the split point is\neditorial and a parser would guess it.\n\nThe shell''s content region loses its max-width and padding: the design''s\nsections run edge to edge and carry their own, because the alternating surface\nand ink backgrounds have to touch the card''s sides. The card''s overflow-hidden\nis what clips every dark section to the corner radius.\n\nlibs/ui/components gains a @portfolio/shared-utils dependency. Slice 10''s file\nlist said it needed none; all five components merge a className through cn,\nwhich lives there. It surfaced as an Nx project-reference sync failure rather\nthan a missing import (D83).\n\nThe Card primitive still names bg-page, now a dead token. ProfileCard\noverrides it through cn and is its only consumer, so it is harmless -- left in\nplace because D25 forbids hand-editing generated shadcn output.\n\nRefs D76, D81, D83, D84.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: load the webfonts from a link tag, not a CSS import\n\nCarlito, JetBrains Mono and Inter come from the Google Fonts CDN, which is\nwhat the design exports themselves reference (Q20 -> D82).\n\nThe first implementation put an @import url(...) at the top of\nlibs/ui/theme/src/theme.css, so that one declaration would cover the shell and\nthe four standalone remote dev surfaces. Vite''s CSS pipeline silently dropped\nit: the served stylesheet carried no @import and no @font-face, the page made\nzero requests to either font origin, and it rendered in system fallbacks --\nwith typecheck, lint, 161 specs and the file-size gate all green. A font that\nnever arrives is a page in a different face, not a broken one, so nothing in\nthe build could see it. It was caught by reading document.fonts and the\nresource timings in the running page.\n\nSo the request is a <link> in the shell''s document head, and in each remote''s\nindex.html for its standalone surface. That is also the faster shape: a CSS\n@import cannot begin its request until the importing sheet has been fetched\nand parsed, which serializes two round trips before any text can paint in the\nright face.\n\nThe four index.html files repeat the same three lines. There is no shared HTML\nlayer between the remotes, and introducing one to save twelve lines would\ncouple four independently deployed apps.\n\napps/shell/src/styles.css changes only in its comment, which had been left\nasserting that the theme carries the font @import -- pointing the next reader\nstraight at the mechanism that failed.\n\nSlice 8 inherits the CSP: style-src must allow fonts.googleapis.com and\nfont-src fonts.gstatic.com, or this regresses in production exactly as\nsilently.\n\nRefs D82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: clear the fixed header''s overlap and offset the anchor links\n\nThe nav bar is pinned flush to the top of the viewport (D84), which made two\nexisting measurements wrong.\n\nThe Header remote''s row carried h-header, D43''s single 4rem token. With the\nbar''s own padding that made the bar 97px while the spacer holding content down\nis 56px, so 41px of the page sat underneath it. Invisible only because the\nhomepage hero is currently a flat block; it would have clipped the hero''s\nspecs strip the moment Slice 13 landed. The row now sizes from its padding,\nwhich is 57px, and content clears the bar by 27px.\n\nBoth homepage sections carried scroll-mt-header, and a utility class beats the\ntheme''s [id] { scroll-margin-top } base rule -- so anchors resolved to 64px and\nnot the 84px the design states. A bar 56px tall wants more than 56px of scroll\nmargin or the heading lands flush against its bottom rule, which is why D81\nsplit the token in the first place. Clicking a nav link now lands the section\nat 84px.\n\nThe two remote loading placeholders reserved the old 64px; they reserve the\nreal bar''s height now, so hydration does not shift the page. The\nmfe-loading-placeholder spec passes the class as an arbitrary string and is\nretargeted so no file names a token that is about to go; its assertion is\nunchanged.\n\nThat leaves --spacing-header with zero readers. D81 assigned its removal to\nSlice 12 on the reasoning that the readers were spread across the three-way\nSITE_SECTIONS contract; they were not, they were four spacing call sites, and\nthese are all four. The token is left defined and inert rather than deleted:\nunder independent deployment a header remote built before this change still\nasks for h-header, and the class only generates while some source names it.\nDeleting it degrades an old remote to content height rather than a wrong one,\nwhich is Slice 8''s problem to weigh, not this commit''s.\n\nMobile still overlaps by 25px: at 375px the interim nav wraps to two lines and\nthe bar is 81px. Slice 12 closes it -- the design''s mobile nav is a 44px\nhamburger, not wrapped links.\n\nRefs D81, D84.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D82-D84 and what building Slice 10 found wrong in the plan\n\nThree of the four decisions here are corrections to the plan found by building\nagainst it rather than by reading it, which is the pattern the README already\nwarns about after the 5-7 wave.\n\nD82 closes Q20: the three typefaces come from the Google Fonts CDN, via a\n<link>. It is written up at length because the failure it records has no\nsignal -- an @import in the theme was silently dropped by Vite and the site\nrendered in system faces with every gate green. Q20''s own wording said \"a\n<link> in the shell''s document head\"; the implementation talked itself out of\nit for a real reason and lost an afternoon to it.\n\nD83 records that this slice''s file list was wrong about\nlibs/ui/components/package.json. It claimed nothing new was needed; all five\ncomponents merge a className through cn, which lives in a package\nui-components did not depend on.\n\nD84 records the nav bar being flush to the viewport top rather than floating\nat the frame inset as both exports draw it.\n\ndesign-sources.md gains the Design -> code delta table plan-design-links.md\nrequires and the plan did not have. Without it, a divergence reads as a defect\n-- and Slice 12 would have rebuilt the export''s floating bar from the design,\nsilently reverting D84. The table says so explicitly.\n\nSlice 10 gains a \"What this slice leaves open\" section: the 25px mobile header\noverlap, the five components carrying R3''s exposure until something mounts\nthem, and --spacing-header''s now-zero readers.\n\nThe README''s status table is corrected -- it still read \"Slices 3-7 built,\nawaiting review\" and named only PR #42 as merged, while #43 and #44 are both\nin this branch''s history.\n\nparallelization.md carries the slices 10-16 dependency graph, the second\nwave''s seam table and its per-slice file estimates. That work predates this\nsession and was sitting uncommitted; it is included here at the maintainer''s\ninstruction. One detail in it is already stale: its slice 10 row does not\nmention the shared-utils dependency, which D83 now records.\n\nRefs D76, D81, D82, D83, D84. Closes Q20.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: close Q18, Q19 and Q21 as D85-D87 before the redesign wave\n\nAll four questions raised on 2026-09-22 by reading the new design exports are\nnow closed, and three of them closed by measuring the repo against the export\nrather than by the agent sent to build against it. That ordering is the whole\npoint: the README''s warning after the 5-7 wave is that plan corrections keep\narriving from builders, and these three would each have arrived that way.\n\nD85 makes the detail and homepage heroes typographic. The question offered\n\"crop an existing screenshot\" as the cheap option and it was not available:\nthe widest asset in the repo is 1.80 -- a 540x300 card thumbnail -- against\n16/7''s 2.29, and four of the eight items are mobile-screenshot-only with no\ncroppable candidate at all. The region and its ratio survive; only the fill\nchanges, so hero and heroCaption come off PortfolioItem entirely.\n\nD86 derives the gallery''s span and ratio from the authored dimensions and\nbuckets them to the design''s two. Three of Q19''s own premises were wrong: it\nis 35 gallery images and not 43 (the other eight are thumbnail), its warning\nthat derivation breaks the design''s rhythm is backwards (the design is 12\nportrait tiles to 8 landscape, the catalogue 26 to 9), and the authored\nwidth/height are display dimensions rather than intrinsic -- but they preserve\nthe ratio exactly, which is all derivation needs.\n\nD87 replaces both of the design''s years figures. 2011 to 2026 is 15 years, not\nthe 14 the question computed; 10+ anchors on no row in the experience list;\n13+ anchors cleanly on the 2013 Cricket Manager title. So the strip reads 15+\nyears shipping and the About stat reads 13+ years in lead & architect roles,\nboth derivable from the table printed directly beneath them.\n\nTwo of these change what a slice builds, not just what it knows -- D85 removes\ntwo fields from Slice 11''s deliverable and D86 turns Slice 15''s gallery from\nauthored data into derived presentation -- so the binding blocks of slices 11,\n13, 14 and 15 are rewritten, and Slice 11''s field table and Slice 15''s Hero and\nGallery sections with them.\n\nQ18/Q19/Q21 go to a third closed-questions file: appending them to the second\nwould have taken it to ~558 lines, over the 500-line cap. Q20 stays where it\nclosed so its existing links keep resolving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the shared UiIcon and the design''s second breakpoint\n\nUiIcon is the sixth shared component (D93), added by the coordinator ahead\nof the redesign wave rather than reported-and-waited: four slices need it —\n12 for the mobile overlay and the detail bar, 13 for the hero CTA and every\nWork card, 14 for the Experience accordion, 15 for the link pills.\n\nIt extends D75 rather than reopening it — Tabler, not a second icon\nlibrary — and keeps SocialIcon''s decorative contract, so the accessible name\nstays on the element around it.\n\n--breakpoint-wide corrects Slice 10, whose comment read \"the frame''s inset\nand its one breakpoint\". The homepage export distinguishes three bands and\ngives the middle one its own hero lede layout, so collapsing to two is a\nvisible regression at tablet width that fails by looking fine (D97).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rebuild the content model, the header and the homepage on the new design\n\nSlices 11-14 of the MFE plan, committed as one change because nothing\nsmaller compiles (D92): Slice 11 removes projectGroups, cardId and\nhero.links, Slice 12 re-points SITE_SECTIONS, and Slices 13-14 are what\nmakes the homepage read the new shape.\n\nThe content model gains the design''s per-item fields and the homepage''s\nfour lower panels. SITE_SECTIONS becomes the design''s five anchors, with\nSECTION_IDS so no file outside the fixture writes one of those strings\n(D96). The header renders two variants -- five anchors on the homepage,\nbrand + back-link on a detail page, since those anchors point at sections a\ndetail page does not have -- chosen by the host route rather than inferred.\n\nEight of the thirteen decisions this work produced are corrections to the\nplan rather than discoveries about the code (D88-D100): an omitted year\nfield, a skills section the field list never mentioned, a file split the\n200-line cap would not hold, a variant spec pointed at a component that\ntakes children, and a theme that claimed the design had one breakpoint when\nit has two. Most were found by running the gates the slices prescribed.\n\nDeliberate divergences from the export, each recorded: the menu control is\na button with aria-expanded, the accordion is a button with aria-controls,\nwhite-space:nowrap is dropped from the two clamped headings because it\noverflows by construction, and the hero region is typographic because no\nasset in the repo reaches 16/7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D88-D100 and what building slices 11-14 found wrong in the plan\n\nEight of the thirteen decisions are corrections to the plan rather than\ndiscoveries about the code -- the same ratio the 5-7 wave produced, and the\npattern the README warns about after it. Most were found by running the\ngates the slices themselves prescribed, not by reading the plan:\n\n- Slice 11 called itself additive while removing three fields; the\n  consumers'' typecheck is what disproved it (D92).\n- Its field table omitted year, which the design reads twice (D89), and\n  never mentioned skillGroups at all (D88).\n- Its file table could not hold the 200-line cap once the new fields went\n  in, so four modules split (D91).\n- Slice 12 pointed its variant spec at a component that takes children and\n  cannot pass a prop (D95).\n- The theme claimed the design had one breakpoint; it has two, and the\n  middle band has its own hero layout (D97).\n\nD100 records the anchor contract''s third leg as verified in the browser --\nall five nav anchors scrolling, four landing at exactly 84px -- which is the\ngate Slice 12 could not finish while the homepage remote was throwing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: group lib source into section folders\n\nEvery lib under libs/ except ui/primitives now keeps its source in folders\nnamed after sections, one level deep: a component plus the subcomponents,\nconsts and specs that exist only to build it. A file used by two or more\nsections gets its own folder (header''s anchor-href). index.ts and\ntest-setup.ts stay at the src root.\n\nui/primitives stays flat because shadcn writes its output to src/ and\nmoving a generated file breaks re-running `shadcn add` (D25).\n\nRelative imports are rewritten to match, and the plan docs and app\nREADMEs that cite lib file paths point at the new locations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: move E2E ahead of deployment and add Slice 17 for UI/navigation fixes\n\nD101: Slice 9 runs before Slice 8. E2E tests a local production build,\nnot a deployment, so every deploy is gated on it from the first one.\nBoth slices add their jobs to the existing ci.yml rather than creating\na second workflow.\n\nD102: the remaining UI and navigation issues become Slice 17, ahead of\nE2E so the suite doesn''t pin down the broken behaviour. Its issue list\nis Q22, still open. Its placement after 15 and 16 is proposed.\n\nAlso regroups Slice 15''s file list into section folders (~26 -> ~31\nfiles) and updates the README''s fixture glob for the nested layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: fill the footer strip, fix the hero break, add experience row hover, run sections full-bleed with capped copy, update hero specs strip, add AWS and smooth anchor scroll\n\n- Footer: build the design''s strip (copyright, circular marks, role line);\n  it was rendering ink-on-ink. Drop the contact block''s bottom padding so\n  the rule-to-strip gap is the export''s 1.5rem.\n- Hero: force the break after \"Building the\" (a \\n in headline.lead) so\n  \"front-end\" no longer splits at its hyphen at desktop width.\n- Experience: pointer cursor, plus a hover/focus state on the rows (accent\n  name and ring, half-strength surface tint).\n- Layout: drop the 1400px card and dark inset; section backgrounds run\n  full-bleed and copy is held to the 1400px column by a new px-page\n  utility, including the portfolio detail page. Body is paper.\n- Smooth scrolling for in-page anchors, off under reduced motion.\n- Content: AWS under Platform & Quality; React, Design System and Figma\n  in the Cosmikata stack; \"Atlanta\" in the specs strip; \"13+ years\n  shipping\" (D103, superseding D87''s strip figure).\n- Plan: Slice 16 marked strip-built; D103 recorded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: teach cn the theme font-size tokens so text-chip survives a text color\n\ntailwind-merge read unknown text-<name> classes as colors, so text-chip was\ndropped whenever a chip also set text-ink / text-paper and every MetaChip\nrendered at 16px instead of 0.58rem. Register the six --text-* sizes from\nlibs/ui/theme with extendTailwindMerge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: trim MetaChip''s label to cap height so its caps sit centred\n\nThe all-caps label left the font''s descent as dead space under the text\n(~6px above, ~9px below). The label span now uses text-box trim-both cap\nalphabetic, with padding at 0.47rem to keep the pill''s height; browsers\nwithout text-box keep py-1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: right-align the header nav at desktop width\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs++RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAemIQADOiEKZJPfRSqXbqQSEqVuDK\nOBiWgCsHuMhyKlx2NId8qMaDcCWqDVvLC3+xzEk5vMLgwrXTrd9I+fFhM8OeaQb7\nYFErIXB7RquyCDivZOf7vNkKw5yEthLBLOHwIknwHOfZDpHqrcAu2Bz7+9PtzVyK\nLO+7jqM3aC4mmdRP4dcI3+a3Br4t4T7UCIzrBJGvpdrvLHMKdAurcl2ORiKTiX5J\nnashxZVvjqPlrNJ9UDjlNxx3DawoYmbdPnC/ygr9/FHs9LEu4/YAcBbTP6+GAJmT\nweEint8M8+Bp0qCue7vaCrh12DQNx+vhBFAD1vCN+JAgCAlXeh5U3j7gju0YWlDV\ngnLXxxDwIiwSCRg9BBXuWclDWbBtO9h+Gg/7E/eEm0G5Kpe7Z4FPcWw6VIACagen\njssQIwPacgPthP0gaJBOGS4ocyBrXqWsqte1jlLgHD6XS3R+yWgOwK5YtqeVkyVi\nw7b8b3lyNBoMTC7WkPF1oof52QPA/cqfN1No71uam6TxEn13Yos4eaYpYgCmPRnx\nUzw3PCJ0GAMuSwvhNCOuYoANdcC+gAPsUb4ogOpwblbfmxc6754TcHFjYhF/SO7g\n9CGzg0k0559gWovUPyMs4/l+hAkkQT0hVZTFQvBleW2KevbJan5BYjXfoDYGDy2p\n4IL0XFs4mL9zQRxjqFya\n=eXa7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T15:26:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2","node_id":"C_kwDOCok6WdoAKGFiNWMxMzkxYjUyN2U4ZTRmOWJkOTJiMGUzZjg4MjkzMjM5MjYwYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede","sha":"d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede"}],"sha":"ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/ab5c1391b527e8e4f9bd92b0e3f88293239260c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:02:57Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:02:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/build out 2 (#44)\n\n* feat: add the Tabler brand-mark component and the two new dependencies\n\nAdds the one SocialIcon that both the footer and the homepage hero will\nrender, plus the two dependencies this work needs.\n\nThe SocialIconName union lives in @portfolio/shared-types rather than\nbeside the component: the homepage''s links are fixture data, and\ntype:shared may not import from libs/ui/*, while type:ui-components may\nimport type:shared. A second copy in the UI package would have the\nfixture and the component agreeing by luck instead of by the compiler.\n\ndompurify and @tabler/icons-react share one lockfile entry, so both\npackage.json changes ride with it rather than splitting the lock from\nits manifests.\n\nRefs D75.\n\n* feat: build the footer remote against the v3 social links\n\nReplaces Slice 4''s placeholder with the real footer: a copyright line and\nthe two outbound links, now drawn as Tabler marks.\n\nv3 has no footer. Verified against 39bbe56 -- the string \"footer\" does\nnot appear anywhere under src/, and there is no <footer> element. Only\nthe two URLs are ported, from v3''s hero section; the footer itself, the\ncopyright line and the layout are invented and flagged as such.\n\nThe root element stays a <div> because ShellFooterRegion already supplies\nthe <footer> landmark.\n\nOne spec changed meaning rather than code: the link-forwarding assertion\ncompared textContent to each label, which the icon swap silently reduced\nto '''' === ''''. It now asserts the accessible name, which the label moved\nto when the mark replaced the text.\n\nRefs D70, D75.\n\n* feat: port the eight portfolio items and render them behind a sanitizer\n\nExpands PortfolioItem to the full v3 shape, ports the item data from\n39bbe56, and builds the item page that renders it.\n\nEight items, not the nine D53 and the slice file both name:\ncosmikata-design-system is commented out in active.data.ts -- the whole\nobject, not just its id -- so it has no data to port and is not\nuncommented. Its route correctly answers not-found.\n\nThe description stays an HTML string and is sanitized on render (D69).\nThe allow-list is p/ul/li/a with href/target/rel, derived from the eight\nreal bodies rather than from DOMPurify''s defaults, and rel=\"noopener\nnoreferrer\" is forced by a hook rather than trusted to the copy.\n\nTwo specs changed their claim rather than their code: route-metadata''s\nand use-content-stub''s assertions that Slice 7 had not landed yet.\n\nThe unavailable state is invented -- v3 has no equivalent -- with no\nretry and no link, deliberately.\n\nAlso corrects five stale \"nine items\" comments in this lib.\n\nRefs D69, D71.\n\n* feat: build the homepage remote from the ported v3 content\n\nExpands HomepageContent to the real shape, ports the hero copy and the\nthree skill lists from 39bbe56, and builds the homepage from them: hero,\nskills, and the two project listings.\n\nTwo specs reversed their claim rather than their code. While Slices 6 and\n7 ran concurrently, portfolio-items.fixture.ts was Slice 7''s empty array,\nso both listings correctly rendered the empty state and the tile drew no\nimage -- and two specs pinned exactly that. Slice 7 then landed the eight\nitems and the thumbnail field, so both went red, which is what a spec\nencoding a temporary state should do when the state ends.\n\nportfolio-item.test-helpers.ts exists for the same reason: these specs\nwrote { slug, title } literals because that was the whole of PortfolioItem\nwhen the wave started. Both agents were green in their own worktrees; only\nthe integration gate saw it.\n\nHomepage membership is projectGroups[].slugs, so an item in neither group\ndoes not appear on the homepage at all -- correct for the eight, and a\nsilent trap for a ninth added later.\n\nRefs D72.\n\n* fix: pass the resolved item to the portfolio remote, and port the images\n\nMfeRemoteMount rendered <RemoteComponent /> with no props. That was\ncorrect for the header, footer and homepage, which take none, and\nsilently wrong for the portfolio item, which needs the resolved item.\n/portfolio/<any-slug> drew the remote''s standalone preview item while the\nserver-rendered <head> correctly described the slug asked for -- a wrong\npage that looks right, and nothing errored.\n\nNothing caught it. The remote''s own specs supply the item themselves, so\nthey play the part of the parent and always remember; the mount''s specs\nnever asserted forwarding because until now no remote took a prop; and\ntypecheck cannot see across the federation boundary. The new specs render\nthrough the mount and go red when the forwarding is removed.\n\nAlso ports the 43 images the eight items reference, from 39bbe56 into\napps/shell/public, paths unchanged so no fixture string needed editing.\nNo slice could have done this: the port was assigned to Slice 6 while\napps/shell was closed to every wave agent.\n\nRefs D73, D74.\n\n* docs: record D69-D75 and correct what the wave found wrong in this plan\n\nCloses Q17, the plan''s last open question, and records the six decisions\nthe Slice 5-7 wave forced.\n\nThree of them are corrections to this plan rather than discoveries about\nthe code, and each was found by the agent sent to build against it:\n\n  D70 - v3 has no footer. The design table said it existed. That is the\n        second row to claim exists for something nobody had checked; the\n        header was the first, the same day.\n  D71 - eight portfolio items, not nine. The slug list had been read off\n        v3''s route directory, and each copy was checked against the\n        previous copy rather than against the data.\n  D74 - the image port was assigned to Slice 6 and simultaneously\n        forbidden to it by the ownership table.\n\nD53 also loses a stale instruction: git show version-3:<path> no longer\nresolves, because that branch was reused for this workspace.\n\nparallelization.md gains the apps/shell exception for Slice 7, which\ncontradicted the slice file. Resolved by reading the route rather than by\npicking a document.\n\nLeft unfixed on purpose: Slice 6''s file list still claims the image port\nwhile the ownership table still forbids it. Which side should change is a\nmaintainer decision, so D74 records the contradiction instead.\n\n* fix: force vite dep pre-bundling in remote dev servers\n\n@module-federation/vite only registers react-dom as a used share from the\nesbuild dep-optimizer pass. On a warm node_modules/.vite cache Vite skips\nthat scan, hostAutoInit never publishes react-dom into the share scope, and\nreact-dom/client crashes on ReactDOMSharedInternals.d — so every standalone\nremote worked on the run that re-optimized and broke on every restart after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50d9e772714a264a2752f5db77dcb59d6d9e0385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/50d9e772714a264a2752f5db77dcb59d6d9e0385"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede","verification":{"payload":"tree 50d9e772714a264a2752f5db77dcb59d6d9e0385\nparent bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790056977 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790056977 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/build out 2 (#44)\n\n* feat: add the Tabler brand-mark component and the two new dependencies\n\nAdds the one SocialIcon that both the footer and the homepage hero will\nrender, plus the two dependencies this work needs.\n\nThe SocialIconName union lives in @portfolio/shared-types rather than\nbeside the component: the homepage''s links are fixture data, and\ntype:shared may not import from libs/ui/*, while type:ui-components may\nimport type:shared. A second copy in the UI package would have the\nfixture and the component agreeing by luck instead of by the compiler.\n\ndompurify and @tabler/icons-react share one lockfile entry, so both\npackage.json changes ride with it rather than splitting the lock from\nits manifests.\n\nRefs D75.\n\n* feat: build the footer remote against the v3 social links\n\nReplaces Slice 4''s placeholder with the real footer: a copyright line and\nthe two outbound links, now drawn as Tabler marks.\n\nv3 has no footer. Verified against 39bbe56 -- the string \"footer\" does\nnot appear anywhere under src/, and there is no <footer> element. Only\nthe two URLs are ported, from v3''s hero section; the footer itself, the\ncopyright line and the layout are invented and flagged as such.\n\nThe root element stays a <div> because ShellFooterRegion already supplies\nthe <footer> landmark.\n\nOne spec changed meaning rather than code: the link-forwarding assertion\ncompared textContent to each label, which the icon swap silently reduced\nto '''' === ''''. It now asserts the accessible name, which the label moved\nto when the mark replaced the text.\n\nRefs D70, D75.\n\n* feat: port the eight portfolio items and render them behind a sanitizer\n\nExpands PortfolioItem to the full v3 shape, ports the item data from\n39bbe56, and builds the item page that renders it.\n\nEight items, not the nine D53 and the slice file both name:\ncosmikata-design-system is commented out in active.data.ts -- the whole\nobject, not just its id -- so it has no data to port and is not\nuncommented. Its route correctly answers not-found.\n\nThe description stays an HTML string and is sanitized on render (D69).\nThe allow-list is p/ul/li/a with href/target/rel, derived from the eight\nreal bodies rather than from DOMPurify''s defaults, and rel=\"noopener\nnoreferrer\" is forced by a hook rather than trusted to the copy.\n\nTwo specs changed their claim rather than their code: route-metadata''s\nand use-content-stub''s assertions that Slice 7 had not landed yet.\n\nThe unavailable state is invented -- v3 has no equivalent -- with no\nretry and no link, deliberately.\n\nAlso corrects five stale \"nine items\" comments in this lib.\n\nRefs D69, D71.\n\n* feat: build the homepage remote from the ported v3 content\n\nExpands HomepageContent to the real shape, ports the hero copy and the\nthree skill lists from 39bbe56, and builds the homepage from them: hero,\nskills, and the two project listings.\n\nTwo specs reversed their claim rather than their code. While Slices 6 and\n7 ran concurrently, portfolio-items.fixture.ts was Slice 7''s empty array,\nso both listings correctly rendered the empty state and the tile drew no\nimage -- and two specs pinned exactly that. Slice 7 then landed the eight\nitems and the thumbnail field, so both went red, which is what a spec\nencoding a temporary state should do when the state ends.\n\nportfolio-item.test-helpers.ts exists for the same reason: these specs\nwrote { slug, title } literals because that was the whole of PortfolioItem\nwhen the wave started. Both agents were green in their own worktrees; only\nthe integration gate saw it.\n\nHomepage membership is projectGroups[].slugs, so an item in neither group\ndoes not appear on the homepage at all -- correct for the eight, and a\nsilent trap for a ninth added later.\n\nRefs D72.\n\n* fix: pass the resolved item to the portfolio remote, and port the images\n\nMfeRemoteMount rendered <RemoteComponent /> with no props. That was\ncorrect for the header, footer and homepage, which take none, and\nsilently wrong for the portfolio item, which needs the resolved item.\n/portfolio/<any-slug> drew the remote''s standalone preview item while the\nserver-rendered <head> correctly described the slug asked for -- a wrong\npage that looks right, and nothing errored.\n\nNothing caught it. The remote''s own specs supply the item themselves, so\nthey play the part of the parent and always remember; the mount''s specs\nnever asserted forwarding because until now no remote took a prop; and\ntypecheck cannot see across the federation boundary. The new specs render\nthrough the mount and go red when the forwarding is removed.\n\nAlso ports the 43 images the eight items reference, from 39bbe56 into\napps/shell/public, paths unchanged so no fixture string needed editing.\nNo slice could have done this: the port was assigned to Slice 6 while\napps/shell was closed to every wave agent.\n\nRefs D73, D74.\n\n* docs: record D69-D75 and correct what the wave found wrong in this plan\n\nCloses Q17, the plan''s last open question, and records the six decisions\nthe Slice 5-7 wave forced.\n\nThree of them are corrections to this plan rather than discoveries about\nthe code, and each was found by the agent sent to build against it:\n\n  D70 - v3 has no footer. The design table said it existed. That is the\n        second row to claim exists for something nobody had checked; the\n        header was the first, the same day.\n  D71 - eight portfolio items, not nine. The slug list had been read off\n        v3''s route directory, and each copy was checked against the\n        previous copy rather than against the data.\n  D74 - the image port was assigned to Slice 6 and simultaneously\n        forbidden to it by the ownership table.\n\nD53 also loses a stale instruction: git show version-3:<path> no longer\nresolves, because that branch was reused for this workspace.\n\nparallelization.md gains the apps/shell exception for Slice 7, which\ncontradicted the slice file. Resolved by reading the route rather than by\npicking a document.\n\nLeft unfixed on purpose: Slice 6''s file list still claims the image port\nwhile the ownership table still forbids it. Which side should change is a\nmaintainer decision, so D74 records the contradiction instead.\n\n* fix: force vite dep pre-bundling in remote dev servers\n\n@module-federation/vite only registers react-dom as a used share from the\nesbuild dep-optimizer pass. On a warm node_modules/.vite cache Vite skips\nthat scan, hostAutoInit never publishes react-dom into the share scope, and\nreact-dom/client crashes on ReactDOMSharedInternals.d — so every standalone\nremote worked on the run that re-optimized and broke on every restart after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqshoRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATIAQAGzst3BFaa3K7OwQ2hC+kRh1\njOWehpNzop9b+ymzOkARhftRacmdUVeDS3hQtD5UofOv60zcS/aB7gLP314DmeFd\nUIMD9L5hG5GQ4XjMLcQsMzwi3EbgMSh3iW9EwrE96FbasyDQ1bn1hJxjVEgoPhHd\ni9ypEtg2kIOPPK3UvjYhzrddXJDd3rHkLmRwZ+pJh9THXodaWFVCkX8te7zdxWi7\nMEqhmEgnFgj9zVil1G1TCmfshrlO5AC/maLW5YSJPot82mcqkjHhPkyyLFN0O5b+\n9WVyOXtRMr6xGgQ9QNAcLySHGb9QgvaX/camQaISmXbAM1o8nKMk6h9D/NzQneoV\ny9tWbnUE+0ksnpaK0QGrPy6wI4HVfNmT5FLezHpZEMcpFSPyuHgTFPRYjx3Z89T1\nHRi/j2y2cGgTcwXlL5IkT6hUV+NRrKS7Gr7gdwAkPrHhGk9KJcV/MUTKj6jp8JMq\nMjPw2MjJ3yEvFAAgmun5d1xiKOvrfwl/rp0u5vBP1z764aAu9mMSmtz+vEXZs+0E\nr8H/jFQRN2SJGooc1OUFXIIZLDWxnWpKTsJgjWWKUvaIlhqVl0qxNig+Jxy7wU0L\nmL0OCWQkVaKyL8Ww0wzUfJZ+MYIMQsY9Z994UeW/EuWw6TzGP+5ujKyByihYpJTf\nc/vTNoMIwzUxvKaZZFpg\n=FNkK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T06:02:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede","node_id":"C_kwDOCok6WdoAKGQ0Mzg3YzM1MDFiOTI3YmVmNmQwMmJiM2UyZGE2NDgwZTAyYzJlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7","sha":"bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7"}],"sha":"d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/d4387c3501b927bef6d02bb3e2da6480e02c2ede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:37:46Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:37:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/build out (#43)\n\n* feat: add the Header remote as an independently built MFE\n\nCreates `apps/header` (skeleton, per D27) and `libs/features/header` (the\ncomponent), the first of the four remotes. The remote builds, tests and runs\nstandalone; the shell does not consume it yet.\n\nThe federation config is D55''s proven shape: `shared` is react + react-dom\nonly, and Vite `base` is the remote''s own origin so component-owned assets\nresolve from :4174 rather than the page''s origin (D42).\n\nTwo shared dependencies Slice 3 specified are absent, per D60: `ui-theme` is\nCSS-only and has no JS module to share, and `ui-components` is unbuilt TS that\nVite cannot resolve from `optimizeDeps`. Both share at build time instead.\n\nThe Header has no v3 reference — the live site has no header at all — so its\nbar, nav label set and section ids are invented and flagged in D59. The ids\nare a contract Slice 6 must match.\n\nAlso adds D43''s `--spacing-header` token and the `@source` line for the new\nlib, without which the Header renders unstyled with every gate green (R3).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: mount the Header remote in the shell\n\nWires `apps/shell` to the remote committed in 0d4cedf: the federation host\nconfig, a `ClientOnly` mount point, and the remote registry''s first real entry.\n\nTwo lines in the host config are load-bearing and easy to lose. The\n`applyToEnvironment` override (D55) is the only thing keeping federation out of\nthe Lambda bundle, because every plugin `federation()` returns hard-codes it to\ntrue. `hostInitInjectLocation: ''entry''` is new beyond D55 (D58): the default\nwraps `src/router.tsx` into a bootstrap that re-exports nothing, and the client\nthen never hydrates — silently, with a 200 and the shell''s own content intact.\n\n`ClientOnly` rather than bare `lazy` is what compiles the remote import out of\nthe server chunk instead of merely deferring it (D55).\n\nExtracts `readEnv` from site.ts now the registry is a second consumer (D29).\nThe registry spec''s claim changes: the header now resolves, and its origin is\nasserted not to be the shell''s — D42''s failure mode, which a same-origin\ndefault would hide on localhost and 404 behind CloudFront.\n\nThe remote''s URL is still resolved at build time, so D12 is not yet satisfied;\nD61 records that and the duplicated default origin it forces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D58-D62 and correct the plan''s Header assertions\n\nBuilding Slice 3 forced five decisions, three of which correct something the\nplan already asserted. Recorded as numbered decisions rather than quiet edits\nso the corrections cannot be lost in a later revision.\n\nD58 and D61 are addenda to D55: the spike verified the built output, and both\nof these live outside what a build inspection can see.\n\nThe README''s design table claimed the Header existed on the v3 site. It does\nnot — no header, no nav component, and no element in the v3 tree carries an\nid. D59 records what was verified, what was ported, and what is invented.\n\nAlso corrects statements that would otherwise contradict the new log: slice\n03''s D19 bullet (\"never baked into the shell''s bundle\") and its Q13 bullet\nlisting ui-* as shared, and parallelization''s 2-to-3 edge, which rested on the\nsame wrong premise. The 3-to-4 edge is now marked as more than sequencing.\n\nPicks up a D57 index bullet that was already missing, unrelated to this work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: share the site-section contract and seed the content seam\n\nMoves the homepage section list out of @portfolio/feature-header into\n@portfolio/shared-fixtures as SITE_SECTIONS, with its shape as SiteSection\nin @portfolio/shared-types (D63). The ids are a contract between three\nindependently deployed units — the Header remote links to them, the Homepage\nremote puts them on section elements, and the shell''s header fallback links to\nthem when the Header is down. The shell cannot import the Header remote (D16,\nand the Nx boundary rule), so a hardcoded copy would have been a second source\nof truth nothing could compare against.\n\nAlso seeds the Slice 5-7 wave''s co-owned packages: HomepageContent and\nPortfolioItem as minimal container types, their fixture modules, and\nuse-content-stub.ts with all three read signatures stubbed. Each module carries\nan OWNER banner so a wave agent that opens the wrong file is told so by the\nfile (D67). Neither content type declares a `description` field — Q17 is open\nand the field''s shape is its slice''s to settle.\n\nFills the remote registry''s footer, homepage and portfolio-item rows on\n4175/4176/4177, and adds a `version` to RemoteEntry (D64) so every diagnostic\npayload can name the deployment it was pointing at.\n\nThe registry spec''s claim reverses here: it asserted those three remotes were\nundefined and now asserts they exist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: isolate each remote behind a shell-owned boundary and fallback\n\nImplements docs/architecture/mfe-failure-and-fallback-behavior.md at the D27\npath: one error boundary per remote, owned by the shell, with a fallback that\nis never federated (D16). A runtime exception or a failed remoteEntry.js now\ndegrades one region instead of taking the route down, which closes D62.\n\nLoading, render and hang failures arrive by different paths and end at the same\nfallback. A rejected import never settles into a React error boundary on its\nown, so the loader routes it there; an import that neither resolves nor rejects\nis caught by a timeout living in the Suspense fallback itself, where mounting\nstarts the clock and resolving unmounts it (R7).\n\nThe retry counter lives in the mount rather than the boundary (D65). React.lazy\ncaches the rejected promise, so clearing the boundary''s error in place re-serves\nthe same rejection — a retry button that looks like it works and does not. The\nmount rebuilds the lazy component per attempt and remounts the boundary by key,\nwhich is also how the boundary resets on success. The bound is visible in the\nUI, not only enforced: at zero attempts the button is replaced by an\nexplanation.\n\nAdds the shell''s location.hash re-apply (D43). A cold deep link looks for a\nsection before the Homepage remote has mounted, finds nothing, and never looks\nagain — silently. Readiness is expressed structurally, by a component that sits\ninside the remote''s own Suspense boundary.\n\nAn unknown portfolio slug is a shell-level not-found, deliberately not a\nfallback (D66): it offers no retry, because a missing item will never appear.\n\nEvery fallback''s visual treatment is invented — the v3 site has no\nremote-failure UI — and each is flagged in the slice''s completion report.\nEvery spec here was seen failing with its behaviour reverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: mount all four remotes in the shell and add /portfolio/$slug\n\nWires every remote through MfeRemoteMount, so each one carries its own error\nboundary, loading state, hang timeout and bounded retry. The Header''s mount\nloses the \"no error boundary yet\" caveat it shipped with in Slice 3; ClientOnly\nstays, since it is what keeps the import out of the SSR path (D55).\n\nThree of the four remotes do not exist yet when this lands. That is the point:\nthis file set is the seam slices 5, 6 and 7 would otherwise all edit while\nrunning concurrently, so it is built once and closed to them. A federation\nentry pointing at a dead origin is not a build error — the runtime fetches\nremoteEntry.js lazily, in the browser — so the failure lands where the boundary\nis already waiting, and the fallback path is observable from the day the seam is\ncreated rather than the day the remote lands.\n\nAdds the /portfolio/$slug route. The item is resolved in the route, before the\nremote is asked for, which is what keeps an unknown slug (a shell-level\nnot-found) apart from a downed remote (its fallback). They look similar and mean\nopposite things. The route also carries the per-slug head values, which is the\ncase D48 was taken for.\n\nOnly the Homepage mount sets isHashTarget: it is the region holding the sections\nan anchor can point at, and re-applying the hash in all three would fire three\nscrolls.\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is generated output, regenerated by the TanStack Start plugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: scaffold the footer, homepage and portfolio-item remotes as runnable apps\n\nCreates all six of the Slice 5-7 wave''s projects at once, tagged per D44, with\na single pnpm install. Adding an Nx project mutates the root tsconfig\nreferences and races pnpm-lock.yaml, so the manifest work is pulled out of the\nparallel slices and done here; each agent then writes code into a project that\nalready exists and registers nothing.\n\nEach remote is runnable, not merely present (D68). Two earlier attempts at a\nthinner scaffold failed: targets with no vite config started Vite on its\ndefaults, bound a random free port instead of the registry''s, printed a URL and\nexited 0 — a target that looked like it worked and served nothing, with every\ngate green. Removing the targets made the failure honest but left three\ndirectories that could not be started at all. So each app carries the full\nskeleton copied from apps/header (D55), and `nx dev <remote>` now serves it on\nits own strictPort port and publishes remoteEntry.js.\n\nEach feature lib carries a placeholder component at the real name, so its slice\nreplaces a body rather than building a skeleton. Every placeholder''s spec\nasserts the string \"Slice N fills this\", which fails the moment the real\ncomponent lands — the placeholder cannot survive its own slice, and it cannot be\nquietly left in either.\n\nThe line held is wiring, not content: no placeholder makes a decision its slice\nowns. The Homepage placeholder renders the SITE_SECTIONS ids and\nscroll-mt-header only because those are an existing contract (D43, D63), and it\nrenders no section content. It is also what let D43''s cold deep link be verified\nlive for the first time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D63-D68 and what Slice 4 actually built\n\nSix decisions came out of building the slice. Three are things the architecture\ndoc implies but does not say and the implementation could not stay silent about:\nthe fallback render prop and where the retry counter has to live (D65), the\nnot-found that is deliberately not a fallback (D66), and the section list that\nneeded a third reader the shell cannot import (D63). The rest are RemoteEntry''s\nversion field (D64), the wave''s per-file split (D67), and the expansion that\nmade all four remotes runnable (D68).\n\nThe filename says D63-D67 and the file holds six. D68 arrived after the file was\nnamed, and decisions are never renumbered, so the name stays and the index\ncarries the real range.\n\nparallelization.md gains the named per-file split the wave cannot start without:\nwhich module of the co-owned libs/shared/types and libs/shared/fixtures each\nagent may open, and the list of paths closed to all three. It also corrects\nSlice 4''s file estimate, which was 2.25x low for three reasons worth carrying\ninto slices 5-7, and supersedes its own claim that the apps have no tsconfig.\n\nSlice 4''s own file records both correction rounds and separates what was seen\non screen from what was only verified in a spec. The header fallback and the\nsuccessful-retry path were never seen in a browser, and the doc says so.\n\nSlices 5-7 shrank: each is now replace one component and its spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c27ab924e6ada4257cfc2a0f9d97c3087b439e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/c27ab924e6ada4257cfc2a0f9d97c3087b439e1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7","verification":{"payload":"tree c27ab924e6ada4257cfc2a0f9d97c3087b439e1f\nparent 7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790051866 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790051866 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/build out (#43)\n\n* feat: add the Header remote as an independently built MFE\n\nCreates `apps/header` (skeleton, per D27) and `libs/features/header` (the\ncomponent), the first of the four remotes. The remote builds, tests and runs\nstandalone; the shell does not consume it yet.\n\nThe federation config is D55''s proven shape: `shared` is react + react-dom\nonly, and Vite `base` is the remote''s own origin so component-owned assets\nresolve from :4174 rather than the page''s origin (D42).\n\nTwo shared dependencies Slice 3 specified are absent, per D60: `ui-theme` is\nCSS-only and has no JS module to share, and `ui-components` is unbuilt TS that\nVite cannot resolve from `optimizeDeps`. Both share at build time instead.\n\nThe Header has no v3 reference — the live site has no header at all — so its\nbar, nav label set and section ids are invented and flagged in D59. The ids\nare a contract Slice 6 must match.\n\nAlso adds D43''s `--spacing-header` token and the `@source` line for the new\nlib, without which the Header renders unstyled with every gate green (R3).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: mount the Header remote in the shell\n\nWires `apps/shell` to the remote committed in 0d4cedf: the federation host\nconfig, a `ClientOnly` mount point, and the remote registry''s first real entry.\n\nTwo lines in the host config are load-bearing and easy to lose. The\n`applyToEnvironment` override (D55) is the only thing keeping federation out of\nthe Lambda bundle, because every plugin `federation()` returns hard-codes it to\ntrue. `hostInitInjectLocation: ''entry''` is new beyond D55 (D58): the default\nwraps `src/router.tsx` into a bootstrap that re-exports nothing, and the client\nthen never hydrates — silently, with a 200 and the shell''s own content intact.\n\n`ClientOnly` rather than bare `lazy` is what compiles the remote import out of\nthe server chunk instead of merely deferring it (D55).\n\nExtracts `readEnv` from site.ts now the registry is a second consumer (D29).\nThe registry spec''s claim changes: the header now resolves, and its origin is\nasserted not to be the shell''s — D42''s failure mode, which a same-origin\ndefault would hide on localhost and 404 behind CloudFront.\n\nThe remote''s URL is still resolved at build time, so D12 is not yet satisfied;\nD61 records that and the duplicated default origin it forces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D58-D62 and correct the plan''s Header assertions\n\nBuilding Slice 3 forced five decisions, three of which correct something the\nplan already asserted. Recorded as numbered decisions rather than quiet edits\nso the corrections cannot be lost in a later revision.\n\nD58 and D61 are addenda to D55: the spike verified the built output, and both\nof these live outside what a build inspection can see.\n\nThe README''s design table claimed the Header existed on the v3 site. It does\nnot — no header, no nav component, and no element in the v3 tree carries an\nid. D59 records what was verified, what was ported, and what is invented.\n\nAlso corrects statements that would otherwise contradict the new log: slice\n03''s D19 bullet (\"never baked into the shell''s bundle\") and its Q13 bullet\nlisting ui-* as shared, and parallelization''s 2-to-3 edge, which rested on the\nsame wrong premise. The 3-to-4 edge is now marked as more than sequencing.\n\nPicks up a D57 index bullet that was already missing, unrelated to this work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: share the site-section contract and seed the content seam\n\nMoves the homepage section list out of @portfolio/feature-header into\n@portfolio/shared-fixtures as SITE_SECTIONS, with its shape as SiteSection\nin @portfolio/shared-types (D63). The ids are a contract between three\nindependently deployed units — the Header remote links to them, the Homepage\nremote puts them on section elements, and the shell''s header fallback links to\nthem when the Header is down. The shell cannot import the Header remote (D16,\nand the Nx boundary rule), so a hardcoded copy would have been a second source\nof truth nothing could compare against.\n\nAlso seeds the Slice 5-7 wave''s co-owned packages: HomepageContent and\nPortfolioItem as minimal container types, their fixture modules, and\nuse-content-stub.ts with all three read signatures stubbed. Each module carries\nan OWNER banner so a wave agent that opens the wrong file is told so by the\nfile (D67). Neither content type declares a `description` field — Q17 is open\nand the field''s shape is its slice''s to settle.\n\nFills the remote registry''s footer, homepage and portfolio-item rows on\n4175/4176/4177, and adds a `version` to RemoteEntry (D64) so every diagnostic\npayload can name the deployment it was pointing at.\n\nThe registry spec''s claim reverses here: it asserted those three remotes were\nundefined and now asserts they exist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: isolate each remote behind a shell-owned boundary and fallback\n\nImplements docs/architecture/mfe-failure-and-fallback-behavior.md at the D27\npath: one error boundary per remote, owned by the shell, with a fallback that\nis never federated (D16). A runtime exception or a failed remoteEntry.js now\ndegrades one region instead of taking the route down, which closes D62.\n\nLoading, render and hang failures arrive by different paths and end at the same\nfallback. A rejected import never settles into a React error boundary on its\nown, so the loader routes it there; an import that neither resolves nor rejects\nis caught by a timeout living in the Suspense fallback itself, where mounting\nstarts the clock and resolving unmounts it (R7).\n\nThe retry counter lives in the mount rather than the boundary (D65). React.lazy\ncaches the rejected promise, so clearing the boundary''s error in place re-serves\nthe same rejection — a retry button that looks like it works and does not. The\nmount rebuilds the lazy component per attempt and remounts the boundary by key,\nwhich is also how the boundary resets on success. The bound is visible in the\nUI, not only enforced: at zero attempts the button is replaced by an\nexplanation.\n\nAdds the shell''s location.hash re-apply (D43). A cold deep link looks for a\nsection before the Homepage remote has mounted, finds nothing, and never looks\nagain — silently. Readiness is expressed structurally, by a component that sits\ninside the remote''s own Suspense boundary.\n\nAn unknown portfolio slug is a shell-level not-found, deliberately not a\nfallback (D66): it offers no retry, because a missing item will never appear.\n\nEvery fallback''s visual treatment is invented — the v3 site has no\nremote-failure UI — and each is flagged in the slice''s completion report.\nEvery spec here was seen failing with its behaviour reverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: mount all four remotes in the shell and add /portfolio/$slug\n\nWires every remote through MfeRemoteMount, so each one carries its own error\nboundary, loading state, hang timeout and bounded retry. The Header''s mount\nloses the \"no error boundary yet\" caveat it shipped with in Slice 3; ClientOnly\nstays, since it is what keeps the import out of the SSR path (D55).\n\nThree of the four remotes do not exist yet when this lands. That is the point:\nthis file set is the seam slices 5, 6 and 7 would otherwise all edit while\nrunning concurrently, so it is built once and closed to them. A federation\nentry pointing at a dead origin is not a build error — the runtime fetches\nremoteEntry.js lazily, in the browser — so the failure lands where the boundary\nis already waiting, and the fallback path is observable from the day the seam is\ncreated rather than the day the remote lands.\n\nAdds the /portfolio/$slug route. The item is resolved in the route, before the\nremote is asked for, which is what keeps an unknown slug (a shell-level\nnot-found) apart from a downed remote (its fallback). They look similar and mean\nopposite things. The route also carries the per-slug head values, which is the\ncase D48 was taken for.\n\nOnly the Homepage mount sets isHashTarget: it is the region holding the sections\nan anchor can point at, and re-applying the hash in all three would fire three\nscrolls.\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is generated output, regenerated by the TanStack Start plugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: scaffold the footer, homepage and portfolio-item remotes as runnable apps\n\nCreates all six of the Slice 5-7 wave''s projects at once, tagged per D44, with\na single pnpm install. Adding an Nx project mutates the root tsconfig\nreferences and races pnpm-lock.yaml, so the manifest work is pulled out of the\nparallel slices and done here; each agent then writes code into a project that\nalready exists and registers nothing.\n\nEach remote is runnable, not merely present (D68). Two earlier attempts at a\nthinner scaffold failed: targets with no vite config started Vite on its\ndefaults, bound a random free port instead of the registry''s, printed a URL and\nexited 0 — a target that looked like it worked and served nothing, with every\ngate green. Removing the targets made the failure honest but left three\ndirectories that could not be started at all. So each app carries the full\nskeleton copied from apps/header (D55), and `nx dev <remote>` now serves it on\nits own strictPort port and publishes remoteEntry.js.\n\nEach feature lib carries a placeholder component at the real name, so its slice\nreplaces a body rather than building a skeleton. Every placeholder''s spec\nasserts the string \"Slice N fills this\", which fails the moment the real\ncomponent lands — the placeholder cannot survive its own slice, and it cannot be\nquietly left in either.\n\nThe line held is wiring, not content: no placeholder makes a decision its slice\nowns. The Homepage placeholder renders the SITE_SECTIONS ids and\nscroll-mt-header only because those are an existing contract (D43, D63), and it\nrenders no section content. It is also what let D43''s cold deep link be verified\nlive for the first time.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D63-D68 and what Slice 4 actually built\n\nSix decisions came out of building the slice. Three are things the architecture\ndoc implies but does not say and the implementation could not stay silent about:\nthe fallback render prop and where the retry counter has to live (D65), the\nnot-found that is deliberately not a fallback (D66), and the section list that\nneeded a third reader the shell cannot import (D63). The rest are RemoteEntry''s\nversion field (D64), the wave''s per-file split (D67), and the expansion that\nmade all four remotes runnable (D68).\n\nThe filename says D63-D67 and the file holds six. D68 arrived after the file was\nnamed, and decisions are never renumbered, so the name stays and the index\ncarries the real range.\n\nparallelization.md gains the named per-file split the wave cannot start without:\nwhich module of the co-owned libs/shared/types and libs/shared/fixtures each\nagent may open, and the list of paths closed to all three. It also corrects\nSlice 4''s file estimate, which was 2.25x low for three reasons worth carrying\ninto slices 5-7, and supersedes its own claim that the apps have no tsconfig.\n\nSlice 4''s own file records both correction rounds and separates what was seen\non screen from what was only verified in a spec. The header fallback and the\nsuccessful-retry path were never seen in a browser, and the doc says so.\n\nSlices 5-7 shrank: each is now replace one component and its spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsgYaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ7sQAEBTt3wzOj7DAZoS2xHMfk4Q\nu+vISZx8g+9onQbHhzj3cxuHKHxVpmvYxOgTmr5FsqRqFyW0JyO0BETJR8CEjZhj\nlGB3sMhhBZzQpVis8pfsh6fy8u5n9LfDDSCm/m0rdoMf7DUehhjOtpfV3m2RPuDO\njedIW5vzXZEdd2IaHNW4Ew4l9D0FmYKTJM+Mxlnz0iT/otq0WGp/AVbfaPQq8ays\nXNdjAogOKGlHKFi85zi1OZbfWIB77Rura284c7Qfv1TY9guca37tXKaHDO7k71wV\npC7xupaFpaWqT7tgO3seP4Xz9jx+oovoBDNGeZRP2HyVfgNZqxIJAGdLjvUFhKu8\n6dj/qqUnY7cOdztryCrI/KNHcbVOM5Ju4BF520ujRdJyICfjnS/S803C+GoK4gp1\nsQ1hIDP/nChUErPqmFwlzAsJDZLFamBeszAyDsuGYAfGbbEPdrhBh5UIU794/a3F\nHa8pMO18K+Gog9x/Foxu1QWl6vA0lWFZIQGxA6Q3uhzNjuk0MdyWHpWGK1oeGk97\nxA06NwnGahUPZLy9zDXqqoPSxA2fNm0lN0+b4WPgtWyLw2FtvcCWEyrz07pMMOfX\nBGHQma9uUWrnzKiKHNkhOrBruIGPo+z+yPTJnhZjViLrg/rJGWiMXzmaB7eYMGHp\nWMrokL52mpI9LAzF57vl\n=17BO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T04:37:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7","node_id":"C_kwDOCok6WdoAKGJmYjc1Yjk2NmNhMmUzNjQ4NTMxNThkNTA2NWIwMTM0OGUzMjMwZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commit/7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618","sha":"7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618"}],"sha":"bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/bfb75b966ca2e364853158d5065b01348e3230d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11258082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AnselmMarie","id":11258082,"login":"AnselmMarie","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU4MDgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AnselmMarie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/commits/7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:57:02Z","email":"AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anselm Marie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:57:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/amarie/new design (#42)\n\n* clean up\n\n* docs: add mfe-architecture plan, with post-D46 residue and link rot corrected\n\nFirst commit of the MFE architecture plan directory. The plan itself was\nwritten in earlier sessions; this commit lands it alongside corrections to\nthe stale claims it had accumulated after the 2026-09-20 tooling prune (D46).\n\nCorrections included here:\n\n- Slice 1''s workspace-root block described the pre-prune repo. It claimed the\n  three ESLint plugins were absent, that biome.json was cosmikata''s file\n  verbatim with no @portfolio import group, that .nxignore carried a _wip\n  entry, and that `next` needed removing — none of which is true of the\n  working tree. Replaced with a created/existing split so a builder extends\n  those files rather than rewriting correct ones.\n- Slice 1 claimed Q15 was still open eighteen lines above saying it closed,\n  and omitted Q14, which open-questions.md lists as blocking it.\n- D44, D45, Q11 and Q16 carried the same pre-prune residue; D32 still said Q9\n  was left open after D36 closed it; D11 named .dev.vars.example, a Cloudflare\n  artifact retired by D31.\n- model.md and slice 6 called the fixtures placeholder/fake against D41, which\n  makes them the site''s real portfolio copy. model.md''s tree omitted the infra\n  CDK project required by D37.\n- Six links into risks.md resolved to nothing: R2, R8 and R10 had no explicit\n  anchors and their headings carry trailing text.\n- use-content-stub.ts is now owned by libs/shared/fixtures. Slice 7 described\n  importing it from libs/features/homepage, which the scope constraints in\n  tools/eslint/module-boundaries.mjs reject at error.\n- Slice 3''s spike gate said \"if all three pass\" over four checks, skipping the\n  cross-origin asset check, and pointed past Slice 4.\n\nVerified: 674 relative links and anchors resolve, 0 broken. The checker was\nproven able to fail by removing an anchor and watching it go red. Index 113\nlines (cap 200), largest other file 485 (cap 500).\n\nLeft open deliberately: Q14, the @portfolio/ui-* Module Federation sharing\nquestion, and the executability gaps raised in review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: convert workspace root to Nx + pnpm, retiring the Next.js stack\n\nThe v2 site was a single Next.js app. The MFE architecture plan needs an Nx\nmonorepo root, so this replaces the root tooling wholesale (D46, closing Q15).\n\npackage.json goes 2.0.5 -> 3.0.0: the Next.js stack and its 18 devDependencies\nare removed (D6), replaced with nx/biome/eslint scripts and the seven\ndevDependencies the lint, format and typecheck gates need. packageManager is\npinned to pnpm 10.33.0 and engines to Node >=22 <23, completing D45.\n\ntools/eslint/module-boundaries.mjs is new and load-bearing: it is the scope and\ntype constraint table that turns D2, D25, D27 and D29 from conventions a\nreviewer has to catch by eye into @nx/enforce-module-boundaries rules. Its\nabsence was what made the ESLint config fail at load (Q11).\n\neslint.config.mjs wires that table in, with projectService for type-aware\nlinting and a relaxed block for config files. Note it sets max-depth to 2\nglobally, which is strict and not yet reflected in any plan slice.\n\n.npmrc excludes @esbuild/* from hoisting: four esbuild versions coexist in the\nworkspace and hoisting any one of them breaks the others with a host/binary\nversion mismatch. The comment explaining that is the point of the file.\n\n.gitignore lands as-is, still carrying Next.js, Expo, Wrangler, OpenNext and\nUniwind sections that are all dead here. Slice 1 of the MFE plan owns pruning\nit; it is committed stale deliberately rather than by oversight.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: make the root an installable Nx + pnpm workspace with its gates\n\nAdds the manifests the workspace never had — nx.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml,\ntsconfig.base.json and the lockfile — plus the two gates the rules already\nassumed existed.\n\ntools/scripts/check-file-size.mjs implements the cap that .claude/rules/\nfile-size.md and plan-split-into-files.md both assert is enforced: source\nfiles hard-gated at 200 lines, plan docs at 500 (index 200) and ratcheted, so\na doc already over cap may shrink but not grow. The husky pre-commit hook and\nthe lint-staged block are what make it run.\n\nPrunes .gitignore of the dead Cloudflare Wrangler, Expo, Next.js, OpenNext,\nStorybook and Uniwind blocks, keeping .nx/polygraph, which was buried inside\nthe Expo block and is a live Nx ignore. Adds arm64 to .npmrc''s supported\narchitectures so pnpm does not fetch x64 binaries for a Graviton Lambda.\n\nNote this section is not independently installable: the lockfile references\nworkspace packages that arrive with the shared libs, the shell and infra.\n\nRefs: D45, D46, D49, D52\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the four libs/shared packages — remote registry, types, fixtures, utils\n\nOne package per concern (D29), all four created now even though some are\nnearly empty, because creating them later means editing root manifests during\nthe Slice 5-7 parallel wave.\n\nThe remote registry is deliberately empty: no remote exists until Slice 3, and\nRemoteRegistry is Partial so a lookup returns undefined rather than the type\nsystem promising entries that are not there. An unregistered remote and a\nremote that failed to load are the same state to a caller (D16).\n\nshared-config reads the environment behind a `typeof process` guard. The\nmodule is scope:shared so it ships to the browser, and the root route''s head\nruns on both sides — a bare process.env read throws during client navigation\nrather than during SSR. That spec was seen failing before the guard was\nrestored.\n\nshared-types runs with --passWithNoTests: it is type declarations with no\nruntime to assert, the named exception in no-deferred-specs.md.\n\nRefs: D12, D16, D19, D20, D29, D41, D48\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the TanStack Start shell and its feature lib, on Lambda from the first build\n\napps/shell holds config, the SSR entry and two routes; the page itself lives\nin libs/features/shell from the first commit, so D27 is established by example\nrather than asserted and then broken. The two are one change: the app does not\nrender without the lib, and the lib is unreachable without the app.\n\nThe Lambda target is set up now rather than retrofitted at Slice 8 (D31, D37).\nVerified: the build emits preset \"aws-lambda\" and exports a handler, and\ninvoking that handler with a synthetic Function URL event returns 200 with the\nrendered regions and the D48 metadata in the body.\n\n__root.tsx implements D48 — title, description and Open Graph emitted\nserver-side from the fixtures, confirmed present in the raw SSR response while\nD36 keeps every visible surface client-rendered.\n\nstyles.css carries the R3 fix. Tailwind 4 auto-detects sources from the Vite\nroot and skips node_modules, where pnpm symlinks every workspace lib, so the\nlayout rendered completely unstyled past a green build, typecheck and test\nrun. The @source line is the fix; Slice 2 moves it into libs/ui/theme.\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is generated by TanStack Router and excluded from Biome and\nthe file-size check; it is committed so a fresh clone typechecks before its\nfirst build.\n\nRefs: D4, D20, D27, D31, D36, D37, D48, D51, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the infra CDK project — defined, not deployed\n\nD37 creates this project in Slice 1, not Slice 8, so apps/shell is built\nagainst its real Lambda adapter from the first commit rather than against a\nplaceholder that gets replaced later. Nothing here runs cdk deploy, and the\nstack deliberately declares no resources.\n\nWhat it does carry are the two constants the shell''s build output depends on\nand that the plan never named: arm64 (D49) and nodejs22.x, pinned to match\n.nvmrc (D45). A spec asserts both, so a silent change cannot desync them from\n.npmrc''s supported architectures.\n\nA second spec asserts the synthesized template has zero resources. That is a\ntripwire, not a placeholder: if it fails, a resource was added outside Slice 8.\n\nThere is no deploy target, so nothing can be run by accident before then.\n\nRefs: D31, D37, D45, D49\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D48-D53, close Q14, and correct the plan against the working tree\n\nThree review passes over the plan found 26 disagreements between what it said\nand what the tree actually held. This applies them.\n\nSix new decisions. D48 closes Q14: the shell server-renders per-route metadata\nfrom the fixtures while D36 keeps every visible surface client-rendered. D49\nthrough D52 were taken while building Slice 1 rather than before it, and that\nis stated plainly at the top of their file — they are the four places the plan\ndescribed a workspace in enough detail to review but not enough to create.\nD50 is the load-bearing one: every gate command in every slice used bare Nx\nproject names while D21 fixed the package scope at @portfolio/*, and nothing\nconnected them, so all of them would have failed \"project not found\" on first\nrun. D53 records where the portfolio content comes from.\n\nThe wave described in parallelization.md was not disjoint. Slices 6 and 7 both\nwrite libs/shared/types and libs/shared/fixtures, and both read\nuse-content-stub.ts — a single file only Slice 6 was permitted to author. Both\nprojects are now co-owned with the coordinator writing the stub. Slice 4 was\nalso missing the six-project scaffold and the single pnpm install entirely,\nwithout which three concurrent agents race on the lockfile.\n\nSlice 4 no longer sends a builder to fix the architecture doc''s boundary path:\nthat edit landed in 031b8fc and the doc already carries it. Slice 3 no longer\nsays the server \"cannot\" load a remote — that was D30''s workerd finding, which\nD31 retired; D32 declines federated SSR by choice. Slice 9 is reclassified\ninvisible, since a passing test suite is not a visible surface.\n\nD10, D24, D26, D28 and D34 gain the corrections their text had outgrown. R3 is\nrecorded as occurred rather than predicted: it fired in Slice 1, rendering the\npage completely unstyled past a green build. questions-closed.md was split at\nQ9 when closing Q14 pushed it over the 500-line cap.\n\nQ17 is raised, not decided: every ported description is an HTML string, and\nthe Contentful plan makes that field editor-supplied, so the choice outlives\nthe fixture.\n\nRefs: D48, D49, D50, D51, D52, D53, Q14, Q17, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the libs/ui design system and a single Tailwind-aware cn\n\nSlice 2. Three packages — @portfolio/ui-theme, ui-primitives and\nui-components — plus the shell rewired to consume them instead of painting\nitself with ad-hoc Tailwind. The page is pixel-identical afterwards, which is\nthe correct outcome: this changes where the styling comes from, not what it\nlooks like.\n\nlibs/ui/theme carries the @theme block moved out of apps/shell and, more\nimportantly, the @source declarations. That list is the R3 seam and it has\nalready caught this project once: Tailwind skips node_modules, every workspace\nlib is a symlink there, so a lib without its line renders completely unstyled\npast a green build, a green typecheck and a green test run. One stylesheet now\nowns the list so no app has to remember, and each new lib still needs a line.\n\nAll three projects are tagged (D44). Untagged, @nx/enforce-module-boundaries is\nsilently inert — the rule passes rather than failing — which would have left\nD25''s primitives/components split a convention again. The boundary was seen\nfiring: a feature importing ui-primitives directly is a lint error.\n\ncn is one implementation, in libs/shared/utils, built from clsx and\ntailwind-merge (D56). It shipped twice and neither copy merged: both were a\nfilter-and-join, so cn(''p-10'',''p-4'') returned both classes and stylesheet order\npicked the winner instead of the caller. That silently defeats the point of the\nwrapper split — a libs/ui/components wrapper forwarding a className could not\noverride a primitive''s default. Nothing exercised that path yet, so it was\nlatent rather than broken. The spec was seen failing against the old\nimplementation on three assertions, including the defect itself.\n\nIt lives in libs/shared/utils because type:shared is the only tier reachable\nfrom ui-primitives, ui-components and feature alike, so one copy needs no\nre-export chain, and because module-boundaries.mjs already named shared utils\nas this helper''s home. That sits against D29 and the tension is recorded in\nD56 rather than waved through. primitives/components.json aliases the shadcn\nCLI''s utils at @portfolio/shared-utils so the next `shadcn add` cannot\nscaffold a third copy.\n\nNo Storybook (D38). Nothing renders a libs/ui component against a real\nstylesheet in isolation until Slice 9''s computed-style assertions, so R3 has\nno browser-level check until then — verified here by looking at the page.\n\nRefs: D3, D25, D26, D29, D38, D40, D44, D50, D51, D56, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D54-D56, close Q2, and re-plan Slice 3 around the passed spike\n\nThe spike gate Slice 3 was blocked on was run early, in its own worktree, in\nparallel with Slice 2 (D54). It passed all four checks, so Q2 — does\n@module-federation/vite compose with TanStack Start? — closes as D55 rather\nthan staying an open question in front of the slice.\n\nD55 carries the verbatim working config, the versions it was proven against,\nand, as importantly, the four things the spike did not prove. Two of its\nfindings were each found by failing first: applyToEnvironment is needed to keep\nfederation out of the aws-lambda server bundle, and remotes needs the object\nform with type: ''module''. The worktree that found them is deleted, which is why\nthe config is recorded verbatim instead of referenced.\n\nD56 records the cn correction that shipped in 5656392 — one clsx +\ntailwind-merge implementation in libs/shared/utils, replacing two copies that\nwere both a filter-and-join. Its tension with D29 is written down rather than\nwaved through.\n\nSlices 3, 5, 6 and 7 are re-planned against the proven seam, and the\nopen-questions ledger drops from two open to one: only Q17 remains.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: drive the workspace with Nx plugins and TS project references\n\nNx was installed and was the entry point, but it was not a build system: ten\nproject.json files carried 28 hand-written nx:run-commands entries shelling out\nto tsc, eslint and vitest with a cwd, and only nx core was installed. The\ncommands were duplicated per project and had already drifted —\n--passWithNoTests on two, --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern on one, bare\nvitest run on the rest.\n\n@nx/js/typescript, @nx/vite and @nx/eslint now infer typecheck, test and lint\nfrom the tsconfig, vitest config and ESLint config each project already had.\nproject.json drops to name, type, source root and tags — the tags stay because\n@nx/enforce-module-boundaries is silently inert for an untagged project.\n\nTypeScript moves to project references. tsconfig.base.json gains composite and\nloses its paths map, a root tsconfig.json lists every project, and nx sync\ngenerates each project''s references from the Nx graph with nx sync:check\nfailing on drift. Cross-package resolution now goes through the workspace\nsymlinks and each package''s exports, so a package''s public type surface is a\nreal compilation boundary rather than whatever its source happened to export.\nLibraries stay source-only: build is false, nothing gains a dist, and\ntypecheck emits declarations to a gitignored out-tsc purely so the next project\nin the graph can be checked against them.\n\nTwo targets stay explicit, which is the right outcome rather than a shortcut.\n@nx/vite only infers a build given build.lib, rollupOptions.input or a root\nindex.html; TanStack Start has none of the three and emits .output/.nitro\nrather than dist, so an inferred target would also have cached the wrong\ndirectory. infra:synth has no plugin.\n\nFour traps, each silent on its own. noEmit turns the typecheck target into an\necho that still passes and checks nothing, so it is gone in favour of\n--emitDeclarationOnly. The inferred test command is a bare vitest, which\nwatches unless CI is set, so watch: false moves into the configs now that the\nconfigs are the source of truth. @nx/vite 21.6.11 declares vite ^5-7 and\nvitest ^1-3 against this workspace''s vite 8.3.0 and vitest 5.0.1 — everything\nworks, but the next @nx/vite upgrade is load-bearing, not routine. And graph\nconstruction failed outright until apps/shell/vite.config.ts pinned\nroot: import.meta.dirname, because Nx loads vite configs from the workspace\nroot and Start resolves its router entry against the root.\n\nui-theme now reports zero targets: it holds one theme.css and nothing lintable,\nso @nx/eslint infers nothing. Its old target already ran ESLint with\n--no-error-on-unmatched-pattern, so nothing is lost, but the empty list should\nnot be read as a misconfiguration.\n\nEvery gate was seen failing before this was reported green, each revert\nconfirmed with git diff first: a wrong return type gives TS2322; a\nnon-existent cross-package import gives TS2305 with the ^typecheck dependency\nrunning first, which is what proves the references carry types across packages\ninstead of falling back to any; a nested ternary and a forbidden import each\ntrip their lint rule; a failing assertion goes red and terminates with CI\nunset, confirming the watch fix. Cold cache is green for 9 projects, a second\nrun serves 27/27 from cache, shell:build produces apps/shell/.output, and the\ndev server renders with its theme intact after the root change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add a gates-only workflow, with nx sync:check ahead of the gates\n\nEvery gate in this repo ran from the lint-staged pre-commit hook, which only\ncovers commits made locally — a push from anywhere that skipped hooks bypassed\nall of them, including the 200-line cap D52 added. D57 makes that worse rather\nthan better: TypeScript project references are generated from the Nx graph, and\nthey drift silently, so nx sync:check runs first, before the gates it would\notherwise make misleading rather than merely red.\n\nNode comes from .nvmrc and pnpm from packageManager, per D45/D46 — the workflow\nreads both pins rather than restating either.\n\nrun-many, not affected, and deliberately so: ten projects run in seconds, while\naffected given a wrong base checks nothing and reports green. D23''s affected is\nabout the deploy jobs, where skipping unchanged work is the point. Slice 8 owns\nthose and extends this workflow with them, plus the project-tag check and the\nReact-major check (D39); it should not add a second workflow.\n\nTwo things the file-size step had to work around. Called the obvious way the\nscript checks nothing: with no arguments it diffs against HEAD, which in a\nfresh checkout is empty, so it would run, pass, and assert nothing — the step\ncomputes the changed paths against the base and passes them explicitly, with a\nfallback to every tracked source and plan file when there is no usable base.\nAnd the plan-doc ratchet is genuinely weaker here than at a desk, because it\ngrandfathers a doc against its own line count at HEAD and CI''s HEAD already\ncontains the change, so an over-cap plan doc warns instead of failing. Source\nfiles are hard-gated exactly as they are locally. Slice 8 should tighten the\nratchet by teaching the script a base ref; the caveat is recorded in the file\nrather than left to be rediscovered.\n\nBoth new gates were seen failing before this was reported working: a 250-line\nsource file exits 1 naming the cap, and a deleted project reference gives\n\"out of sync\" naming the missing reference. The step''s shell logic was run\nagainst a real 36-file commit range. The action versions and runner behaviour\nare unproven until the first run on GitHub, which cannot be executed from here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9242bbaae74e725b0bc1f63a2a46b09c95461b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/trees/b9242bbaae74e725b0bc1f63a2a46b09c95461b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnselmMarie/anselmmarie.github.io/git/commits/7b3bf6054c0616193b9aeba5c3d07c8c27eb4618","verification":{"payload":"tree b9242bbaae74e725b0bc1f63a2a46b09c95461b3\nparent 39bbe56de4468f9415a16195892f138a0b9f3a78\nauthor Anselm Marie <AnselmMarie@users.noreply.github.com> 1790020622 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790020622 -0400\n\nFeat/amarie/new design (#42)\n\n* clean up\n\n* docs: add mfe-architecture plan, with post-D46 residue and link rot corrected\n\nFirst commit of the MFE architecture plan directory. The plan itself was\nwritten in earlier sessions; this commit lands it alongside corrections to\nthe stale claims it had accumulated after the 2026-09-20 tooling prune (D46).\n\nCorrections included here:\n\n- Slice 1''s workspace-root block described the pre-prune repo. It claimed the\n  three ESLint plugins were absent, that biome.json was cosmikata''s file\n  verbatim with no @portfolio import group, that .nxignore carried a _wip\n  entry, and that `next` needed removing — none of which is true of the\n  working tree. Replaced with a created/existing split so a builder extends\n  those files rather than rewriting correct ones.\n- Slice 1 claimed Q15 was still open eighteen lines above saying it closed,\n  and omitted Q14, which open-questions.md lists as blocking it.\n- D44, D45, Q11 and Q16 carried the same pre-prune residue; D32 still said Q9\n  was left open after D36 closed it; D11 named .dev.vars.example, a Cloudflare\n  artifact retired by D31.\n- model.md and slice 6 called the fixtures placeholder/fake against D41, which\n  makes them the site''s real portfolio copy. model.md''s tree omitted the infra\n  CDK project required by D37.\n- Six links into risks.md resolved to nothing: R2, R8 and R10 had no explicit\n  anchors and their headings carry trailing text.\n- use-content-stub.ts is now owned by libs/shared/fixtures. Slice 7 described\n  importing it from libs/features/homepage, which the scope constraints in\n  tools/eslint/module-boundaries.mjs reject at error.\n- Slice 3''s spike gate said \"if all three pass\" over four checks, skipping the\n  cross-origin asset check, and pointed past Slice 4.\n\nVerified: 674 relative links and anchors resolve, 0 broken. The checker was\nproven able to fail by removing an anchor and watching it go red. Index 113\nlines (cap 200), largest other file 485 (cap 500).\n\nLeft open deliberately: Q14, the @portfolio/ui-* Module Federation sharing\nquestion, and the executability gaps raised in review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: convert workspace root to Nx + pnpm, retiring the Next.js stack\n\nThe v2 site was a single Next.js app. The MFE architecture plan needs an Nx\nmonorepo root, so this replaces the root tooling wholesale (D46, closing Q15).\n\npackage.json goes 2.0.5 -> 3.0.0: the Next.js stack and its 18 devDependencies\nare removed (D6), replaced with nx/biome/eslint scripts and the seven\ndevDependencies the lint, format and typecheck gates need. packageManager is\npinned to pnpm 10.33.0 and engines to Node >=22 <23, completing D45.\n\ntools/eslint/module-boundaries.mjs is new and load-bearing: it is the scope and\ntype constraint table that turns D2, D25, D27 and D29 from conventions a\nreviewer has to catch by eye into @nx/enforce-module-boundaries rules. Its\nabsence was what made the ESLint config fail at load (Q11).\n\neslint.config.mjs wires that table in, with projectService for type-aware\nlinting and a relaxed block for config files. Note it sets max-depth to 2\nglobally, which is strict and not yet reflected in any plan slice.\n\n.npmrc excludes @esbuild/* from hoisting: four esbuild versions coexist in the\nworkspace and hoisting any one of them breaks the others with a host/binary\nversion mismatch. The comment explaining that is the point of the file.\n\n.gitignore lands as-is, still carrying Next.js, Expo, Wrangler, OpenNext and\nUniwind sections that are all dead here. Slice 1 of the MFE plan owns pruning\nit; it is committed stale deliberately rather than by oversight.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: make the root an installable Nx + pnpm workspace with its gates\n\nAdds the manifests the workspace never had — nx.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml,\ntsconfig.base.json and the lockfile — plus the two gates the rules already\nassumed existed.\n\ntools/scripts/check-file-size.mjs implements the cap that .claude/rules/\nfile-size.md and plan-split-into-files.md both assert is enforced: source\nfiles hard-gated at 200 lines, plan docs at 500 (index 200) and ratcheted, so\na doc already over cap may shrink but not grow. The husky pre-commit hook and\nthe lint-staged block are what make it run.\n\nPrunes .gitignore of the dead Cloudflare Wrangler, Expo, Next.js, OpenNext,\nStorybook and Uniwind blocks, keeping .nx/polygraph, which was buried inside\nthe Expo block and is a live Nx ignore. Adds arm64 to .npmrc''s supported\narchitectures so pnpm does not fetch x64 binaries for a Graviton Lambda.\n\nNote this section is not independently installable: the lockfile references\nworkspace packages that arrive with the shared libs, the shell and infra.\n\nRefs: D45, D46, D49, D52\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the four libs/shared packages — remote registry, types, fixtures, utils\n\nOne package per concern (D29), all four created now even though some are\nnearly empty, because creating them later means editing root manifests during\nthe Slice 5-7 parallel wave.\n\nThe remote registry is deliberately empty: no remote exists until Slice 3, and\nRemoteRegistry is Partial so a lookup returns undefined rather than the type\nsystem promising entries that are not there. An unregistered remote and a\nremote that failed to load are the same state to a caller (D16).\n\nshared-config reads the environment behind a `typeof process` guard. The\nmodule is scope:shared so it ships to the browser, and the root route''s head\nruns on both sides — a bare process.env read throws during client navigation\nrather than during SSR. That spec was seen failing before the guard was\nrestored.\n\nshared-types runs with --passWithNoTests: it is type declarations with no\nruntime to assert, the named exception in no-deferred-specs.md.\n\nRefs: D12, D16, D19, D20, D29, D41, D48\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the TanStack Start shell and its feature lib, on Lambda from the first build\n\napps/shell holds config, the SSR entry and two routes; the page itself lives\nin libs/features/shell from the first commit, so D27 is established by example\nrather than asserted and then broken. The two are one change: the app does not\nrender without the lib, and the lib is unreachable without the app.\n\nThe Lambda target is set up now rather than retrofitted at Slice 8 (D31, D37).\nVerified: the build emits preset \"aws-lambda\" and exports a handler, and\ninvoking that handler with a synthetic Function URL event returns 200 with the\nrendered regions and the D48 metadata in the body.\n\n__root.tsx implements D48 — title, description and Open Graph emitted\nserver-side from the fixtures, confirmed present in the raw SSR response while\nD36 keeps every visible surface client-rendered.\n\nstyles.css carries the R3 fix. Tailwind 4 auto-detects sources from the Vite\nroot and skips node_modules, where pnpm symlinks every workspace lib, so the\nlayout rendered completely unstyled past a green build, typecheck and test\nrun. The @source line is the fix; Slice 2 moves it into libs/ui/theme.\n\nrouteTree.gen.ts is generated by TanStack Router and excluded from Biome and\nthe file-size check; it is committed so a fresh clone typechecks before its\nfirst build.\n\nRefs: D4, D20, D27, D31, D36, D37, D48, D51, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the infra CDK project — defined, not deployed\n\nD37 creates this project in Slice 1, not Slice 8, so apps/shell is built\nagainst its real Lambda adapter from the first commit rather than against a\nplaceholder that gets replaced later. Nothing here runs cdk deploy, and the\nstack deliberately declares no resources.\n\nWhat it does carry are the two constants the shell''s build output depends on\nand that the plan never named: arm64 (D49) and nodejs22.x, pinned to match\n.nvmrc (D45). A spec asserts both, so a silent change cannot desync them from\n.npmrc''s supported architectures.\n\nA second spec asserts the synthesized template has zero resources. That is a\ntripwire, not a placeholder: if it fails, a resource was added outside Slice 8.\n\nThere is no deploy target, so nothing can be run by accident before then.\n\nRefs: D31, D37, D45, D49\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D48-D53, close Q14, and correct the plan against the working tree\n\nThree review passes over the plan found 26 disagreements between what it said\nand what the tree actually held. This applies them.\n\nSix new decisions. D48 closes Q14: the shell server-renders per-route metadata\nfrom the fixtures while D36 keeps every visible surface client-rendered. D49\nthrough D52 were taken while building Slice 1 rather than before it, and that\nis stated plainly at the top of their file — they are the four places the plan\ndescribed a workspace in enough detail to review but not enough to create.\nD50 is the load-bearing one: every gate command in every slice used bare Nx\nproject names while D21 fixed the package scope at @portfolio/*, and nothing\nconnected them, so all of them would have failed \"project not found\" on first\nrun. D53 records where the portfolio content comes from.\n\nThe wave described in parallelization.md was not disjoint. Slices 6 and 7 both\nwrite libs/shared/types and libs/shared/fixtures, and both read\nuse-content-stub.ts — a single file only Slice 6 was permitted to author. Both\nprojects are now co-owned with the coordinator writing the stub. Slice 4 was\nalso missing the six-project scaffold and the single pnpm install entirely,\nwithout which three concurrent agents race on the lockfile.\n\nSlice 4 no longer sends a builder to fix the architecture doc''s boundary path:\nthat edit landed in 031b8fc and the doc already carries it. Slice 3 no longer\nsays the server \"cannot\" load a remote — that was D30''s workerd finding, which\nD31 retired; D32 declines federated SSR by choice. Slice 9 is reclassified\ninvisible, since a passing test suite is not a visible surface.\n\nD10, D24, D26, D28 and D34 gain the corrections their text had outgrown. R3 is\nrecorded as occurred rather than predicted: it fired in Slice 1, rendering the\npage completely unstyled past a green build. questions-closed.md was split at\nQ9 when closing Q14 pushed it over the 500-line cap.\n\nQ17 is raised, not decided: every ported description is an HTML string, and\nthe Contentful plan makes that field editor-supplied, so the choice outlives\nthe fixture.\n\nRefs: D48, D49, D50, D51, D52, D53, Q14, Q17, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add the libs/ui design system and a single Tailwind-aware cn\n\nSlice 2. Three packages — @portfolio/ui-theme, ui-primitives and\nui-components — plus the shell rewired to consume them instead of painting\nitself with ad-hoc Tailwind. The page is pixel-identical afterwards, which is\nthe correct outcome: this changes where the styling comes from, not what it\nlooks like.\n\nlibs/ui/theme carries the @theme block moved out of apps/shell and, more\nimportantly, the @source declarations. That list is the R3 seam and it has\nalready caught this project once: Tailwind skips node_modules, every workspace\nlib is a symlink there, so a lib without its line renders completely unstyled\npast a green build, a green typecheck and a green test run. One stylesheet now\nowns the list so no app has to remember, and each new lib still needs a line.\n\nAll three projects are tagged (D44). Untagged, @nx/enforce-module-boundaries is\nsilently inert — the rule passes rather than failing — which would have left\nD25''s primitives/components split a convention again. The boundary was seen\nfiring: a feature importing ui-primitives directly is a lint error.\n\ncn is one implementation, in libs/shared/utils, built from clsx and\ntailwind-merge (D56). It shipped twice and neither copy merged: both were a\nfilter-and-join, so cn(''p-10'',''p-4'') returned both classes and stylesheet order\npicked the winner instead of the caller. That silently defeats the point of the\nwrapper split — a libs/ui/components wrapper forwarding a className could not\noverride a primitive''s default. Nothing exercised that path yet, so it was\nlatent rather than broken. The spec was seen failing against the old\nimplementation on three assertions, including the defect itself.\n\nIt lives in libs/shared/utils because type:shared is the only tier reachable\nfrom ui-primitives, ui-components and feature alike, so one copy needs no\nre-export chain, and because module-boundaries.mjs already named shared utils\nas this helper''s home. That sits against D29 and the tension is recorded in\nD56 rather than waved through. primitives/components.json aliases the shadcn\nCLI''s utils at @portfolio/shared-utils so the next `shadcn add` cannot\nscaffold a third copy.\n\nNo Storybook (D38). Nothing renders a libs/ui component against a real\nstylesheet in isolation until Slice 9''s computed-style assertions, so R3 has\nno browser-level check until then — verified here by looking at the page.\n\nRefs: D3, D25, D26, D29, D38, D40, D44, D50, D51, D56, R3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: record D54-D56, close Q2, and re-plan Slice 3 around the passed spike\n\nThe spike gate Slice 3 was blocked on was run early, in its own worktree, in\nparallel with Slice 2 (D54). It passed all four checks, so Q2 — does\n@module-federation/vite compose with TanStack Start? — closes as D55 rather\nthan staying an open question in front of the slice.\n\nD55 carries the verbatim working config, the versions it was proven against,\nand, as importantly, the four things the spike did not prove. Two of its\nfindings were each found by failing first: applyToEnvironment is needed to keep\nfederation out of the aws-lambda server bundle, and remotes needs the object\nform with type: ''module''. The worktree that found them is deleted, which is why\nthe config is recorded verbatim instead of referenced.\n\nD56 records the cn correction that shipped in 5656392 — one clsx +\ntailwind-merge implementation in libs/shared/utils, replacing two copies that\nwere both a filter-and-join. Its tension with D29 is written down rather than\nwaved through.\n\nSlices 3, 5, 6 and 7 are re-planned against the proven seam, and the\nopen-questions ledger drops from two open to one: only Q17 remains.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: drive the workspace with Nx plugins and TS project references\n\nNx was installed and was the entry point, but it was not a build system: ten\nproject.json files carried 28 hand-written nx:run-commands entries shelling out\nto tsc, eslint and vitest with a cwd, and only nx core was installed. The\ncommands were duplicated per project and had already drifted —\n--passWithNoTests on two, --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern on one, bare\nvitest run on the rest.\n\n@nx/js/typescript, @nx/vite and @nx/eslint now infer typecheck, test and lint\nfrom the tsconfig, vitest config and ESLint config each project already had.\nproject.json drops to name, type, source root and tags — the tags stay because\n@nx/enforce-module-boundaries is silently inert for an untagged project.\n\nTypeScript moves to project references. tsconfig.base.json gains composite and\nloses its paths map, a root tsconfig.json lists every project, and nx sync\ngenerates each project''s references from the Nx graph with nx sync:check\nfailing on drift. Cross-package resolution now goes through the workspace\nsymlinks and each package''s exports, so a package''s public type surface is a\nreal compilation boundary rather than whatever its source happened to export.\nLibraries stay source-only: build is false, nothing gains a dist, and\ntypecheck emits declarations to a gitignored out-tsc purely so the next project\nin the graph can be checked against them.\n\nTwo targets stay explicit, which is the right outcome rather than a shortcut.\n@nx/vite only infers a build given build.lib, rollupOptions.input or a root\nindex.html; TanStack Start has none of the three and emits .output/.nitro\nrather than dist, so an inferred target would also have cached the wrong\ndirectory. infra:synth has no plugin.\n\nFour traps, each silent on its own. noEmit turns the typecheck target into an\necho that still passes and checks nothing, so it is gone in favour of\n--emitDeclarationOnly. The inferred test command is a bare vitest, which\nwatches unless CI is set, so watch: false moves into the configs now that the\nconfigs are the source of truth. @nx/vite 21.6.11 declares vite ^5-7 and\nvitest ^1-3 against this workspace''s vite 8.3.0 and vitest 5.0.1 — everything\nworks, but the next @nx/vite upgrade is load-bearing, not routine. And graph\nconstruction failed outright until apps/shell/vite.config.ts pinned\nroot: import.meta.dirname, because Nx loads vite configs from the workspace\nroot and Start resolves its router entry against the root.\n\nui-theme now reports zero targets: it holds one theme.css and nothing lintable,\nso @nx/eslint infers nothing. Its old target already ran ESLint with\n--no-error-on-unmatched-pattern, so nothing is lost, but the empty list should\nnot be read as a misconfiguration.\n\nEvery gate was seen failing before this was reported green, each revert\nconfirmed with git diff first: a wrong return type gives TS2322; a\nnon-existent cross-package import gives TS2305 with the ^typecheck dependency\nrunning first, which is what proves the references carry types across packages\ninstead of falling back to any; a nested ternary and a forbidden import each\ntrip their lint rule; a failing assertion goes red and terminates with CI\nunset, confirming the watch fix. Cold cache is green for 9 projects, a second\nrun serves 27/27 from cache, shell:build produces apps/shell/.output, and the\ndev server renders with its theme intact after the root change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add a gates-only workflow, with nx sync:check ahead of the gates\n\nEvery gate in this repo ran from the lint-staged pre-commit hook, which only\ncovers commits made locally — a push from anywhere that skipped hooks bypassed\nall of them, including the 200-line cap D52 added. D57 makes that worse rather\nthan better: TypeScript project references are generated from the Nx graph, and\nthey drift silently, so nx sync:check runs first, before the gates it would\notherwise make misleading rather than merely red.\n\nNode comes from .nvmrc and pnpm from packageManager, per D45/D46 — the workflow\nreads both pins rather than restating either.\n\nrun-many, not affected, and deliberately so: ten projects run in seconds, while\naffected given a wrong base checks nothing and reports green. D23''s affected is\nabout the deploy jobs, where skipping unchanged work is the point. Slice 8 owns\nthose and extends this workflow with them, plus the project-tag check and the\nReact-major check (D39); it should not add a second workflow.\n\nTwo things the file-size step had to work around. Called the obvious way the\nscript checks nothing: with no arguments it diffs against HEAD, which in a\nfresh checkout is empty, so it would run, pass, and assert nothing — the step\ncomputes the changed paths against the base and passes them explicitly, with a\nfallback to every tracked source and plan file when there is no usable base.\nAnd the plan-doc ratchet is genuinely weaker here than at a desk, because it\ngrandfathers a doc against its own line count at HEAD and CI''s HEAD already\ncontains the change, so an over-cap plan doc warns instead of failing. Source\nfiles are hard-gated exactly as they are locally. Slice 8 should tighten the\nratchet by teaching the script a base ref; the caveat is recorded in the file\nrather than left to be rediscovered.\n\nBoth new gates were seen failing before this was reported working: a 250-line\nsource file exits 1 naming the cap, and a deleted project reference gives\n\"out of sync\" naming the missing reference. The step''s shell logic was run\nagainst a real 36-file commit range. The action versions and runner behaviour\nare unproven until the first run on GitHub, which cannot be executed from here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsYwOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtQ0QAIVLA/E1LheeRSOWtfQYGsAt\njuxTb7B3yPwUD3Un5dMNwt3w7Pa6g1zkdgSmBHfOv6WCQKb5d9hgFzEIvisoyv7p\n/hMsycAQ5XgRa+XaLUrqC8iAzFoj/d36PFZmDI0Qs31AXCzrau4d+LKGCrX0iPNi\nQVOhcJcJL7kHLQU/IhSMwxPXQLohVY3twEJ9xF4s0Z/bw5peDIWFUl4clQTupjVm\nQfN99V6y1ij/Gg3wMq4APBb+AV3Vm/mV4KjpnMlOZMcBrUK7rvqawm31sgr6z5zu\n38ohx+PFhAI8WvurfhstlikCUgpjgm4gW/CpAQBKpqZN5CkH+xBNrYwRK0GFDfKu\nB2zfu1Ls4pObUPkKHNH5PQxPkCacwMtm60eXr5LcfX01KR3oHM7cMgOG/w4zdU77\n1F49tAz8f+bpPD0sTAZPAnhq80FAEY+JJK6ulu7UW5GUgTfsIbxiXSEX8B/AW+gZ\npCzP/IyET42medl8BRC43hH1SfbxGhhgWaxTi56Bb0I7iCceCjYzRLHmWjd/KFp/\nHYIN7H1Q7ZHXFdG6sWNXMZAsbM2PwyMDLAfgNz0i8/nKRyjNgEEcmG28R2WOWee3\nr7GL4fALaI+zdktiH6lCy4RKqZGKnAb+eMNtjO+Sy9JPlBIpusS6NS+YGq9o6+7f\nWF35WVjiJB5yOgLZgL4R\n=ka50\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:57:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/