","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ihor-romaniuk","id":17108583,"login":"ihor-romaniuk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTA4NTgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ihor-romaniuk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-account/commits/bc85a0158fe4d8eaedf9e757eceeca0d692b1bc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:33:03Z","email":"ihor.romaniuk@raccoongang.com","name":"Ihor Romaniuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T21:33:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: send ''x'' as the social platform id for X (Twitter) (#1460)\n\nThe Twitter-to-X rename (#1215) changed the platform id sent to the\naccounts API from ''twitter'' to ''xTwitter'', but ''xTwitter'' is an i18n\nmessage key, not an API value. The accounts API only accepts facebook,\nx and linkedin, so the X field on the account settings page fails to\nsave with a 400, and an X link set on the profile page (which sends ''x'')\nis never matched when unpacking the account response, leaving the field\nblank.\n\nOnly the platform id was wrong; the social_link_x form key introduced by\nthe same change is correct and stays as is. No data migration is needed\nbecause ''xTwitter'' was always rejected by the serializer.","tree":{"sha":"8945d98ec6298731576b620bcf5f5dadb529f0e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-account/git/trees/8945d98ec6298731576b620bcf5f5dadb529f0e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-account/git/commits/bc85a0158fe4d8eaedf9e757eceeca0d692b1bc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8945d98ec6298731576b620bcf5f5dadb529f0e3\nparent ac13b6c2665ea729316b16fec9a011bb9b7d621d\nauthor Ihor Romaniuk <ihor.romaniuk@raccoongang.com> 1789075983 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789075983 -0600\n\nfix: send ''x'' as the social platform id for X (Twitter) (#1460)\n\nThe Twitter-to-X rename (#1215) changed the platform id sent to the\naccounts API from ''twitter'' to ''xTwitter'', but ''xTwitter'' is an i18n\nmessage key, not an API value. The accounts API only accepts facebook,\nx and linkedin, so the X field on the account settings page fails to\nsave with a 400, and an X link set on the profile page (which sends ''x'')\nis never matched when unpacking the account response, leaving the field\nblank.\n\nOnly the platform id was wrong; the social_link_x form key introduced by\nthe same change is correct and stays as is. No data migration is needed\nbecause ''xTwitter'' was always rejected by the serializer.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoyIPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMNcQADovYtQ/4Gn3CwU3YblWi3Ke\nAPEP08WL8jXQ67foZfuZZxF+d59a37KrEDURhsRblSC6oBMqJyy+DVl9pazdWH91\nzWqQP+bkosLHg6exIxHdhfXlCNB2yYBPu7Tg64LE/wYtESCfTVap3MNIXgPoZjaC\nJa+Tl8U1s+7Nb/EpSTZr9dPhgTbK1bBDFH7KXTEWWAZLG72X0UkwQT+ohxlQRUSo\nxanjVH2xbYLtIeYu8Ti2aXnxrBlvRcPFYprd/SUF+Xx7h1CAuk1PItYt1pprbXnn\nLUpvR2p9C4uS67LiBG+IeIHbaLe6ZwkINEBErNtXHvDwryfaeF0gulSzlXoqT3qp\ni1LLbFox2+GWpG8PQ3sFdYhAy1kU7uYO2l4/RqtbtIwrab+zS4fVhP4AEqRzCEXT\neNMwATdXd8eTISsuciJ54C0/LQyANF7E/D836T01VrP/c3OxA4qpN62d07N2D3Zi\n0RMyPk5C8L0c0JljaWmbEyc/g7L9yOnLLNJuEwhREjHVSPqWOa9zxB/0THlmIj07\naSNuk3t2xPQX8ubZ3FzidjVdb9MgRL1SVJ8mUju/x6DYka88NWxGghKOm3V