,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/338196b8f9337ada07fe41a4ea54f74f419e93c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T05:34:05Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T05:34:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: make the courseware redirects declarative and drop their fire-once guards (#2146)\n\nThe seven memoized redirect rules in redirects.ts and the render-time /preview\nstrip in Course.jsx become eight rule hooks in CoursewareRedirects.tsx, each\nreturning its redirect URL or null from the route and the page''s cached\nqueries, applied first match wins and rendered as one <Navigate replace>\nbeside TabPage. The two lookups are queries enabled while their rule applies:\nthe resume block is keyed by the visit to the course root (the router''s\nlocation key) so every visit asks again, and a unit''s parent sequence is\ncourse structure and kept for the session. CoursewareContainer''s memoized\nposition guard becomes an effect on the route''s unit id, and the container\nfetches the minimal course outline the redirects read. reselect and\nreact-redux leave src/courseware.\n\nBehaviour differences: outline failure over a loaded sequence resolves in one\nhop; the two lookups take the app''s retry policy and log their errors; the\nparent-sequence lookup is reused within a session where it was re-requested\nafter every navigation; the /preview strip for a user who is not staff happens\non the first render, not the second; the section-to-sequence and\nempty-sequence redirects keep the /preview prefix for staff.\n\nCloses #2135\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbc1b69c3a392620918215ee0b8f25481a249a40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/cbc1b69c3a392620918215ee0b8f25481a249a40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/338196b8f9337ada07fe41a4ea54f74f419e93c9","verification":{"payload":"tree cbc1b69c3a392620918215ee0b8f25481a249a40\nparent c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790919245 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790919245 -0400\n\nrefactor: make the courseware redirects declarative and drop their fire-once guards (#2146)\n\nThe seven memoized redirect rules in redirects.ts and the render-time /preview\nstrip in Course.jsx become eight rule hooks in CoursewareRedirects.tsx, each\nreturning its redirect URL or null from the route and the page''s cached\nqueries, applied first match wins and rendered as one <Navigate replace>\nbeside TabPage. The two lookups are queries enabled while their rule applies:\nthe resume block is keyed by the visit to the course root (the router''s\nlocation key) so every visit asks again, and a unit''s parent sequence is\ncourse structure and kept for the session. CoursewareContainer''s memoized\nposition guard becomes an effect on the route''s unit id, and the container\nfetches the minimal course outline the redirects read. reselect and\nreact-redux leave src/courseware.\n\nBehaviour differences: outline failure over a loaded sequence resolves in one\nhop; the two lookups take the app''s retry policy and log their errors; the\nparent-sequence lookup is reused within a session where it was re-requested\nafter every navigation; the /preview strip for a user who is not staff happens\non the first render, not the second; the section-to-sequence and\nempty-sequence redirects keep the /preview prefix for staff.\n\nCloses #2135\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv0JNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeP8QACJ86W1AkEMUND9dtJd8p97J\nwMGXjXvEiXmmVSy1CMGz4HJZaYpzi6fa/Ra64Q17u2sctAF/47QP+y1s9L43mLHK\n4Bd/2C+h+0pLH37FdpO1BuR5EIYMndy9QOZm7Vr9Tgt8d6ielaQo7f+TrkWaRHFD\nU0oUAzPxqsQ7ueKf06GkwRW/mWmrPU0GR6DVakO0UVSx+xITTOSZ+ViYYMyjH4GV\nTVNcksSqAncbGJr+4lto9OrUFyTy63tc5OCa7PMVxiHJA603U+5U9booQiQd8uc7\nxJjsgAzv1gR3n2Cc3pONJB5yNoeOzmmfBvBN789LLl/MVMt2Xt8CuN82C6zauolu\nGwU5EMcsJTK6hXZeIt6hY2NqsyVOZ9FN0yRg/X2x8dJXcUpfgokO7lnBRrTCW2hk\n6hSSwu3GUU7dsYI/uEKiYoo8TAjc/7WEXsRKAhMfusAviasX/kXghTAFJQFSUuzU\nkl2KriZu1/s3ATlmmWSZeunzPOlnda7y/a5K3aR8sd/aEF3P6OONb1ddF6PqJPLN\nUdP+dam4qgJxDlU9QFSxZ78BLfNoLSligPP0MatGAX63EH78qkzx0Pl+nCyfC+x1\nGhOHM+r/oIpJUeOIsxvGsnip7GL/ysaNc+R7COeuoaNbzuLI+xOMhhMwFN9bxpLd\noT/Orfid1AN8k4YPTmKT\n=d7Sx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T05:34:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/338196b8f9337ada07fe41a4ea54f74f419e93c9","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDMzODE5NmI4ZjkzMzdhZGEwN2ZlNDFhNGVhNTRmNzRmNDE5ZTkzYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7","sha":"c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7"}],"sha":"338196b8f9337ada07fe41a4ea54f74f419e93c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/338196b8f9337ada07fe41a4ea54f74f419e93c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:02:14Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:02:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: read the redirects and container from the courseware queries, not the model store (#2144)\n\n`CoursewareContainer` reads `celebrations` from its own courseware metadata\nquery, and `useCoursewareRedirects` reads the sections and the first section\nfrom the outline query it already holds, in place of the four `useSelector`\nreads of `state.models` through `modelReader.ts`, which is deleted. With no\nreader left, the metadata and outline queries stop mirroring `coursewareMeta`\nand `sections` into the model store. `CoursewareMeta.celebrations` names the\none field read, `firstSection`.\n\nNo behaviour or request change: the store entries were these queries''\nresults, written by the bridge in the query cache''s `onSuccess` before\nobservers re-rendered, so every render saw what the query results now\nprovide directly. The redirects'' `shallowEqual` / `defaultMemoize` guards\nstay for #2135.\n\nThe bridge suite in `apiHooks.test.tsx`, which pinned the merge of the two\nmirrors, is replaced by a `useSequenceIds` suite covering what it also\ntested: empty until the course is loaded, then the sequences in section\norder, and no request of its own.\n\nCloses #2089. Part of #1946 (layer D4 of #1977).\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: nothing writes the `coursewareMeta` or `sections` models\ninto the model store any more, so `useModel(''coursewareMeta'', courseId)` and\n`useModel(''sections'', sectionId)` return `{}`, and a direct\n`state.models.coursewareMeta[courseId]` read is `undefined`. Read the\ncourseware metadata from `useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false\n}).data`, and the outline''s course entry (`id`, `title`, `sectionIds`,\n`hasScheduledContent`) and `sections` from `useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId,\n{ enabled: false }).data`. The `org.openedx.frontend.learning.upgrade_panel.v1`\nslot keeps passing `model: ''coursewareMeta''`; a plugin that read the store\nthrough that prop switches to the query — see the PR description for the\nmigration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"496fe509e6ae27fb14d16c6987085a278284c126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/496fe509e6ae27fb14d16c6987085a278284c126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7","verification":{"payload":"tree 496fe509e6ae27fb14d16c6987085a278284c126\nparent d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790913734 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790913734 -0400\n\nrefactor!: read the redirects and container from the courseware queries, not the model store (#2144)\n\n`CoursewareContainer` reads `celebrations` from its own courseware metadata\nquery, and `useCoursewareRedirects` reads the sections and the first section\nfrom the outline query it already holds, in place of the four `useSelector`\nreads of `state.models` through `modelReader.ts`, which is deleted. With no\nreader left, the metadata and outline queries stop mirroring `coursewareMeta`\nand `sections` into the model store. `CoursewareMeta.celebrations` names the\none field read, `firstSection`.\n\nNo behaviour or request change: the store entries were these queries''\nresults, written by the bridge in the query cache''s `onSuccess` before\nobservers re-rendered, so every render saw what the query results now\nprovide directly. The redirects'' `shallowEqual` / `defaultMemoize` guards\nstay for #2135.\n\nThe bridge suite in `apiHooks.test.tsx`, which pinned the merge of the two\nmirrors, is replaced by a `useSequenceIds` suite covering what it also\ntested: empty until the course is loaded, then the sequences in section\norder, and no request of its own.\n\nCloses #2089. Part of #1946 (layer D4 of #1977).\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: nothing writes the `coursewareMeta` or `sections` models\ninto the model store any more, so `useModel(''coursewareMeta'', courseId)` and\n`useModel(''sections'', sectionId)` return `{}`, and a direct\n`state.models.coursewareMeta[courseId]` read is `undefined`. Read the\ncourseware metadata from `useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false\n}).data`, and the outline''s course entry (`id`, `title`, `sectionIds`,\n`hasScheduledContent`) and `sections` from `useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId,\n{ enabled: false }).data`. The `org.openedx.frontend.learning.upgrade_panel.v1`\nslot keeps passing `model: ''coursewareMeta''`; a plugin that read the store\nthrough that prop switches to the query — see the PR description for the\nmigration.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyzGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwTMQACb55xEF164dZAklUh4SSnl3\nPv5CdqeNF9Nuxq7d0cee46Z47Jvi7j1bw0Lu8yfAj8tQKjd6Q5BvD4w9BCPardd6\n+b13Z1oceuKGZBzcbdmsh03A097VsY5zAV3urtyE4pObeAEuplMFw7QoNPn6IiQr\nuiR8ZFJjLSTVS4Li+TdpZvw6WXZIJ/HNLQ59GD4cvFnUPQKTKeibIHZoQzKzjtIl\nvjDoOMMVWFbbEgEQ3ElQtvOYTb35nrHqn8pKmmN7LouZI/5qYxuAkpDPD4ACCQZ+\nqhMimsT6mexK8ZpLziWRYybodp/H4Q0Spe3VwFacolM8J8IXU4HjGKJk9MCMtMDH\ntbIicXwdP4lq0Iyd3BYELBreULyPUPrGA5+3Y1ZXfal584RgmCJaEiCURqw6Vtf7\nx430cw69wmwbpoYS1edF4jXRdn2yB7vsnE3Ls3oFVpcjVM5vLeX+4evlNLbd+aD9\nFQL4Byy9dlNJFqL2GopdSPNxtIg6FYUPKJmKb82V/TmemjMerx49nhPT231Zaeo6\nGBcjl6ZAzOB8Fd0oX1D/hK01i8fPgo+RRCEB2NlnZA3vdLDiuTobf2cMFxwXxyX2\nIpRp/mNsUtaj3XM2jTEBpNi9/p1/lVxIY63pMc3TUTdCGymbOSTnprkXq1yPm6lY\n0ANtOAxgq9vQLHX0SyFc\n=coPy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T04:02:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKGM0NjU1YjU2MzE3YjU2ZDVjZmM1YmE2M2MxNzdlNDBiZmVmYTBlZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530","sha":"d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530"}],"sha":"c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/c4655b56317b56d5cfc5ba63c177e40bfefa0ee7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:44:50Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:44:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: read sections and coursewareMeta from the courseware queries, not useModel (#2140)\n\nLayer D3 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The readers of the\n`coursewareMeta` and `sections` models read the query that owns each field:\n`useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false })` for the metadata, and\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false })` for the outline''s\ncourse entry (`id`, `title`, `sectionIds`, `hasScheduledContent`) and its\nsections. The integrity-signature write patches the cached metadata.\n\n- Readers: `Course`, `Sequence`, `CourseBreadcrumbs`, `useSequenceIds`,\n  `CourseExit`, `GetCourseExitNavigation`, `CourseCelebration`,\n  `LockPaywall`, the sequence-navigation and outline-sidebar hooks,\n  `UnitSuspense`, `useShouldDisplayHonorCode`, `SocialIcons`,\n  `UpgradePanel`, the entrance-exam alert and `CertificateStatus`. A local\n  that holds the metadata query''s result is named `coursewareMetadata`,\n  after its hook, where it used to hold the merged store entry.\n  `modelKeys` leaves `Unit/constants.ts`.\n- The course `title` comes from the outline at every reader. The store\n  entry took it from whichever of the two queries responded last since\n  #2023 split `fetchCourse`; the metadata endpoint''s `name` is the\n  HTML-escaped `display_name_with_default_escaped`, so a course named \"R&D\"\n  could show \"R&amp;D\" in the page title. Before #2023 the outline''s\n  unescaped title always won; this restores that. The metadata normalizer no\n  longer maps `name` to `title` at all, so the escaped value has no reader\n  to reach (#2137 records what is known and what is open).\n- `SidebarProvider` builds the widgets'' `course` from the metadata, the\n  outline''s course entry and the course-home metadata, in that order, as the\n  store entry was, and asks every widget with whatever is loaded, as it has\n  since #1885. `isAvailable` receives that spread''s own type, each field\n  optional; the built-in widgets type themselves from the slot.\n  `SidebarWidgetContext.course` gains the outline''s fields as optional.\n- `useSequenceIds` reads the course''s sections through a new\n  `useCourseSections(courseId)`, whose `select` does the lookup\n  `useModels(''sections'', …)` did; the outline''s query options move into a\n  `minimalCourseOutlineQuery(courseId)` factory that both outline hooks\n  spread.\n- `useSaveIntegritySignature` sets `userNeedsIntegritySignature: false` on\n  the cached metadata with `setQueryData` (a no-op when nothing is cached);\n  `useDispatch` leaves `courseware/data/apiHooks.ts`.\n- `CourseBreadcrumbs` builds its sections only once the outline is there,\n  so it renders while the outline is pending.\n- Tests: suites that read the seeded store for these models mock or seed\n  the queries. A test-only `CourseQueryGate` renders a component only while\n  the course''s queries are in the states a test names, by default the two\n  `TabPage` waits for having succeeded; `LoadedCourse` (now in\n  `course/test-utils.jsx`) and the unit and sequence navigation suites render\n  through it, and `initializeTestStore` gains `preventSequenceLoad` for the\n  sequence navigation''s loading case. The integrity writer suite asserts on\n  the cache. `CoursewareContainer` and `CourseExit` each count\n  the courseware metadata and the learning-sequences outline once per load.\n  Negative check: with one reader per page fetching, exactly the matching\n  count case fails.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the `coursewareMeta` store model, a mirror of the\ncourseware metadata query until #2089''s layer B removes it, no longer\npicks up the integrity-signature save: `userNeedsIntegritySignature` stays\n`true` there until the next fetch. Read it from\n`useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false }).data` in\n`courseware/data/apiHooks`. `useCoursewareMetadata(courseId).data` no longer\nhas `title` (see #2137); read the course title from\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.courses[courseId].title`\nor `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.title`. The page\ntitle and the course-end page''s title use the outline''s unescaped course\ntitle. A sidebar widget''s `isAvailable` typed from\n`SidebarWidget[''isAvailable'']` now sees every `course` field as optional\n(type-only; widgets are asked as before).\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2089.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23239dc7cf199b05f8ac8a8a05f2222063f3fd2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/23239dc7cf199b05f8ac8a8a05f2222063f3fd2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530","verification":{"payload":"tree 23239dc7cf199b05f8ac8a8a05f2222063f3fd2b\nparent b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790912690 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790912690 -0400\n\nrefactor!: read sections and coursewareMeta from the courseware queries, not useModel (#2140)\n\nLayer D3 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The readers of the\n`coursewareMeta` and `sections` models read the query that owns each field:\n`useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false })` for the metadata, and\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false })` for the outline''s\ncourse entry (`id`, `title`, `sectionIds`, `hasScheduledContent`) and its\nsections. The integrity-signature write patches the cached metadata.\n\n- Readers: `Course`, `Sequence`, `CourseBreadcrumbs`, `useSequenceIds`,\n  `CourseExit`, `GetCourseExitNavigation`, `CourseCelebration`,\n  `LockPaywall`, the sequence-navigation and outline-sidebar hooks,\n  `UnitSuspense`, `useShouldDisplayHonorCode`, `SocialIcons`,\n  `UpgradePanel`, the entrance-exam alert and `CertificateStatus`. A local\n  that holds the metadata query''s result is named `coursewareMetadata`,\n  after its hook, where it used to hold the merged store entry.\n  `modelKeys` leaves `Unit/constants.ts`.\n- The course `title` comes from the outline at every reader. The store\n  entry took it from whichever of the two queries responded last since\n  #2023 split `fetchCourse`; the metadata endpoint''s `name` is the\n  HTML-escaped `display_name_with_default_escaped`, so a course named \"R&D\"\n  could show \"R&amp;D\" in the page title. Before #2023 the outline''s\n  unescaped title always won; this restores that. The metadata normalizer no\n  longer maps `name` to `title` at all, so the escaped value has no reader\n  to reach (#2137 records what is known and what is open).\n- `SidebarProvider` builds the widgets'' `course` from the metadata, the\n  outline''s course entry and the course-home metadata, in that order, as the\n  store entry was, and asks every widget with whatever is loaded, as it has\n  since #1885. `isAvailable` receives that spread''s own type, each field\n  optional; the built-in widgets type themselves from the slot.\n  `SidebarWidgetContext.course` gains the outline''s fields as optional.\n- `useSequenceIds` reads the course''s sections through a new\n  `useCourseSections(courseId)`, whose `select` does the lookup\n  `useModels(''sections'', …)` did; the outline''s query options move into a\n  `minimalCourseOutlineQuery(courseId)` factory that both outline hooks\n  spread.\n- `useSaveIntegritySignature` sets `userNeedsIntegritySignature: false` on\n  the cached metadata with `setQueryData` (a no-op when nothing is cached);\n  `useDispatch` leaves `courseware/data/apiHooks.ts`.\n- `CourseBreadcrumbs` builds its sections only once the outline is there,\n  so it renders while the outline is pending.\n- Tests: suites that read the seeded store for these models mock or seed\n  the queries. A test-only `CourseQueryGate` renders a component only while\n  the course''s queries are in the states a test names, by default the two\n  `TabPage` waits for having succeeded; `LoadedCourse` (now in\n  `course/test-utils.jsx`) and the unit and sequence navigation suites render\n  through it, and `initializeTestStore` gains `preventSequenceLoad` for the\n  sequence navigation''s loading case. The integrity writer suite asserts on\n  the cache. `CoursewareContainer` and `CourseExit` each count\n  the courseware metadata and the learning-sequences outline once per load.\n  Negative check: with one reader per page fetching, exactly the matching\n  count case fails.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the `coursewareMeta` store model, a mirror of the\ncourseware metadata query until #2089''s layer B removes it, no longer\npicks up the integrity-signature save: `userNeedsIntegritySignature` stays\n`true` there until the next fetch. Read it from\n`useCoursewareMetadata(courseId, { enabled: false }).data` in\n`courseware/data/apiHooks`. `useCoursewareMetadata(courseId).data` no longer\nhas `title` (see #2137); read the course title from\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.courses[courseId].title`\nor `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.title`. The page\ntitle and the course-end page''s title use the outline''s unescaped course\ntitle. A sidebar widget''s `isAvailable` typed from\n`SidebarWidget[''isAvailable'']` now sees every `course` field as optional\n(type-only; widgets are asked as before).\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2089.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyiyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnzMQAFZdkry7oF37aGbsXWGMTQhD\nBAWLImwTA9TGfCChspkktr4+dr6bJmJS3Zaz6JAh8+KkfWxUdeS5I2+N9dbMeooC\nkay2kEwDVJ/0qY0yGNVtrY6VHcDebacz/EIY/c8PanMl20I3D8n8/b2DL+X8pMXJ\npKMD53NiqLr71ITa87qZIwonSJeex9Wof/ysvsSbQXmRdKh4Dn2cZ24XF4e71FII\nygfdbDyrB8iW/RPdvu4tfLYM1iGp//2HlzJud4VQKssYHB98/vhXay2DkcLenW1/\nhY92IzUdi/2fVlCvaGct9+VHHJaHfW5M+ksHCvH7UdweAdTc2pWVrS1XGpNZetBY\ng3947u3Mqhd+tm6BFgCdLoTWveIFvpxQwW9rfkX/47jBMgMO84Jfiz79HYYs0SBd\nDyOJp6yrq9OvotAuIPs3kaRqM6GbTM/aEvvKQp5+bosUCYcNznF1ITK0zmxX2qDK\n9BRshWY2nfRI0NNPXoYuhTSAuKQb+kH54Mu3TV/77Uyjg4AJPTtiWIlK7GwWiAn/\nLsX8Q+KvfFZUtAhqkOZLUS/oqGiOrOXGAYdJYM4S17ai7eX/fJw1kzcBEICh2Tv5\nB7U0qPlqIvpCp6R8XYhvGP9trU9K/E3GO8sxR/m/OenV5j41rd/abGGvoZP43vGc\n33D1ALfXjUq2chxBPhJu\n=ZsJ9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T03:44:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKGQxYzk1NzExN2ZkMTE5YTdiNTAyYWNmZDdmZjkyZjViZmU5NDg1MzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b","sha":"b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b"}],"sha":"d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/d1c957117fd119a7b502acfd7ff92f5bfe948530"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:28:19Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:28:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: handle a slow or failed outline on the courseware and course-end pages (#2139)\n\n* test: reproduce the courseware and course-end pages rendering before the outline has loaded\n\nAdds failing cases for #2138. Both pages gate `TabPage` on the course-home\nmetadata and the courseware metadata only, so when the learning-sequences\noutline lands after both, they render without it. Each case holds the\noutline request on a promise it releases later, the test form of the\nmanual repro''s delayed outline, and waits for both metadata queries by\ntheir query state rather than for the spinner, so the cases hold whether\nthe fix gates the pages on the outline again or makes each reader handle\nit pending.\n\n- `CourseBreadcrumbsSlot/index.test.tsx` (new): the default\n  `CourseBreadcrumbs` inserted as the slot''s README shows, through the real\n  FPF (`jest.unmock`, since `setupTest.js` mocks it for every suite), and\n  rendered behind a test gate that waits, as the courseware page does, for\n  both metadata queries. With the outline held the inserted breadcrumbs\n  throw in the `useModels` read; with the outline also in the gate they\n  render (a baseline that passes on this commit).\n- `CoursewareContainer.test`: the Next control is enabled before it can\n  navigate, a link to the current unit; the page title has an empty\n  segment.\n- `CourseExit.test`, when the outline is loading: the page does not\n  redirect, and does not render any course-end content. The page''s mode\n  depends on `hasScheduledContent`, which only the outline carries, so the\n  two cases run for three learners who are not passing, each of whom gets a\n  different wrong outcome on this commit: an audit learner who cannot view a\n  certificate is redirected, one who can is shown the not-passing page, and\n  a learner with no certificate data who cannot view one is shown the\n  celebration page.\n\nSix of these cases fail on this commit (the slot case, the two courseware\nones, and one per course-end learner); the next commit on this layer fixes them.\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2138.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: render the courseware and course-end pages correctly while the outline is loading\n\nSince the courseware and course-end pages stopped waiting for the\nlearning-sequences outline, they render in a window where only the\nmetadata has loaded. In that window:\n\n- The unit and sequence navigation now renders disabled until it has a\n  link to navigate to, instead of links to the current page.\n- Course sets the page title only once the outline has loaded, leaving\n  the tab page''s title in place rather than one with empty segments.\n- The course breadcrumbs show their existing not-loaded state instead\n  of throwing inside an inserted plugin.\n- The course-end page waits for the outline through TabPage, which now\n  accepts several tab-data queries (tabDataQueries) and shows every\n  failed query''s error detail, de-duplicated.\n\nWhen the outline fails, the course-end page again redirects to the\ncourse home, as it did before the React Query conversion.\n\nCloses #2138\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb5653ebaf4b77975f872ca59f292965b7751d26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/fb5653ebaf4b77975f872ca59f292965b7751d26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b","verification":{"payload":"tree fb5653ebaf4b77975f872ca59f292965b7751d26\nparent 76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790911699 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790911699 -0400\n\nfix: handle a slow or failed outline on the courseware and course-end pages (#2139)\n\n* test: reproduce the courseware and course-end pages rendering before the outline has loaded\n\nAdds failing cases for #2138. Both pages gate `TabPage` on the course-home\nmetadata and the courseware metadata only, so when the learning-sequences\noutline lands after both, they render without it. Each case holds the\noutline request on a promise it releases later, the test form of the\nmanual repro''s delayed outline, and waits for both metadata queries by\ntheir query state rather than for the spinner, so the cases hold whether\nthe fix gates the pages on the outline again or makes each reader handle\nit pending.\n\n- `CourseBreadcrumbsSlot/index.test.tsx` (new): the default\n  `CourseBreadcrumbs` inserted as the slot''s README shows, through the real\n  FPF (`jest.unmock`, since `setupTest.js` mocks it for every suite), and\n  rendered behind a test gate that waits, as the courseware page does, for\n  both metadata queries. With the outline held the inserted breadcrumbs\n  throw in the `useModels` read; with the outline also in the gate they\n  render (a baseline that passes on this commit).\n- `CoursewareContainer.test`: the Next control is enabled before it can\n  navigate, a link to the current unit; the page title has an empty\n  segment.\n- `CourseExit.test`, when the outline is loading: the page does not\n  redirect, and does not render any course-end content. The page''s mode\n  depends on `hasScheduledContent`, which only the outline carries, so the\n  two cases run for three learners who are not passing, each of whom gets a\n  different wrong outcome on this commit: an audit learner who cannot view a\n  certificate is redirected, one who can is shown the not-passing page, and\n  a learner with no certificate data who cannot view one is shown the\n  celebration page.\n\nSix of these cases fail on this commit (the slot case, the two courseware\nones, and one per course-end learner); the next commit on this layer fixes them.\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2138.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: render the courseware and course-end pages correctly while the outline is loading\n\nSince the courseware and course-end pages stopped waiting for the\nlearning-sequences outline, they render in a window where only the\nmetadata has loaded. In that window:\n\n- The unit and sequence navigation now renders disabled until it has a\n  link to navigate to, instead of links to the current page.\n- Course sets the page title only once the outline has loaded, leaving\n  the tab page''s title in place rather than one with empty segments.\n- The course breadcrumbs show their existing not-loaded state instead\n  of throwing inside an inserted plugin.\n- The course-end page waits for the outline through TabPage, which now\n  accepts several tab-data queries (tabDataQueries) and shows every\n  failed query''s error detail, de-duplicated.\n\nWhen the outline fails, the course-end page again redirects to the\ncourse home, as it did before the React Query conversion.\n\nCloses #2138\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyTTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdNsQAJDHGKgUZkTS4AEhAwoxSC1Q\nn9Pl4yQVYXOB3o5muTi9DsshSUsVpVMKIbzCxdZKFqd+sTmmQCCDfN9ZpMjErear\nul6Vszuqe88rvEOSMCBGosURHwfCashEQvbVwHlH1OoaQbD74ChcB6SiKpMvBzCO\n2o7PtM3kegutUsxAzjS2/Eu7U1blOtLbZG9bKrGwkbssemUyXRTiBSCjTjhcVFa0\nl8AT53/E6zRL1gR2HM0yK56RLzgqO28d7xmn+KBdSx6gx35djCOxVu3E9mtsu1cL\nfM50PQZf0czwXqMpVugUYOAyM7lhE//d5skOK2izfGXoU8NaZNUpZVs1tNnvT29D\nCH0YQIqSEujh8MwNk71LdlEsatA9Y7oE8j702/IemQb98v2fSGpKDccQdDhhMmfq\nKJgzp+Gf4NSj9m9aMqfT9OIX7mGd2JxP3oa7Q/zKHPaQ7jhcmbCl3bmG20h+b5+H\nVVOaHEviT4vv3FKwTjTma5wvVcG1iNBRXK07YZsZz83Qy0qookH7mLvSXQCYWohq\nOlG/4V1CG2liJITnIa8yx0PusW3hcEbd8sptEDmPT4BCBUiBmQrRrO68GGBqTd82\nO10Bz7rcFwtAkyZRGb51Yf0SsrKgiHssXbVIicJj8VnrXGshiXphu68EU8j5sWzK\njjeI2IHo2MY+3cQ2fPmx\n=+xRb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T03:28:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKGI1NWFkOWNiYWJmZDlhNjNjYjYwZjY0NTgxZDk4YjIyNmE2NjY2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711","sha":"76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711"}],"sha":"b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/b55ad9cbabfd9a63cb60f64581d98b226a66669b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:54:16Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:54:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: read sequences from the courseware queries, not useModel (#2134)\n\nLayer D2 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The eleven readers of the\n`sequences` model read the active sequence from the sequence query and other\nsequences'' id / title / sectionId from the outline query; the position writer\npatches the cached sequence; the three `sequences` store selectors in\nCoursewareContainer and redirects.ts read the cache; neither query writes the\n`sequences` model any more.\n\n- Readers take the query that owns the fields they read. `sectionId` only\n  ever came from the outline, so `Sequence`, `Course`, the entrance-exam\n  alert and `UnitNavigationEffortEstimate` read both queries. `CourseBreadcrumbs`\n  reads the outline once and indexes into it, replacing the `useModels` call\n  inside `.map()`. `UnitNavigationEffortEstimate` drops the `Object.keys`\n  guards #808 added for the `{}` sentinel.\n- `useSaveSequencePosition` writes `activeUnitIndex` into the cached sequence\n  at its exact key and snapshots the entry for rollback (the TanStack\n  optimistic-update shape); it drops\n  `useStore` / `useDispatch`.\n- The `sequences` selectors in `CoursewareContainer` and `redirects.ts` come\n  forward from D4: the bridge runs only from a fetch, so a store read of\n  `activeUnitIndex` would go stale once the writer moved. The redirect rules\n  take a full `SequenceMetadata`; their `unitIds !== undefined` guards, and\n  the fixtures for the store''s partial outline entry, go with the store.\n- Types come from #2129: `SequenceMetadata` from `courseware/data/sequenceMetadata`\n  and `MinimalCourseOutline` on `useMinimalCourseOutline`; this layer adds\n  none of its own.\n- Tests: the position suite asserts on the cache; the redirect suite builds\n  full fixtures; the `SequenceContent` suite renders behind the loaded\n  sequence as `Sequence` does; two container resume cases await the unit; a\n  new container case pins that each unit change saves the position and load\n  does not; another pins the first-section celebration record when next\n  leaves the first section. The breadcrumb suite''s section fixture passes\n  sequence ids, not objects, so its jump-nav rows are built. Negative check: with the position write disabled, exactly the two\n  hook cases that read the cached index fail.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''sequences'', id)` returns `{}`. The active\nsequence''s full shape is `useSequenceMetadata(sequenceId, { enabled: false })\n.data?.sequence`; any sequence''s `id`, `title` and `sectionId` are\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.sequences[id]`,\nboth from `courseware/data/apiHooks`.\n\nPart of #1946. Closes #2088.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bf697f26b06fa6993bea20ebba293db675f03e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/1bf697f26b06fa6993bea20ebba293db675f03e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711","verification":{"payload":"tree 1bf697f26b06fa6993bea20ebba293db675f03e9\nparent 5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790618056 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790618056 -0400\n\nrefactor!: read sequences from the courseware queries, not useModel (#2134)\n\nLayer D2 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The eleven readers of the\n`sequences` model read the active sequence from the sequence query and other\nsequences'' id / title / sectionId from the outline query; the position writer\npatches the cached sequence; the three `sequences` store selectors in\nCoursewareContainer and redirects.ts read the cache; neither query writes the\n`sequences` model any more.\n\n- Readers take the query that owns the fields they read. `sectionId` only\n  ever came from the outline, so `Sequence`, `Course`, the entrance-exam\n  alert and `UnitNavigationEffortEstimate` read both queries. `CourseBreadcrumbs`\n  reads the outline once and indexes into it, replacing the `useModels` call\n  inside `.map()`. `UnitNavigationEffortEstimate` drops the `Object.keys`\n  guards #808 added for the `{}` sentinel.\n- `useSaveSequencePosition` writes `activeUnitIndex` into the cached sequence\n  at its exact key and snapshots the entry for rollback (the TanStack\n  optimistic-update shape); it drops\n  `useStore` / `useDispatch`.\n- The `sequences` selectors in `CoursewareContainer` and `redirects.ts` come\n  forward from D4: the bridge runs only from a fetch, so a store read of\n  `activeUnitIndex` would go stale once the writer moved. The redirect rules\n  take a full `SequenceMetadata`; their `unitIds !== undefined` guards, and\n  the fixtures for the store''s partial outline entry, go with the store.\n- Types come from #2129: `SequenceMetadata` from `courseware/data/sequenceMetadata`\n  and `MinimalCourseOutline` on `useMinimalCourseOutline`; this layer adds\n  none of its own.\n- Tests: the position suite asserts on the cache; the redirect suite builds\n  full fixtures; the `SequenceContent` suite renders behind the loaded\n  sequence as `Sequence` does; two container resume cases await the unit; a\n  new container case pins that each unit change saves the position and load\n  does not; another pins the first-section celebration record when next\n  leaves the first section. The breadcrumb suite''s section fixture passes\n  sequence ids, not objects, so its jump-nav rows are built. Negative check: with the position write disabled, exactly the two\n  hook cases that read the cached index fail.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''sequences'', id)` returns `{}`. The active\nsequence''s full shape is `useSequenceMetadata(sequenceId, { enabled: false })\n.data?.sequence`; any sequence''s `id`, `title` and `sectionId` are\n`useMinimalCourseOutline(courseId, { enabled: false }).data?.sequences[id]`,\nboth from `courseware/data/apiHooks`.\n\nPart of #1946. Closes #2088.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquqnICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/jMQAAszOsRBLCq9kbNb4kZCzG5i\n5YqbL7zyqDY/MrXmi6xJZIireZc02AWOAlKu/TVyl8uY75XSPVsIar0b1cXn7vyK\n1/Uv4kh3aG16KxErx7XFc0mMAREVcpw4fhl14O7rOMVw2NQ7VrQEG+LAy8CZk2Ax\njN1GI0//ARZJCY12ohGGWmI8duoDqt6I4bl5wZcrz5VL0ysKCRf9Gfn2TPw4/wAL\nzpAaKtLi3hZ8IorFFauNYmp3nh6iZ3AOYfe7Gov/tX4UdXFTiM1xo9dNR6FmZj1I\nsmtdeA/QPvZ2UsFZHb5OxUewksE5SBt8pCJIWvBwQIYmVA+b1hVOWJWXJ+twhS7l\nq4ijunfL1+hWC9je6BVZ81UzxNk+lDkimP4NybvBJ9t+jFRgqa5g7GliOY0pyNdY\nXB0W+qp+Lw9ENIB4r2ElORmNPXZKFxa1fVc4iQFQbZ+y9apDbCgNRtTJ9W5ynKbT\nWXbnEmECGlg+/luDRcJRPeMMGroOQ92rOjxW8wSb40VigW7sOcET2c1IAmwIexYo\nFF2GX2Hr/kfwMENzGw6Gc+PTrvZtJDuQ8cER6DImfnu0sCyjNf+LZenSnXUTfH4u\nZb4tPSOCLdHHzFVn2s+Fw0pHOV3NfFn2khmCism0gyLeDU58tdU0ERn3nFwBw6lV\n/HcR60ic0YARvsjUYOnc\n=wiWf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T17:54:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDc2ZmExZjA2YTdiNmYxODNkZjAxMDk0NDhlMDBlNTY2MDllOTQ3MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed","sha":"5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed"}],"sha":"76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/76fa1f06a7b6f183df0109448e00e56609e94711"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:01:58Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:01:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: type the courseware normalizers on the functions that produce them (#2131)\n\nConverts courseware/data/utils.js to TypeScript, one file per normalizer, and\ndeclares each normalizer''s input and output types on the function, moving\nCoursewareMeta, SequenceUnit, SequenceMetadata and SequenceMetadataData out of\napiHooks.ts to live beside the code that builds them. Part of the model-store\ndissolution (#1977).\n\n- One file per endpoint object, named after its top type, each holding the\n  output types, the input type and the normalizer, and each normalizer named\n  after its output type: coursewareMeta.ts exports normalizeCoursewareMeta\n  (/api/courseware/course/, was normalizeMetadata), sequenceMetadata.ts\n  exports normalizeSequenceMetadata (/api/courseware/sequence/),\n  minimalCourseOutline.ts exports normalizeMinimalCourseOutline\n  (/api/learning_sequences/v1/course_outline/, was\n  normalizeLearningSequencesData) and courseNavigationOutline.ts exports\n  normalizeCourseNavigationOutline (/api/course_home/v1/navigation/, was\n  normalizeOutlineBlocks; the file is the renamed courseOutline.ts and keeps\n  applyUnitCompletion).\n- Output types are named for the endpoint each models: SequenceMetadata /\n  SequenceUnit and CoursewareMeta keep their names; the navigation sidebar''s\n  tree is CourseNavigationOutline with CourseNavigationSection / Sequence /\n  Unit; the learning-sequences outline is MinimalCourseOutline with\n  MinimalCourseMetadata / MinimalSectionMetadata / MinimalSequenceMetadata,\n  named for what it keeps relative to SequenceMetadata.\n- useCoursewareOutline becomes useMinimalCourseOutline, matching its typed\n  result; nothing merged points plugins at the old name for its data.\n- Input types name the fields each normalizer reads, open-ended, with\n  nullability from the platform''s serializers; they are not exported.\n- CoursewareMeta names all thirty fields; the eight camel-cased sub-objects\n  stay unknown until a reader names their insides. SequenceMetadata follows\n  SequenceBlock.get_metadata: bannerText and format are nullable, gatedContent\n  is always present, allowProctoringOptOut is optional because the payload\n  never carries it. SequenceUnit.complete is optional, as the platform sends\n  it only for a signed-in user.\n- normalizeCourseNavigationOutline drops the never-read courseId parameter\n  its predecessor kept from the course-home copy it was based on; its four\n  callers pass only blocks.\n- The release filter''s clock is Date.now() so the comparison type-checks; the\n  comparison is unchanged.\n- api.js imports each normalizer from its file; the six importers of the\n  moved types repoint to them.\n\nPart of #1946. Closes #2129.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53304d3ec92450f4b336e7c895fcdd6f350116a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/53304d3ec92450f4b336e7c895fcdd6f350116a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed","verification":{"payload":"tree 53304d3ec92450f4b336e7c895fcdd6f350116a7\nparent 8c4af0c8ded1199e7df0f619677f0c4fed524d5f\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790607718 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790607718 -0400\n\nrefactor: type the courseware normalizers on the functions that produce them (#2131)\n\nConverts courseware/data/utils.js to TypeScript, one file per normalizer, and\ndeclares each normalizer''s input and output types on the function, moving\nCoursewareMeta, SequenceUnit, SequenceMetadata and SequenceMetadataData out of\napiHooks.ts to live beside the code that builds them. Part of the model-store\ndissolution (#1977).\n\n- One file per endpoint object, named after its top type, each holding the\n  output types, the input type and the normalizer, and each normalizer named\n  after its output type: coursewareMeta.ts exports normalizeCoursewareMeta\n  (/api/courseware/course/, was normalizeMetadata), sequenceMetadata.ts\n  exports normalizeSequenceMetadata (/api/courseware/sequence/),\n  minimalCourseOutline.ts exports normalizeMinimalCourseOutline\n  (/api/learning_sequences/v1/course_outline/, was\n  normalizeLearningSequencesData) and courseNavigationOutline.ts exports\n  normalizeCourseNavigationOutline (/api/course_home/v1/navigation/, was\n  normalizeOutlineBlocks; the file is the renamed courseOutline.ts and keeps\n  applyUnitCompletion).\n- Output types are named for the endpoint each models: SequenceMetadata /\n  SequenceUnit and CoursewareMeta keep their names; the navigation sidebar''s\n  tree is CourseNavigationOutline with CourseNavigationSection / Sequence /\n  Unit; the learning-sequences outline is MinimalCourseOutline with\n  MinimalCourseMetadata / MinimalSectionMetadata / MinimalSequenceMetadata,\n  named for what it keeps relative to SequenceMetadata.\n- useCoursewareOutline becomes useMinimalCourseOutline, matching its typed\n  result; nothing merged points plugins at the old name for its data.\n- Input types name the fields each normalizer reads, open-ended, with\n  nullability from the platform''s serializers; they are not exported.\n- CoursewareMeta names all thirty fields; the eight camel-cased sub-objects\n  stay unknown until a reader names their insides. SequenceMetadata follows\n  SequenceBlock.get_metadata: bannerText and format are nullable, gatedContent\n  is always present, allowProctoringOptOut is optional because the payload\n  never carries it. SequenceUnit.complete is optional, as the platform sends\n  it only for a signed-in user.\n- normalizeCourseNavigationOutline drops the never-read courseId parameter\n  its predecessor kept from the course-home copy it was based on; its four\n  callers pass only blocks.\n- The release filter''s clock is Date.now() so the comparison type-checks; the\n  comparison is unchanged.\n- api.js imports each normalizer from its file; the six importers of the\n  moved types repoint to them.\n\nPart of #1946. Closes #2129.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquoFnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlDUQAI7bGERyLJXTuoIqiMt+5lCz\nv8RmFfLVrPCfqLzlO3CEtV0LSve60CaPthH52lywEmbTmbeofGdeoSyfSAr0vEL0\nQ5Hl5adVzCJlHQGA9zf00/58bT4b/Gv26U7zGkdE5NDjRKQ/SJg6wJJT9ajrv5UN\nT9xE9kjO/3IptX+FK1X3Op9N2LRj+SvFzsCEyyXQlcPxQkQWMasgFLkJTGy0Ec7i\nHzr5k+JlNiowMZeiNwXwwxmxRD5AI54/9eNz+Fh0sZI7Xk8pa