ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/5cbac207debf05a53a3ce475db5a678e0dbd30ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/8c4af0c8ded1199e7df0f619677f0c4fed524d5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:55:51Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:55:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: read units from the sequence query, not useModel (#2128)\n\nLayer D1 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The six readers of the\n`units` model read the unit through `useUnit(sequenceId, unitId)`, a disabled\n`select` observer of the sequence query CoursewareContainer fetches; the\nbookmark and completion writers patch the cached sequence with `setQueryData`\nat its exact key; the query no longer writes the `units` model.\n\n- `useUnit(sequenceId, unitId)` in `courseware/data/apiHooks.ts`, the\n  `useDiscussionTopic` shape: never fetches, `undefined` for a unit not in the\n  sequence. `sequenceMetadataQuery(sequenceId, isPreview)` is the query''s\n  options builder; `useIsPreview()` is the one derivation of the key''s preview\n  flag; `updateSequenceUnit(queryClient, key, unitId, patch)` patches one unit\n  of a cached sequence. `SequenceUnit` names the normalizer''s fields.\n- Readers: `Sequence`, `SequenceContent`, `Unit`, `UnitSuspense`,\n  `useShouldDisplayHonorCode`, `UnitButton`. `SequenceContent` threads\n  `sequenceId` to `Unit`, which passes it on. `SequenceContent`''s\n  `!unit` guard is reachable again: a unit id that is not in the sequence\n  renders the no-content message (#98''s handling of deleted units, dead since\n  #808 made useModel return `{}` for a missing id).\n- Writers: `useSetBookmarked(sequenceId, unitId, bookmarked)` gains the\n  sequence id (`BookmarkButton` takes it as a prop, from `unit.sequenceId`);\n  `useCheckBlockCompletion` reads its already-complete guard from the cache;\n  the outline sidebar''s completion check names the active sequence, not the\n  clicked unit''s, so a cross-sequence click posts to the handler of the\n  sequence that contains the unit. Both hooks drop `useDispatch` / `useStore`.\n- Bridge: the `units` mirror leaves the sequence query''s `meta`;\n  `modelKeys.units` is gone.\n- Tests: suites that rendered readers against the seeded store mount the\n  container''s fetches beside the component and read the cached unit; the two\n  writer suites assert on the cache; `SidebarUnit.test` pins the active\n  sequence in the completion request. Negative check: with `useUnit` fetching,\n  exactly the hook''s fetches-nothing case and #2123''s request count fail.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''units'', unitId)` returns `{}`; read the unit with\n`useUnit(sequenceId, unitId).data` from `courseware/data/apiHooks`, which is\n`undefined` for a unit not in the sequence. `BookmarkButton` takes a required\n`sequenceId` prop. `UnitTitleSlot`''s `unit` (the same object in its\n`pluginProps`) gains `sequenceId`. A URL naming a unit that is not in its\nsequence renders \"There is no content here.\" instead of an iframe.\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2088.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a61a05561a50eb39d8d7c422ed9d8056b94097b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/a61a05561a50eb39d8d7c422ed9d8056b94097b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/8c4af0c8ded1199e7df0f619677f0c4fed524d5f","verification":{"payload":"tree a61a05561a50eb39d8d7c422ed9d8056b94097b5\nparent 12de1ec6fbf20df2dedd733a137e4cee320a6fc8\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790607351 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790607351 -0400\n\nrefactor!: read units from the sequence query, not useModel (#2128)\n\nLayer D1 of the model-store dissolution (#1977). The six readers of the\n`units` model read the unit through `useUnit(sequenceId, unitId)`, a disabled\n`select` observer of the sequence query CoursewareContainer fetches; the\nbookmark and completion writers patch the cached sequence with `setQueryData`\nat its exact key; the query no longer writes the `units` model.\n\n- `useUnit(sequenceId, unitId)` in `courseware/data/apiHooks.ts`, the\n  `useDiscussionTopic` shape: never fetches, `undefined` for a unit not in the\n  sequence. `sequenceMetadataQuery(sequenceId, isPreview)` is the query''s\n  options builder; `useIsPreview()` is the one derivation of the key''s preview\n  flag; `updateSequenceUnit(queryClient, key, unitId, patch)` patches one unit\n  of a cached sequence. `SequenceUnit` names the normalizer''s fields.\n- Readers: `Sequence`, `SequenceContent`, `Unit`, `UnitSuspense`,\n  `useShouldDisplayHonorCode`, `UnitButton`. `SequenceContent` threads\n  `sequenceId` to `Unit`, which passes it on. `SequenceContent`''s\n  `!unit` guard is reachable again: a unit id that is not in the sequence\n  renders the no-content message (#98''s handling of deleted units, dead since\n  #808 made useModel return `{}` for a missing id).\n- Writers: `useSetBookmarked(sequenceId, unitId, bookmarked)` gains the\n  sequence id (`BookmarkButton` takes it as a prop, from `unit.sequenceId`);\n  `useCheckBlockCompletion` reads its already-complete guard from the cache;\n  the outline sidebar''s completion check names the active sequence, not the\n  clicked unit''s, so a cross-sequence click posts to the handler of the\n  sequence that contains the unit. Both hooks drop `useDispatch` / `useStore`.\n- Bridge: the `units` mirror leaves the sequence query''s `meta`;\n  `modelKeys.units` is gone.\n- Tests: suites that rendered readers against the seeded store mount the\n  container''s fetches beside the component and read the cached unit; the two\n  writer suites assert on the cache; `SidebarUnit.test` pins the active\n  sequence in the completion request. Negative check: with `useUnit` fetching,\n  exactly the hook''s fetches-nothing case and #2123''s request count fail.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''units'', unitId)` returns `{}`; read the unit with\n`useUnit(sequenceId, unitId).data` from `courseware/data/apiHooks`, which is\n`undefined` for a unit not in the sequence. `BookmarkButton` takes a required\n`sequenceId` prop. `UnitTitleSlot`''s `unit` (the same object in its\n`pluginProps`) gains `sequenceId`. A URL naming a unit that is not in its\nsequence renders \"There is no content here.\" instead of an iframe.\n\nPart of #1946. Part of #2088.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqun/3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWu4QABUdgxQOrqEIXP/TQCNtFgQe\n40futBhNdCbNG27TUq8Tr6WQqU/RrtiWlDa0ymanFk5LWPIbo4gSIHlYrYmGWZVm\ns+W6nkhzjoVpG4ZxVQs/8meys5Rr6O3jL8wItjWq/xoaj+TcTkihkiZIhubNvxV/\niv