arents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0","sha":"61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0"}],"sha":"66a9be40f30e4e9d957a579c811cc98bba5d3e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/66a9be40f30e4e9d957a579c811cc98bba5d3e1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:55:59Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:55:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: read courseHomeMeta from the query in the courseware, course-end pages and widgets (#2110)\n\nThe course-home metadata has been query-backed since #2010, and #2085 moved\nits tab-page, alert and course-home-tab readers onto the query. This moves the\nremaining 22 reads the same way: the courseware subtree, the course-end pages,\nthe sidebar provider and upgrade widget, the product tours and the streak\nmodal read `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data ?? {}` where\nthey destructure, `.data?.field` for a single field, and `.data` alone where\nthe whole object feeds a memo. Every site renders under a page that already\nfetches the query, so nothing fetches differently.\n\nThe two celebration writers marked a celebration as shown by dispatching\n`updateModel` into the store; they now write the query''s cache entry with\n`queryClient.setQueryData`, spreading the same `celebrations` they spread\nbefore, and `useQueryClient()` replaces `useDispatch()` in `Course`, the\nfirst-section modal and the streak modal. The server-side celebration POST is\nunchanged and stays outside React Query; #1973 owns making it a mutation. The\nthree tab readers in this set take the tab-URL hooks from #2085, and\n`HiddenAfterDue` drops its `courseId` prop in favour of the route param.\n\nWith no reader or writer left on the store, `useCourseHomeMeta` drops its\nbridge `meta` entry, so nothing writes the `courseHomeMeta` model any more.\nThe sidebar README''s \"Accessing Course Data\" section is rewritten around the\nquery hooks so it no longer suggests `useModel` returns this data.\n\nTests: suites that rendered these components against the seeded store mount\nthe owner''s query hooks beside them (`Course`, `Sequence`, `LockPaywall`, the\n`CourseExit` bodies) or, where the suite''s own axios adapter precludes a\nfetch, seed the query (`HonorCode`, the streak modal); `UpgradePanel` and\n`SidebarContextProvider` mock the hook instead of `useModel`. The celebration\nutils are tested against a real query cache, the streak modal suite covers the\nclose-time cache write, and a new `CelebrationModal` suite covers the\nfirst-section modal''s open-time POST and cache write, which no unskipped test\nexercised.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''courseHomeMeta'', courseId)` from\n./src/generic/model-store no longer returns the course-home metadata; it\nreturns `{}`. Read `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data` from\n./src/course-home/data/apiHooks instead. Under any course page it returns what\nthat page fetched; see src/courseware/course/sidebar/README.md.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2086.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c8aca4371652fa05649409bc9fd84e0b2665df5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/8c8aca4371652fa05649409bc9fd84e0b2665df5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c8aca4371652fa05649409bc9fd84e0b2665df5\nparent ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790218559 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790218559 -0400\n\nrefactor!: read courseHomeMeta from the query in the courseware, course-end pages and widgets (#2110)\n\nThe course-home metadata has been query-backed since #2010, and #2085 moved\nits tab-page, alert and course-home-tab readers onto the query. This moves the\nremaining 22 reads the same way: the courseware subtree, the course-end pages,\nthe sidebar provider and upgrade widget, the product tours and the streak\nmodal read `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data ?? {}` where\nthey destructure, `.data?.field` for a single field, and `.data` alone where\nthe whole object feeds a memo. Every site renders under a page that already\nfetches the query, so nothing fetches differently.\n\nThe two celebration writers marked a celebration as shown by dispatching\n`updateModel` into the store; they now write the query''s cache entry with\n`queryClient.setQueryData`, spreading the same `celebrations` they spread\nbefore, and `useQueryClient()` replaces `useDispatch()` in `Course`, the\nfirst-section modal and the streak modal. The server-side celebration POST is\nunchanged and stays outside React Query; #1973 owns making it a mutation. The\nthree tab readers in this set take the tab-URL hooks from #2085, and\n`HiddenAfterDue` drops its `courseId` prop in favour of the route param.\n\nWith no reader or writer left on the store, `useCourseHomeMeta` drops its\nbridge `meta` entry, so nothing writes the `courseHomeMeta` model any more.\nThe sidebar README''s \"Accessing Course Data\" section is rewritten around the\nquery hooks so it no longer suggests `useModel` returns this data.\n\nTests: suites that rendered these components against the seeded store mount\nthe owner''s query hooks beside them (`Course`, `Sequence`, `LockPaywall`, the\n`CourseExit` bodies) or, where the suite''s own axios adapter precludes a\nfetch, seed the query (`HonorCode`, the streak modal); `UpgradePanel` and\n`SidebarContextProvider` mock the hook instead of `useModel`. The celebration\nutils are tested against a real query cache, the streak modal suite covers the\nclose-time cache write, and a new `CelebrationModal` suite covers the\nfirst-section modal''s open-time POST and cache write, which no unskipped test\nexercised.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useModel(''courseHomeMeta'', courseId)` from\n./src/generic/model-store no longer returns the course-home metadata; it\nreturns `{}`. Read `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data` from\n./src/course-home/data/apiHooks instead. Under any course page it returns what\nthat page fetched; see src/courseware/course/sidebar/README.md.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2086.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtJE/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbPQQAFeQiGca1ZzbvRuZlKgDRGTY\n93