4bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38","sha":"ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38"}],"sha":"61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/61e0bd96abdde6666f198aa70abf67b0275ef1e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:50:42Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:50:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: read courseHomeMeta from the query in the tab page, alerts and course-home tabs (#2109)\n\nThe course-home metadata has been query-backed since #2010, but its readers\nstill went through the model store the bridge mirrors it into. The 31 reads in\nthe tab page, the alerts and the course-home tabs now take the query result\ndirectly, as disabled observers under the page that fetches it, so nothing\nfetches differently: `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data ?? {}`\nwhere the reader destructures, `.data` alone where the whole object feeds a\n`useMemo`, and the query already in hand in `TabPage` and `DatesTab`.\n\n`useCourseHomeMeta` gains a `CourseHomeMeta` type naming the fields the\nTypeScript readers need, with an index signature for plugins. `LoadedTabPage`\nrenders only after the owner''s query settled, so it narrows on `isSuccess` and\nthrows otherwise, the way the React Query docs describe making `data` defined;\n`TabPage` renders its header while pending and keeps a `Partial` default.\n\nThree tab-URL hooks (`useCourseOutlineUrl`, `useDatesTabUrl`,\n`useProgressTabUrl`) wrap the B1 accessors so `RelatedLinks`, `DetailedGrades`\nand `CertificateStatusAlert` stop handling a `tabs` array; `tabs` leaves the\ncertificate alert''s payload.\n\nEvery page that owns the query gains a once-per-load request-count case, so a\nreader that forgets the option fails that page''s suite. The bridge entry stays\nuntil B3 (#2086), which takes the remaining 22 reads and the celebration\nwriters.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2085.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85be5bb672daba86b85d635d8b89d159e6b54580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/85be5bb672daba86b85d635d8b89d159e6b54580"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38","verification":{"payload":"tree 85be5bb672daba86b85d635d8b89d159e6b54580\nparent 68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790218242 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790218242 -0400\n\nrefactor: read courseHomeMeta from the query in the tab page, alerts and course-home tabs (#2109)\n\nThe course-home metadata has been query-backed since #2010, but its readers\nstill went through the model store the bridge mirrors it into. The 31 reads in\nthe tab page, the alerts and the course-home tabs now take the query result\ndirectly, as disabled observers under the page that fetches it, so nothing\nfetches differently: `useCourseHomeMeta(courseId, { enabled: false }).data ?? {}`\nwhere the reader destructures, `.data` alone where the whole object feeds a\n`useMemo`, and the query already in hand in `TabPage` and `DatesTab`.\n\n`useCourseHomeMeta` gains a `CourseHomeMeta` type naming the fields the\nTypeScript readers need, with an index signature for plugins. `LoadedTabPage`\nrenders only after the owner''s query settled, so it narrows on `isSuccess` and\nthrows otherwise, the way the React Query docs describe making `data` defined;\n`TabPage` renders its header while pending and keeps a `Partial` default.\n\nThree tab-URL hooks (`useCourseOutlineUrl`, `useDatesTabUrl`,\n`useProgressTabUrl`) wrap the B1 accessors so `RelatedLinks`, `DetailedGrades`\nand `CertificateStatusAlert` stop handling a `tabs` array; `tabs` leaves the\ncertificate alert''s payload.\n\nEvery page that owns the query gains a once-per-load request-count case, so a\nreader that forgets the option fails that page''s suite. The bridge entry stays\nuntil B3 (#2086), which takes the remaining 22 reads and the celebration\nwriters.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2085.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtJACCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/6gQAKSACiZ4NEyM55dugGe0a5rT\nTvXulFQHDldT6Lr1fIbxuSBUnW3MeW8/Ge/iLjfNyOoNyD0aEYxTBUzsgQHuFDW3\n8Hnw/mSeYVWgsYZbA+bfEMWRHhT0Fcqv0dbEPIBj+nBpwk46Key2tRbZxx8ia7Js\n4+qsC06Wl3u9rfrwfiisNQsmmfAGkd73jtepUmY9LW5y74J1FDgr45D4sbC2EeSA\nOIWWfi46wQJ6CdC1v6t4Ofzje1mV6Ajkd7hjokNAQPt2ugsBjY8oa5Xo4avSY6+b\nNcoU4wD5wzH0I8PjS1st0jK9+4y3w48Dh5IbJQMArZcf1S/ITunEezx+X89VW1Ec\nNsheI02AawWjnj3yFjj+JvoQKpjVXmB02U0zQ6SQ0/e+jQaXEJabxcMR3pJo/xOn\nzg+4bZyGOqJW+W/8l8I0ot6RohuZ/HHeRTH1PS25CGJJheAmg+KWkm5u15EX9kWn\nhuDcARrkQoWEAb4kDG9PgOW3Kzdymej0yUn7YOUngem/ij96Z6vriPgv4hWkyz5t\n6OMFVzZYi0CM0GsSgtZ9H7evEFZMdJCEOl/SOSEx2Hd5Sq38yBerqAmbGvIoqQTE\n8tlwb/8LDMR2r+BqdWX7iQL3vc0Yo8y7pvWgSdNwFGcftS5GsrZA0M1aVwU9OS4f\nNUFw+bxoSclrGQbuUNyz\n=p6rS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T02:50:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKGFlMzY3YTY2MjRiYzliMzE4ZGFmODQ4ZDM1NjNlZWNjMmQ1NmZlMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc","sha":"68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc"}],"sha":"ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/ae367a6624bc9b318daf848d3563eecc2d56fe38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:03:58Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:03:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: make the LoadedTabPage streak test actually assert (#2108)\n\nThe *shows streak celebration modal* case could not fail. Its `StreakModal`\nmock rendered a bare div whatever its props, and `LoadedTabPage` always\nrenders `StreakModal`, open or closed, so \"the mock is in the document\" was\ntrue on every render. Its fixture also set `celebrations` on the courseware\nmetadata factory, while `LoadedTabPage` has read `celebrations` from\n`courseHomeMeta` since AA-1018; the test store builds that from a separate\nfactory with `celebrations: null`, so the streak never reached the component.\nRemoving `celebrations` from the fixture left the test green.\n\nThe fixture now goes on the `courseHomeMetadata` factory, through the\n`initializeTestStore` option the suite''s staff case already uses, and the\nmodal is no longer mocked: closed it renders nothing, open it renders a\ndialog titled with the streak length, so the case asserts a dialog reading\n\"3 day streak\" is on the page and *renders correctly* asserts there is no\ndialog on the default fixture. Removing `celebrations` from the fixture now\nfails the streak case, and forcing the modal open in the component fails the\ncontrast. The component is unchanged.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2107.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65a758f4e3a93ad8a24c23b3e9202f15c9637cd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/65a758f4e3a93ad8a24c23b3e9202f15c9637cd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 65a758f4e3a93ad8a24c23b3e9202f15c9637cd3\nparent 8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790183038 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790183038 -0400\n\ntest: make the LoadedTabPage streak test actually assert (#2108)\n\nThe *shows streak celebration modal* case could not fail. Its `StreakModal`\nmock rendered a bare div whatever its props, and `LoadedTabPage` always\nrenders `StreakModal`, open or closed, so \"the mock is in the document\" was\ntrue on every render. Its fixture also set `celebrations` on the courseware\nmetadata factory, while `LoadedTabPage` has read `celebrations` from\n`courseHomeMeta` since AA-1018; the test store builds that from a separate\nfactory with `celebrations: null`, so the streak never reached the component.\nRemoving `celebrations` from the fixture left the test green.\n\nThe fixture now goes on the `courseHomeMetadata` factory, through the\n`initializeTestStore` option the suite''s staff case already uses, and the\nmodal is no longer mocked: closed it renders nothing, open it renders a\ndialog titled with the streak length, so the case asserts a dialog reading\n\"3 day streak\" is on the page and *renders correctly* asserts there is no\ndialog on the default fixture. Removing `celebrations` from the fixture now\nfails the streak case, and forcing the modal open in the component fails the\ncontrast. The component is unchanged.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2107.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtAZ+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa60QAKKnHjqhI5tSmpTUQ37Wk6mn\n/YyruIhhIRcEh3yLnRrJYodn58HbYN5aDZsxuukJEfm91FoKy4p5umwBojJsLGoQ\nw8VNIO9WkH4sr4cj/fTD4WZCPNbG7aFJNCbLBa/71xVemXuT7Rdhm2r5AP7sqhaf\nYTdEuV3lDPE3d/UCBP65t2ELhTkhSQG4njKOf6X4qIYrrbt0+xBBpG2noijfViNP\nZnHc2nr7cv2XzQwkvY7bO+OleSYRmgrsnc4Jwaww3LadLrS/ZfpzKrHVGVYjBHyk\nEo32LxZwIYxoMfFds4MI+0aICxQBbC6rQpjxQZlboAj9zSnN9BWz3IAKHeyLL+5K\nk3MpSj+yozWplR0pCrlc8rQM/X/tCRvR+j3ZsMI9o/ZtI9DVYUpjWcPZLIQaVWe5\nPx1HnEx9jCogAAvvcFHpZMBr5DMvTAgotwq6NafPhvgc0X+UZ6OFfW9Dgkx9M9oq\nb7k07tpxJzjF4dRW/5F0PQsFsX5e+GS0cPyFctPin5vl8IlyT/zpJJPpznyhtJYy\ninUasNNDP6hrTqBtDNBsstRNr/MwqkXT6tmas+fxkG4H4sp1HemKPjPLquOleWV+\nXkgR+IDGBDKuPN8i1fYI69x9Zt59HcIKhEmwnLec9t6M4dtQQeZ/w1jhi6znsZmh\nSFBYOW6vezQ4obv0a1ut\n=2afG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T17:03:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDY4Yzc2MDgxNTI0YmI4NWM2OWYwMDViOTM4NjU1ZGYzYTg5MGI1ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae","sha":"8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae"}],"sha":"68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/68c76081524bb85c69f005b938655df3a890b5fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:11:18Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:11:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: stop the progress tab data refetching from components under the tab (#2106)\n\nOne load of the progress tab requested `/api/course_home/progress/` twice.\n`ProgressTab` fetches it and gates on it, and every component under the gate\nreads it through `useProgressData()`, which was a fetching observer of the\nsame query: 22 call sites, 21 files under `course-home/progress-tab/` plus\nthe grade-breakdown slot. They mount in one commit after the data has landed,\nfind it stale at the default `staleTime` of 0, and refetch. React Query\ndedupes them against each other, which is why the count was two and not\ntwenty-two, but not against the owner''s already-settled fetch.\n\nThis is the defect #2083 fixed on the outline and dates tabs and #2098 fixed\non the courseware gate, and it gets the same fix: the owner fetches, the\nreaders under it subscribe without fetching. `useProgressTabData` takes the\ncourse-home `{ enabled }` option, and `useProgressData()` passes\n`{ enabled: false }`; it takes no option of its own, since every caller\nrenders under `ProgressTab`, which fetches the same key from the same route\nparams. A disabled observer returns the query''s current state and re-renders\nwhen the owner''s fetch lands, so every reader sees the same value as before.\n`ProgressTab` keeps fetching.\n\nA `staleTime` would have hidden the reader fetches without deciding who owns\nthem, and would have changed the owner''s freshness too: the progress payload\nchanges server-side with no app action, and `useRequestCert`, which renders\nunder this tab, relies on refetch-on-mount to resync.\n\n`useExamsData()`, the plugin-facing hook in the same module, reads through\n`useProgressData()` and inherits the change. Its documented use, a widget in\na progress-tab slot, renders under `ProgressTab` and returns exactly what it\ndid; the README now says so, and says how a widget outside the tab fetches\nthe data itself. #2104, the layer below, moved the progress query''s 404\nredirect out of the `queryFn` so that fetch has no side effect.\n\nTests: a disabled case for `useProgressTabData`; a `useProgressData` describe\nwith the two cases `useIsCourseLoaded` has (fetches nothing on its own; reads\nthe owner''s result without fetching again), sharing the route wrapper with\nthe `useExamsData` cases; and a request count in `ProgressTab.test.jsx` that\nwaits for the client to go idle and then counts one progress request (two\nbefore this change).\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useExamsData` and `useProgressData`\n(./src/course-home/progress-tab/hooks) no longer fetch the progress data\nthemselves; they read what `ProgressTab` has fetched. In a progress-tab slot,\nthe documented use, they return exactly what they did. Rendered anywhere else\nthey now return null / undefined unless something rendered on the page\nfetches the progress data — for example, a widget calling\n`useProgressTabData(courseId)` from ./src/course-home/data/apiHooks; see\nsrc/course-home/progress-tab/README.md.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2103.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b77ad28fce9f0b3e1e1b40ccd6fc9c0a4647876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/4b77ad28fce9f0b3e1e1b40ccd6fc9c0a4647876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b77ad28fce9f0b3e1e1b40ccd6fc9c0a4647876\nparent 2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790172678 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790172678 -0400\n\nrefactor!: stop the progress tab data refetching from components under the tab (#2106)\n\nOne load of the progress tab requested `/api/course_home/progress/` twice.\n`ProgressTab` fetches it and gates on it, and every component under the gate\nreads it through `useProgressData()`, which was a fetching observer of the\nsame query: 22 call sites, 21 files under `course-home/progress-tab/` plus\nthe grade-breakdown slot. They mount in one commit after the data has landed,\nfind it stale at the default `staleTime` of 0, and refetch. React Query\ndedupes them against each other, which is why the count was two and not\ntwenty-two, but not against the owner''s already-settled fetch.\n\nThis is the defect #2083 fixed on the outline and dates tabs and #2098 fixed\non the courseware gate, and it gets the same fix: the owner fetches, the\nreaders under it subscribe without fetching. `useProgressTabData` takes the\ncourse-home `{ enabled }` option, and `useProgressData()` passes\n`{ enabled: false }`; it takes no option of its own, since every caller\nrenders under `ProgressTab`, which fetches the same key from the same route\nparams. A disabled observer returns the query''s current state and re-renders\nwhen the owner''s fetch lands, so every reader sees the same value as before.\n`ProgressTab` keeps fetching.\n\nA `staleTime` would have hidden the reader fetches without deciding who owns\nthem, and would have changed the owner''s freshness too: the progress payload\nchanges server-side with no app action, and `useRequestCert`, which renders\nunder this tab, relies on refetch-on-mount to resync.\n\n`useExamsData()`, the plugin-facing hook in the same module, reads through\n`useProgressData()` and inherits the change. Its documented use, a widget in\na progress-tab slot, renders under `ProgressTab` and returns exactly what it\ndid; the README now says so, and says how a widget outside the tab fetches\nthe data itself. #2104, the layer below, moved the progress query''s 404\nredirect out of the `queryFn` so that fetch has no side effect.\n\nTests: a disabled case for `useProgressTabData`; a `useProgressData` describe\nwith the two cases `useIsCourseLoaded` has (fetches nothing on its own; reads\nthe owner''s result without fetching again), sharing the route wrapper with\nthe `useExamsData` cases; and a request count in `ProgressTab.test.jsx` that\nwaits for the client to go idle and then counts one progress request (two\nbefore this change).\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `useExamsData` and `useProgressData`\n(./src/course-home/progress-tab/hooks) no longer fetch the progress data\nthemselves; they read what `ProgressTab` has fetched. In a progress-tab slot,\nthe documented use, they return exactly what they did. Rendered anywhere else\nthey now return null / undefined unless something rendered on the page\nfetches the progress data — for example, a widget calling\n`useProgressTabData(courseId)` from ./src/course-home/data/apiHooks; see\nsrc/course-home/progress-tab/README.md.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2103.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs94GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQIEQABxrxmLdZsQem74QcU7N/BDe\nd5kcaydY/163gTgfq4W+IG3xSVMPIbkGEh92Ie8T+ncNyT2x0fZK/j+MIDJf0EGu\n9A3i2t997YlVDf9tN9jDNXKa0Qz4HbhpSFEXaaa82tEM1It3Cq0ONwqqP8s1v6Kz\n3umKflk2uWsjyShHWCDEgJ3kKWiBwLNNrG1KjaEOndFQRUG7FQfBg7/t0B0tJtiI\nnV/hrEclvW0lftdGmxq174IksVUy2Rwrg6/dfYlmaUozhMiRuZfIDvFVKYelBo/x\nLq4WMOdGdpJ6hE+XPPVBaMFkjWrezJa/c7iBm5FFydIx5NvRmMQoL4r3ymg5rS0e\nXJvcgHhY+Qu8tAThH4iesjvBOt0emwSg2lKMUcuxDvnc/QJu+nrHYyV88WAO5nTb\npd1Nt0+c0u8Qn+FHjohcZizpv81swFEon7rB5Z5o/9vjzdvCcsgox2ECHPaReUgs\nlMCuqkRdto09MxAe3fQl3cJIkjCZ82NeIhtKGsUDhZgdM1EPWFhwxn7aoY9Q0lJI\na4SkhPbLiqlzEV7weBlQzFxyew2Wr/Z5vxhMbo+HJnYUF6+Jmgp4aw/jobAKzPkt\nvNxZBQ/v/C85MePNqA6S8NBKNn6qm7hNHDE4Ywh2KZ0qj9/a2GstzGnL2TGAlBcQ\nOH5UES/gMpkmZ/bglLQq\n=NOgx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:11:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDhmZmE1ZmUzOTVjYTQ5NTc3NWIxM2JkMjMyNzViZGNiYjk3NGQwYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a","sha":"2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a"}],"sha":"8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/8ffa5fe395ca495775b13bd23275bdcbb974d0ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:04:54Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:04:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: move the progress tab''s legacy-page redirect out of the query and into ProgressTab (#2105)\n\n`getProgressTabData`, the `queryFn` of `useProgressTabData`, answered a 404\nfrom `/api/course_home/progress/` by calling `location.replace` to the LMS''s\nlegacy progress page and resolving to `{}`. The destination is right: the\nendpoint 404s when the MFE progress tab is not active for the course (the\n`course_home.course_home_mfe_progress_tab` course flag, an Old Mongo course,\nor `DisableProgressPageStackedConfig`), and the legacy view is the page that\nworks there. But the redirect sat inside the query, so anything that fetched\nthe query navigated the whole page, not just the progress tab. A plugin\nwidget calling `useExamsData()` from a slot on another tab fetched through it\nand, on such a course, bounced the learner off the outline to the legacy\nprogress page.\n\nThe side effect belongs to the fetch''s owner. `getProgressTabData` now lets\nthe 404 propagate like every other unhandled status; the 401 and 403\nbranches, which resolve to `{}` because access is decided from the metadata\nrequest, are unchanged. `ProgressTab`, the component that fetches this query,\nreads the status off `tabDataQuery.error`, calls `location.replace` from an\neffect, and renders `PageLoading` while the browser navigates, announcing\n`TabPage`''s existing loading message. Rendering `TabWithTimer` instead would\nhave shown `TabPage`''s error view (\"There was an error loading this course.\")\nuntil the legacy page, which computes grades, finished loading. Any other\nfetcher of the progress query now reads an error and stays on its page. The\nredirect still fires on every 404, as before: the endpoint''s two 404 causes\n(tab disabled; bad or unauthorized `student_id`) are indistinguishable from\nthe response, and this change is about where the redirect lives, not when.\n\nLetting the 404 throw has one new consequence: the global `QueryCache`\n`onError` would log it as an error. Before this change the 404 was not logged\nat all, since the query succeeded, so the hook declares\n`logStatusAs: { 404: ''silent'' }` to keep it that way, through the mechanism\nthe courseware outline query uses for its expected 403. Retries already skip\n4xx.\n\nThe hook''s 404 test now asserts the query errors without navigating, and\n`ProgressTab.test.jsx` gains the redirect case; its `fetchAndRender` took a\n`waitForLoaded` option because the loading indicator it normally waits out is\nthe expected view here.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2104.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adbd70c04a6d6bdcf9b2aeb4cf5557521b63a908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/adbd70c04a6d6bdcf9b2aeb4cf5557521b63a908"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a","verification":{"payload":"tree adbd70c04a6d6bdcf9b2aeb4cf5557521b63a908\nparent 20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790172294 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790172294 -0400\n\nrefactor: move the progress tab''s legacy-page redirect out of the query and into ProgressTab (#2105)\n\n`getProgressTabData`, the `queryFn` of `useProgressTabData`, answered a 404\nfrom `/api/course_home/progress/` by calling `location.replace` to the LMS''s\nlegacy progress page and resolving to `{}`. The destination is right: the\nendpoint 404s when the MFE progress tab is not active for the course (the\n`course_home.course_home_mfe_progress_tab` course flag, an Old Mongo course,\nor `DisableProgressPageStackedConfig`), and the legacy view is the page that\nworks there. But the redirect sat inside the query, so anything that fetched\nthe query navigated the whole page, not just the progress tab. A plugin\nwidget calling `useExamsData()` from a slot on another tab fetched through it\nand, on such a course, bounced the learner off the outline to the legacy\nprogress page.\n\nThe side effect belongs to the fetch''s owner. `getProgressTabData` now lets\nthe 404 propagate like every other unhandled status; the 401 and 403\nbranches, which resolve to `{}` because access is decided from the metadata\nrequest, are unchanged. `ProgressTab`, the component that fetches this query,\nreads the status off `tabDataQuery.error`, calls `location.replace` from an\neffect, and renders `PageLoading` while the browser navigates, announcing\n`TabPage`''s existing loading message. Rendering `TabWithTimer` instead would\nhave shown `TabPage`''s error view (\"There was an error loading this course.\")\nuntil the legacy page, which computes grades, finished loading. Any other\nfetcher of the progress query now reads an error and stays on its page. The\nredirect still fires on every 404, as before: the endpoint''s two 404 causes\n(tab disabled; bad or unauthorized `student_id`) are indistinguishable from\nthe response, and this change is about where the redirect lives, not when.\n\nLetting the 404 throw has one new consequence: the global `QueryCache`\n`onError` would log it as an error. Before this change the 404 was not logged\nat all, since the query succeeded, so the hook declares\n`logStatusAs: { 404: ''silent'' }` to keep it that way, through the mechanism\nthe courseware outline query uses for its expected 403. Retries already skip\n4xx.\n\nThe hook''s 404 test now asserts the query errors without navigating, and\n`ProgressTab.test.jsx` gains the redirect case; its `fetchAndRender` took a\n`waitForLoaded` option because the loading indicator it normally waits out is\nthe expected view here.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2104.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9yGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQckQAKxe9BUWIAInjJiAx1ICA3Re\nC6KLZIezXr/W0LqZXasHSjgjs6GX05P6yd1BxqQVM2uGuJh9guvz2adjDSXQeZYg\n9CnAp0gr2zz9vZB1Zc5ybnDuHjHXtK6RhnIlyEnDaXG/K1x2gqT4P2oVVjoLy83k\n89YQPrOoMqiPMFCUKFMOvs8xXpi8et7WnT233v4OwjDuA/D3kgV1D2cL+b6GWrYA\ngRtymnfZ9R93UkDh0UoKFHDLTzpHw6AtQRHV8DJ/PyqrP/NGWmytcvwSOn/s49NA\nyo/nKs2Ho3iMmw8akoLiB3DUygo07CXss43vVQpHnG99C1jOLDyLRJ1Q7UTuZK/f\n5jitv0dkz36mhOZSyy+xU/FJU6Ixevd3SfHGouHkIZbqoK2GfMZUE5TNZZ5f9f44\n15QQaAybYCq/pgFJnlLhPLM3XEyuZWEtoWVc+t7wqhXqK31xYgiFSxa1CsGC/ilF\nT6aQakNVRAC3tB8hiMDP72W90PjkNxbcePiS8j1DE3mkGR8tB8V1xBg1VY1/gPwW\nLCOPXVNW+77RG4JNN6ebC2YouSpwwbPcoZ2bup20tqwkiuI5g/HhdZxt3B7CAqri\nveGnzupk5zuZyfJmOtKmNVY/1BvJP9TLyiE9GL1s4P2+L01x2fA2jg90u9YdmsGb\nCUPds+UkYhiHK674OItO\n=enSM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:04:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDJiYzM3YzFmZDRiOTkyOTgyMmZkZjI4NzRhYTMxNTVhYzM1MWE0MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d","sha":"20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d"}],"sha":"2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/2bc37c1fd4b9929822fdf2874aa3155ac351a40a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:44:11Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:44:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: stop the courseware gate queries refetching from components under the gate (#2102)\n\nOne outline-to-courseware navigation requested\n`/api/course_home/course_metadata/`, `/api/courseware/course/` and\n`/api/learning_sequences/v1/course_outline/` three times each: exactly the\nthree queries `useIsCourseLoaded` observes. `CoursewareContainer` fetches them\nonce. Its own calls, including the one inside `useCoursewareRedirects`, mount in\none render and dedupe. The other two requests came from `UnitNavigation` and\n`UnitNavigationEffortEstimate`, both through `useSequenceIds` →\n`useIsCourseLoaded`. That hook is a gate check, but it was also a fetching\nobserver of all three queries, called from components that render only once\nthe gate is open, so each one mounted on data that had just landed, found it\nstale at the default `staleTime` of 0, and refetched. `CourseBreadcrumbs` and\n`useSequenceNavigationMetadata` call it directly too. They happened to be\ndeduped against a fetch already in flight, which is why the count depended on\nmount timing rather than on structure.\n\nThis is the defect #2083 fixed on the course-home tabs, and it gets the same\nfix: the owner fetches, and the readers under it subscribe to the cache entry\nwithout fetching. Here no caller of `useIsCourseLoaded` needs it to fetch. Its\ntwo default callers, `useCoursewareRedirects` and `CoursewareContainer` itself\n(through `useSequenceIds`), run inside a render that already calls the three\nquery hooks directly. So `useIsCourseLoaded` never fetches, passing\n`{ enabled: false }` to `useCourseHomeMeta`, `useCoursewareMetadata` and\n`useCoursewareOutline`, which take that option now. `useSequenceIds` has no\nquery of its own, so it follows with no change of its own, and the gated call\nsites are untouched. A disabled observer returns the query''s current state and\nre-renders when the owner''s fetch lands, so every caller reads the same value\nas before, and invalidation still refetches through the owner''s observers.\n\nA `staleTime` would have hidden the extra fetches without deciding who owns\nthem, and would also have delayed the owner''s refetch on navigation, which\n`course_metadata` uses to record the learner''s daily streak.\n\nThe courseware hooks module declares its own `QueryOptions`, matching the\ncourse-home one, since `src/` has no shared module for it to live in. Tests\nthat render a gated component, or the gate hooks, without `CoursewareContainer`\nnow mount its query hooks themselves: component suites render\n`MountCourseQueryHooks`, a new test helper in `src/tests/`, and the hook tests\ncall the three query hooks alongside the gate hook.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2098.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"693bc02b9fdfe23d33569b7f1bfb01332f45b719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/693bc02b9fdfe23d33569b7f1bfb01332f45b719"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d","verification":{"payload":"tree 693bc02b9fdfe23d33569b7f1bfb01332f45b719\nparent 236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790163851 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790163851 -0400\n\nrefactor: stop the courseware gate queries refetching from components under the gate (#2102)\n\nOne outline-to-courseware navigation requested\n`/api/course_home/course_metadata/`, `/api/courseware/course/` and\n`/api/learning_sequences/v1/course_outline/` three times each: exactly the\nthree queries `useIsCourseLoaded` observes. `CoursewareContainer` fetches them\nonce. Its own calls, including the one inside `useCoursewareRedirects`, mount in\none render and dedupe. The other two requests came from `UnitNavigation` and\n`UnitNavigationEffortEstimate`, both through `useSequenceIds` →\n`useIsCourseLoaded`. That hook is a gate check, but it was also a fetching\nobserver of all three queries, called from components that render only once\nthe gate is open, so each one mounted on data that had just landed, found it\nstale at the default `staleTime` of 0, and refetched. `CourseBreadcrumbs` and\n`useSequenceNavigationMetadata` call it directly too. They happened to be\ndeduped against a fetch already in flight, which is why the count depended on\nmount timing rather than on structure.\n\nThis is the defect #2083 fixed on the course-home tabs, and it gets the same\nfix: the owner fetches, and the readers under it subscribe to the cache entry\nwithout fetching. Here no caller of `useIsCourseLoaded` needs it to fetch. Its\ntwo default callers, `useCoursewareRedirects` and `CoursewareContainer` itself\n(through `useSequenceIds`), run inside a render that already calls the three\nquery hooks directly. So `useIsCourseLoaded` never fetches, passing\n`{ enabled: false }` to `useCourseHomeMeta`, `useCoursewareMetadata` and\n`useCoursewareOutline`, which take that option now. `useSequenceIds` has no\nquery of its own, so it follows with no change of its own, and the gated call\nsites are untouched. A disabled observer returns the query''s current state and\nre-renders when the owner''s fetch lands, so every caller reads the same value\nas before, and invalidation still refetches through the owner''s observers.\n\nA `staleTime` would have hidden the extra fetches without deciding who owns\nthem, and would also have delayed the owner''s refetch on navigation, which\n`course_metadata` uses to record the learner''s daily streak.\n\nThe courseware hooks module declares its own `QueryOptions`, matching the\ncourse-home one, since `src/` has no shared module for it to live in. Tests\nthat render a gated component, or the gate hooks, without `CoursewareContainer`\nnow mount its query hooks themselves: component suites render\n`MountCourseQueryHooks`, a new test helper in `src/tests/`, and the hook tests\ncall the three query hooks alongside the gate hook.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2098.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs7uLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2hMQADg89a1ec7CerJkABNqMvBCy\nUlr7Kkb74i7ygoYqjmIj+nraTt9XA+EXSsH/eZN3aX63+YGxXIZqTDr/1kj2ADhF\n2Vjd85PjM57DXCuENAyCePaUugLo+3hsJWdK+INBMTI3Dt6PBLisoDHbOTUinuWR\nw/M4RPT9p6sUP4gkBpoIujH9b0N2iBzRYYnptt8pP5shOPT+vYIrMq062sDP39kc\nBgDIOhOqVDdwHibusD0gsi8fe1dEygQMokhxZSbQtCse7KEoGnd9aRaVm7meQV9l\n3OAMTa9zFbVgx3f4EtIHfsa81t/ck1ppB5ofMbZtFxay8K8NNrsKqwKAp0Kf+MwY\nnNr3Ck2s6vOrbftrojVsmw+zamRPb0M1x0DelTxyqzSg7R1yqqTR/TZ+64atD6fQ\nWdjNQymsJGwp+N9vxI0VA1sTSAoKypZC/xYdY3qUTTVmcV+9etR//byL1mCdnTow\n3SdgND4xvhTINxa4mjT3PWL6GN21y6g0FHz7kKAizKtX4nVUCCcjSmO83lMVUyFW\nAySD9KPtNbRguYwHTXnUCY/LF9KdcArFzW4dZR9PGmq1C5jj9QIcuC23pKESe0az\n5KbgZtFrS1GiO2p04LpQFa7UgY1MNogFvRYgYftJ/VasxoH+S2wpA58kfOnYmb4S\n2VlSPOiJ9vuIU6XH5iEk\n=Wz2f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T11:44:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDIwZDBjZWEzMDk0ZWMwMGM1M2U3NzA0OWQ1OWUyYzM3MDUzYjY3NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a","sha":"236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a"}],"sha":"20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/20d0cea3094ec00c53e77049d59e2c37053b675d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:38:22Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:38:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: make the useIsCourseLoaded tests actually assert (#2101)\n\nFour `useIsCourseLoaded` tests, for a pending query, a learner without access,\na failed outline and a failed metadata request, registered their special handler\nand then called `mockHappyPath()`. axios-mock-adapter replaces an existing\nhandler with the same method and URL, so the special handler was gone before\nthe hook rendered and all three queries succeeded. The tests passed anyway\nbecause they asserted `false` as soon as three requests had been dispatched,\nbefore anything settled, and the hook is `false` at that moment for every input.\nDeleting the four special handlers left them green.\n\nEach now registers its handler after the happy path, waits for the queries to\nsettle rather than for requests to be sent, and asserts its own precondition\n(the metadata query is pending; the outline or metadata query is in error;\n`courseAccess.hasAccess` is false) before asserting the result, so a test whose\nsetup stops applying fails instead of passing. `renderLoaded` takes the client\nso the tests can inspect it. Deleting any one special handler now fails its\ntest. The hook itself is unchanged.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2100.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd2c28ceafb186f0efce8941934413352bbfb140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/cd2c28ceafb186f0efce8941934413352bbfb140"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a","verification":{"payload":"tree cd2c28ceafb186f0efce8941934413352bbfb140\nparent 49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790163502 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790163502 -0400\n\ntest: make the useIsCourseLoaded tests actually assert (#2101)\n\nFour `useIsCourseLoaded` tests, for a pending query, a learner without access,\na failed outline and a failed metadata request, registered their special handler\nand then called `mockHappyPath()`. axios-mock-adapter replaces an existing\nhandler with the same method and URL, so the special handler was gone before\nthe hook rendered and all three queries succeeded. The tests passed anyway\nbecause they asserted `false` as soon as three requests had been dispatched,\nbefore anything settled, and the hook is `false` at that moment for every input.\nDeleting the four special handlers left them green.\n\nEach now registers its handler after the happy path, waits for the queries to\nsettle rather than for requests to be sent, and asserts its own precondition\n(the metadata query is pending; the outline or metadata query is in error;\n`courseAccess.hasAccess` is false) before asserting the result, so a test whose\nsetup stops applying fails instead of passing. `renderLoaded` takes the client\nso the tests can inspect it. Deleting any one special handler now fails its\ntest. The hook itself is unchanged.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2100.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs7ouCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4/MQAH5T02Rh91DcBrQ5ROqFHUIS\n8XlIXWxBf07/0r39WK8WJ+Wf0dJr4xBf4V4Y2yRk1frV8SfZ7mKCpZuEDPzyPSYI\nk9+z9pX2uI/rUvmkaqdUdkJkDPTdQemD5WT5LnZUQjJ42KtmYiyIqB+JKuAKkB6Z\nhgmKO57MIOgSHHM5P15gngBWqa57Z9bWRUftRVKClfUnwbkeDfGh5Z8wK+bIlgTl\nKRDlU8Ujb+/XKkz11/0nDHEizd69FPwqXDYc6ApAuKlkTieCE1yAYoNb9JaAEdWK\nBVLRitf5/EIjOoszYBU3yHKHgYdjeDv238VhIeG0AREXJ0IpwD33sVSR7svYnuYx\nXlbV4Po92avRr4xoRYpqUZQNeKdt7MHgznVGqzbykdXXltC1WvxJQfE32kdql9tL\nt3hQ+ns82lIf1JpUlKaRdl1rHN+7eerZGwoLSKf/bZ9c0DA7oKKWPohE8uStZOVG\n87j62f0M+AdwNblrK84sZr3QFQ2b/SA2ypGsvRO43UmY/dVdNiePVZQae32rZS4n\nI+9dil02WWU1SlDBACJxLKnRfY3nbXKn2Y3+PkZrJUBc788fptKNRWEglosrhv05\nPZ5RGrzh1JFnuFPphKPWiYmhag+/teZhETap+N6ojaGf/tFSymROItaVPEcicETT\nWc2uMUGo4PZJKMCqr9aW\n=fLmr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T11:38:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDIzNjUxM2U2MWI0NzI5NTIwNjEyYzQxZmIxNzFlYzVlODZlOTA5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154","sha":"49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154"}],"sha":"236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/236513e61b4729520612c41fb171ec5e86e9094a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:32:33Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:32:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: take tab identity out of the course-home metadata query (#2099)\n\n`tabs[].slug` was never a property of the tab. `course_metadata` returns one entry,\n`tabId: ''courseware''`, for a destination this MFE splits into two pages, and\n`normalizeCourseHomeCourseMetadata` stamped it with whichever page was asking so\nthat the nav''s `slug === activeTabSlug` check would highlight it on either. That\nmeant `rootSlug` in the query key, and one endpoint cached twice per course.\n\nNothing about a tab is an input to the request — it is\n`GET /api/course_home/course_metadata/{courseId}?browser_timezone=…` and the\nresponse is identical for every page — so the whole tabs mapping goes with the\nparameter rather than being reduced to `slug: tab.tabId`. `camelCaseObject` has\nalready produced `tabId`, and the endpoint sends only `tab_id`, `title` and\n`url`, so what remained would have re-spelled one field and filtered nothing.\nThe normalizer now computes only `isMasquerading`, and `course-home/data/` has\nno opinion about tabs at all.\n\n`course-tabs/utils.ts` becomes the only module naming a tab id, exporting an\naccessor per destination that returns what callers use — `getCourseOutlineUrl`,\n`getDatesTabUrl`, `getProgressTabUrl`, `hasDiscussionTab` — over a private\n`getTab`, alongside `isActiveTab`, which knows the Course tab covers both the\noutline and the content routes, and `getActiveTab`. All eight lookups move onto\nthem, so no component outside `course-tabs/` names a tab field or holds a tab.\n`CourseTabLink` keeps its `slug` prop — the slot README documents operators\npassing a custom tab name there, and `activeTabSlug` is a page name rather than a\ntab id, so that identity''s domain is wider than `course_metadata`''s and does not\nmove with this change.\n\n`useCourseHomeMeta(courseId)` and `courseHomeQueryKeys.metadata(courseId)` lose\nthe parameter, along with ten call sites — including `useIFrameBehavior`, which\nbuilds the key directly to invalidate it. Both contexts now share one cache\nentry. That does not reduce requests in the browser: `useCourseHomeMeta` sets no\n`staleTime`, so a shared key still refetches for each observer that remounts on it,\nand counting `course_metadata` hits across an outline-to-courseware crossing gives\nexactly 3 either way, five runs each. Collapsing the keys turns a cache miss into a stale\nhit; reducing the count is a `staleTime` question this layer leaves tractable by\nhaving one key to tune instead of two.\n\nThe tab factory emitted `slug` alongside a derived `tab_id`, plus `priority` and\n`type` that this endpoint never sends, and the mapping is what stripped them.\n`useModel` returns `any`, so no reader of this payload is type-checked and that\nfixture is the only thing between a missed consumer and a silent production\nbreak; it now matches the pact. Of the three tests #2023 added to pin the old\nbehaviour, the two asserting a data-layer opinion about tab ids are deleted and\nthe third inverts into both contexts sharing one cache entry. `discussionsPrefetch`\ngains the test it never had — nothing exercised its tab gate.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2084.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ad1b3c5a427a7f43cc8e774e5e9c54042fde51d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/3ad1b3c5a427a7f43cc8e774e5e9c54042fde51d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ad1b3c5a427a7f43cc8e774e5e9c54042fde51d\nparent 218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790163153 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790163153 -0400\n\nrefactor: take tab identity out of the course-home metadata query (#2099)\n\n`tabs[].slug` was never a property of the tab. `course_metadata` returns one entry,\n`tabId: ''courseware''`, for a destination this MFE splits into two pages, and\n`normalizeCourseHomeCourseMetadata` stamped it with whichever page was asking so\nthat the nav''s `slug === activeTabSlug` check would highlight it on either. That\nmeant `rootSlug` in the query key, and one endpoint cached twice per course.\n\nNothing about a tab is an input to the request — it is\n`GET /api/course_home/course_metadata/{courseId}?browser_timezone=…` and the\nresponse is identical for every page — so the whole tabs mapping goes with the\nparameter rather than being reduced to `slug: tab.tabId`. `camelCaseObject` has\nalready produced `tabId`, and the endpoint sends only `tab_id`, `title` and\n`url`, so what remained would have re-spelled one field and filtered nothing.\nThe normalizer now computes only `isMasquerading`, and `course-home/data/` has\nno opinion about tabs at all.\n\n`course-tabs/utils.ts` becomes the only module naming a tab id, exporting an\naccessor per destination that returns what callers use — `getCourseOutlineUrl`,\n`getDatesTabUrl`, `getProgressTabUrl`, `hasDiscussionTab` — over a private\n`getTab`, alongside `isActiveTab`, which knows the Course tab covers both the\noutline and the content routes, and `getActiveTab`. All eight lookups move onto\nthem, so no component outside `course-tabs/` names a tab field or holds a tab.\n`CourseTabLink` keeps its `slug` prop — the slot README documents operators\npassing a custom tab name there, and `activeTabSlug` is a page name rather than a\ntab id, so that identity''s domain is wider than `course_metadata`''s and does not\nmove with this change.\n\n`useCourseHomeMeta(courseId)` and `courseHomeQueryKeys.metadata(courseId)` lose\nthe parameter, along with ten call sites — including `useIFrameBehavior`, which\nbuilds the key directly to invalidate it. Both contexts now share one cache\nentry. That does not reduce requests in the browser: `useCourseHomeMeta` sets no\n`staleTime`, so a shared key still refetches for each observer that remounts on it,\nand counting `course_metadata` hits across an outline-to-courseware crossing gives\nexactly 3 either way, five runs each. Collapsing the keys turns a cache miss into a stale\nhit; reducing the count is a `staleTime` question this layer leaves tractable by\nhaving one key to tune instead of two.\n\nThe tab factory emitted `slug` alongside a derived `tab_id`, plus `priority` and\n`type` that this endpoint never sends, and the mapping is what stripped them.\n`useModel` returns `any`, so no reader of this payload is type-checked and that\nfixture is the only thing between a missed consumer and a silent production\nbreak; it now matches the pact. Of the three tests #2023 added to pin the old\nbehaviour, the two asserting a data-layer opinion about tab ids are deleted and\nthe third inverts into both contexts sharing one cache entry. `discussionsPrefetch`\ngains the test it never had — nothing exercised its tab gate.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2084.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs7jRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAje0QAAAC8ELD0w/Q0xWkHXLM6aWH\nEpdNY0/zUA4xbSt7fU0vEKixSkYiCeAvf2f1H6QgDD8M7bg+gBgf7+PaOeHJ6XQy\niU3NkB/lbSJDElBriVnweWiB/2vjm+W42/fTg7OxGU+pWnX1sLlKz/emSCaYenlA\nmZDsnTfSJpyXAM7d3UMFKx3BOCA+IoCBFtlqbLC4034V1QuOriJap35HVGwLL+h6\nWvR9SHNd+METfzf/NB1URV/R+74evhn+6pIpJD1qpW0SaMbq1obhPssDDQoeGNKG\nggv8+B87RaGLRKNIYtxsmE/E+dJPVWK/KX8oIkRrzYtT9SVLaCxH1ujtxkamtsJq\n5LbSyyt991vdaxqhJoCX2x4Wg3q1M5y7O/S3vMw8GqodUfpB+RK/48t/k77YbN/U\nEJrD8s/Xa44X9pl+xp5lvtaUKVbBJPbdqX6bBjYRcN4bRKla2qOloVE7AA7E7og/\ntkxaKJnSS6m/8CHToxTkqzW1V55rzFL9dAgiUanwqCAOHVTtawOTDJv9MfMC5xKY\nyW5Lfh9k+csUJbtI4qgmMMxZaXtBD3PPoTJ7FALudmJfZp+tFsiyKieqOIxESMjM\nFKp68EDczQFUZcyxkDb7dxtx222cePnwsw3Guct71E79xTvzGiB3haa9z6753u+m\nHgjbjfEEG5p1tj3L5XE8\n=Ns1J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T11:32:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDQ5ZTRhYzM3ZTY2ZDYxYTdkMmE3NTcwNjVmZWJhOTM3ZDlkMGYxNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935","sha":"218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935"}],"sha":"49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/49e4ac37e66d61a7d2a757065feba937d9d0f154"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:00:20Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:00:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: read the dates and outline tab data from their queries (#2093)\n\nThe dates and outline tabs have been query-backed since #1984 and #1991,\nbut their readers still went through the model store the bridge mirrors\nthose queries into. They now take the query result directly: seventeen\n`useModel(''dates'' | ''outline'', courseId)` reads become\n`useDatesTabData(courseId).data` / `useOutlineTabData(courseId).data`,\nwith a `?? {}` default where the reader destructures, since `useModel`\nreturned `{}` for a missing model.\n\nReaders pass `enabled: false`, leaving the tab as the only fetcher. Without\nit each of them observes a query that has already resolved by the time it\nmounts — `TabPage` renders children only once it has — and refetches at the\ndefault `staleTime` of 0, which made each tab load issue two requests for\nits own data instead of one.\n\nTwo of those readers are not the outline tab''s. `useEnrollmentAlert` and\n`useLogistrationAlert` are called by `LoadedTabPage`, so they run on every\ntab while only the outline tab fetches the data — they stay hidden until\nsomething else populates it. Fetching there would fire the outline request\non every tab, so they read the cache entry the outline tab fills, the way\n`useProctoringInfoData` already takes an `enabled` argument.\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` and `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` selected their model with\na `model` prop, so their parents now pass `datesBannerInfo` and `hasEnded`\ninstead. `ShiftDatesAlert` keeps `model` — it is also a request parameter,\nreaching `postCourseDeadlines` as the reset-deadlines research event\nlocation. `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` used it only to pick the model, so it\ndrops the prop.\n\nThe bridge keeps mirroring both queries: the access-expiration masquerade\nbanner reads `useModel(tab, courseId)` with a dynamic tab slug, the scoped\none-reader bridge the progress tab kept in #1998. All three entries drop\ntogether in #1999.\n\n`useOutlineTabData` gains a partial type for the fields its TypeScript\nreaders need, with an index signature so plugins importing the hook are not\nlimited to that list — the full shape is openedx-platform''s to describe, and\na copy here would drift. The sequence shape it names is exported as\n`OutlineSequence` and now types `SequenceLink` and `SequenceTitle`, which\nhad declared it inline and as `object`. The hook also accepts\n`string | undefined` like its sibling hooks.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2083.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f55e95a18cecf47bdd923e7b6188fdf3240cb573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/f55e95a18cecf47bdd923e7b6188fdf3240cb573"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935","verification":{"payload":"tree f55e95a18cecf47bdd923e7b6188fdf3240cb573\nparent 4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790110820 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790110820 -0400\n\nrefactor: read the dates and outline tab data from their queries (#2093)\n\nThe dates and outline tabs have been query-backed since #1984 and #1991,\nbut their readers still went through the model store the bridge mirrors\nthose queries into. They now take the query result directly: seventeen\n`useModel(''dates'' | ''outline'', courseId)` reads become\n`useDatesTabData(courseId).data` / `useOutlineTabData(courseId).data`,\nwith a `?? {}` default where the reader destructures, since `useModel`\nreturned `{}` for a missing model.\n\nReaders pass `enabled: false`, leaving the tab as the only fetcher. Without\nit each of them observes a query that has already resolved by the time it\nmounts — `TabPage` renders children only once it has — and refetches at the\ndefault `staleTime` of 0, which made each tab load issue two requests for\nits own data instead of one.\n\nTwo of those readers are not the outline tab''s. `useEnrollmentAlert` and\n`useLogistrationAlert` are called by `LoadedTabPage`, so they run on every\ntab while only the outline tab fetches the data — they stay hidden until\nsomething else populates it. Fetching there would fire the outline request\non every tab, so they read the cache entry the outline tab fills, the way\n`useProctoringInfoData` already takes an `enabled` argument.\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` and `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` selected their model with\na `model` prop, so their parents now pass `datesBannerInfo` and `hasEnded`\ninstead. `ShiftDatesAlert` keeps `model` — it is also a request parameter,\nreaching `postCourseDeadlines` as the reset-deadlines research event\nlocation. `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` used it only to pick the model, so it\ndrops the prop.\n\nThe bridge keeps mirroring both queries: the access-expiration masquerade\nbanner reads `useModel(tab, courseId)` with a dynamic tab slug, the scoped\none-reader bridge the progress tab kept in #1998. All three entries drop\ntogether in #1999.\n\n`useOutlineTabData` gains a partial type for the fields its TypeScript\nreaders need, with an index signature so plugins importing the hook are not\nlimited to that list — the full shape is openedx-platform''s to describe, and\na copy here would drift. The sequence shape it names is exported as\n`OutlineSequence` and now types `SequenceLink` and `SequenceTitle`, which\nhad declared it inline and as `object`. The hook also accepts\n`string | undefined` like its sibling hooks.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2083.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuxkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwKkQAKzYYo314mKbmV8BVm/3+A8W\nOyTRbv0VOpAmSuwkRKh7TLO86QowjU8TB5vcwaLTQPn28PRkVFnb1rKi6XWgO0cu\nlb0H2UI6jnSm6SFXk+wBLf8Ts1fsFRGItNs+Mv6KTZ+eZX6NqFv24WXMtHqlRHdX\nNM3YCaACoH3rcg2QW+bLb3npGTDoCqCG7iGUaqm8G5wAkk6vJ49fg/OL1kc3uHGR\nDrsagoKpANkVZzpJt662Yml9mWjhUhkU3qnZsdzIYdzse/3NhIWy7dK88Yh1DAZ4\nufl4ai1KfWg3a6GLw00cZayBgU5DsEZ09xkNHSTGXorTh5dNVK372DyBJ3fYAtaP\nb8IlKkSSeFLhmowfbWKvBKgSZt990+RM5LZ+k7kSSWdU/K7KYSe8Mf1Lzj5Vm2dw\n7v4x1fGlSZdbQLQTBPLXS6bCoe5R6bODNPyotloTPu6EtHo2Ps8v4pJVDC8Gp4RC\n9CDeRG8qor8yDAcqRDNr8Y3OxfvfbfM1PdArKzURm2bs/uw84Xxu+JZfRyNuhYZT\nOro+SRSrfN1b8sC5EVIJp1I3ID3TABVrTeoYF+5BMS3NzdETM2rnOZsYCP3NmJ7o\nSViRfXVPOJO1hILAiJbjZ8FNW6krlzRa/ZnkxB3yMo7ZobDd6Og3yrT+5GncyEgc\nzHRJDtA/sGwO5fQEKPr8\n=EU00\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T21:00:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDIxOGM5ZGZiNmE5MWYwNDRjYjYzZWNjMmI0MTk4OWZhNTRmMTQ5MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337","sha":"4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337"}],"sha":"218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/218c9dfb6a91f044cb63ecc2b41989fa54f14935"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:46:37Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:46:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: convert the suggested-schedule alerts to TypeScript (#2092)\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` and `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` become `.tsx`, so their\nprops are a `Props` interface instead of `propTypes` + `defaultProps` —\nthe destructuring-default shape `UnitButton` uses. Structural only: both\nstill read `useModel(model, courseId)`, and nothing else changes.\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` passes `courseId` to two query keys and to the\nreset-deadlines mutation, all of which want a `string` while `useParams()`\nyields `string | undefined`. Rather than assert it three times, `!courseId`\njoins the early return the component already has, narrowing it for the rest\nof the body. The guard cannot fire today — `useModel` returns `{}` for a\nmissing id, so the destructure above it throws first — but it is what lets\nthe conversion drop the assertions.\n\nPeeled out of #2083, which gives both components new props; doing the\nconversion first keeps that layer''s diff to the data-source change.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2091.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bdf5907a5b4bd2f7102ae97bfce2475a84fe287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/9bdf5907a5b4bd2f7102ae97bfce2475a84fe287"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bdf5907a5b4bd2f7102ae97bfce2475a84fe287\nparent a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790109997 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790109997 -0400\n\nrefactor: convert the suggested-schedule alerts to TypeScript (#2092)\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` and `UpgradeToShiftDatesAlert` become `.tsx`, so their\nprops are a `Props` interface instead of `propTypes` + `defaultProps` —\nthe destructuring-default shape `UnitButton` uses. Structural only: both\nstill read `useModel(model, courseId)`, and nothing else changes.\n\n`ShiftDatesAlert` passes `courseId` to two query keys and to the\nreset-deadlines mutation, all of which want a `string` while `useParams()`\nyields `string | undefined`. Rather than assert it three times, `!courseId`\njoins the early return the component already has, narrowing it for the rest\nof the body. The guard cannot fire today — `useModel` returns `{}` for a\nmissing id, so the destructure above it throws first — but it is what lets\nthe conversion drop the assertions.\n\nPeeled out of #2083, which gives both components new props; doing the\nconversion first keeps that layer''s diff to the data-source change.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2091.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuktCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmvIQACHIw92UtodLL8jApMxvWT7I\nNzBDdcz7tBdkL81VqHL/NPBMCH4HWn0a3OT4N5A1naL62LZevZAdXTuHQxDpC7DV\n+4Un+7lIa9lSGVFjG8jevyH5+nEhCYOxajAgplp7m5V4SuhFL//K+hCybpUVp0Ju\nuKSVx9wRJunzJmPZQS9fdAX7q5KC8kx1RX87olWLq4z1Ixj8JrZ5jhsxHr4QGfUE\nj8rFqrC2CFHasWKuaIG3Y1vJAe/I51faKC0H/OF87PBSpNzYbdbX3xKwRO4qmHyI\nR2kejjF4qiD7weAQIKAYpW0ye0Y3wr/d9JeQXT8f0ygGpIeZpNYiRTeQZSd7eejv\n599qLK+Vh3E3FIUHXxDIQ0rbqOMUimM3/wiT6Z0qMm2N5LHUJa14yZwu8O/oFFMU\nzqRMBqe66jiYzEeH13SD+hVxq0PbNLRhcwIvhqzaazwDcqXkOcQbckVVVLf4RFqO\n/xNmP+9dUEXikUELl+O1xKW8hwkBy47ghHGOZnCa35V8y6UMd6B13/1bunkaIunZ\nUH5CZLjAxf/COPOdWn2Kq3O9kHfIxEFxh6ic/hyH+/x5sPIKoa7tN9qDm835XI8S\n1Cj87+h8JRn3FFDiGcWHJTRA0tfcKhrYXa2qtUtE9iJtKEyPfYfpZ6d2U3vsLZnj\nNGaleNLT6Kg6hk6kBidn\n=suEu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T20:46:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDRmZTI2OTVhYWUxYzA5M2M4NzcwOWE1Mzc2MDgyNzAwZTdlNTkzMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004","sha":"a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004"}],"sha":"4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/4fe2695aae1c093c87709a5376082700e7e59337"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T22:15:28Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T22:15:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor!: move the plugin override registry off Redux onto React context (#2082)\n\nThe `generic/plugin-store` slice let a plugin rendered in a slot register\nan override for a host-computed value (`registerOverrideMethod`), and the\nhost folded the registered overrides over its default\n(`usePluginsCallback`). It was learning''s own Redux, and the only reason\n`store.ts` carried a middleware option (the serializable-check exemption,\nbecause the payload is a function).\n\nIt is client state — nothing is fetched — so it moves to React context:\n`PluginOverridesProvider` holds the registry, mounted at the route root\nbeside `ToastProvider`. The contract is unchanged: same\n`{ pluginName, methodName, method }` payload, same fold (default first,\nthen each override in registration order), overwrite on re-register, and\noverrides outlive the component that registered them. Plugins obtain\n`registerOverrideMethod` from `usePluginOverrides()` and call it from\ntheir own effect instead of dispatching it. New: `unregisterOverrideMethod`\nfor plugins that want cleanup. `usePluginsCallback` keeps its signature,\nso the unit component changes only its import path.\n\n`store.ts` drops the `plugins` reducer and the whole `middleware` option,\nleaving `models` + `specialExams`. The module gets its first tests; the\n`setupTest.js` module mock (which faked an empty registry because the test\nstore never mounted the reducer) is replaced by the real provider in the\nrender wrapper, and the unit test gains a case where a registered override\nreaches the iframe `src`. `generic/plugin-overrides/README.md` documents\nthe contract and the migration.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2017.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `registerOverrideMethod` is no longer a Redux action\ncreator and cannot be dispatched. Plugins import `usePluginOverrides` from\n`@src/generic/plugin-overrides` (was `@src/generic/plugin-store`) and call\n`registerOverrideMethod(payload)` from an effect; see\n`src/generic/plugin-overrides/README.md`. The `plugins` reducer is gone\nfrom the store.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4fe0175f02b7281c94dcbf6aa6feeff374d09a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/a4fe0175f02b7281c94dcbf6aa6feeff374d09a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/a9391edd38d222bd6d68566f4892c6bda9dbf004","verification":{"payload":"tree a4fe0175f02b7281c94dcbf6aa6feeff374d09a4\nparent a51108e1db95043ecc1e8ffb21fee0a808320d0a\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1790028928 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790028928 -0400\n\nrefactor!: move the plugin override registry off Redux onto React context (#2082)\n\nThe `generic/plugin-store` slice let a plugin rendered in a slot register\nan override for a host-computed value (`registerOverrideMethod`), and the\nhost folded the registered overrides over its default\n(`usePluginsCallback`). It was learning''s own Redux, and the only reason\n`store.ts` carried a middleware option (the serializable-check exemption,\nbecause the payload is a function).\n\nIt is client state — nothing is fetched — so it moves to React context:\n`PluginOverridesProvider` holds the registry, mounted at the route root\nbeside `ToastProvider`. The contract is unchanged: same\n`{ pluginName, methodName, method }` payload, same fold (default first,\nthen each override in registration order), overwrite on re-register, and\noverrides outlive the component that registered them. Plugins obtain\n`registerOverrideMethod` from `usePluginOverrides()` and call it from\ntheir own effect instead of dispatching it. New: `unregisterOverrideMethod`\nfor plugins that want cleanup. `usePluginsCallback` keeps its signature,\nso the unit component changes only its import path.\n\n`store.ts` drops the `plugins` reducer and the whole `middleware` option,\nleaving `models` + `specialExams`. The module gets its first tests; the\n`setupTest.js` module mock (which faked an empty registry because the test\nstore never mounted the reducer) is replaced by the real provider in the\nrender wrapper, and the unit test gains a case where a registered override\nreaches the iframe `src`. `generic/plugin-overrides/README.md` documents\nthe contract and the migration.\n\nPart of #1946 (Stage 1). Closes #2017.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `registerOverrideMethod` is no longer a Redux action\ncreator and cannot be dispatched. Plugins import `usePluginOverrides` from\n`@src/generic/plugin-overrides` (was `@src/generic/plugin-store`) and call\n`registerOverrideMethod(payload)` from an effect; see\n`src/generic/plugin-overrides/README.md`. The `plugins` reducer is gone\nfrom the store.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsayACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZbQQAFIHqDyIIqaiX8vHNTSrLgRP\nSYNXscY/BvxnldDm1nE4j5XFWHlsRE6PecUxrWHUFQrK8nSDvW3w/QZrC1RrKeuJ\nCkdzMlqE3x2lOb+GP0bHdG0aD9rWuDs4iQxN4dDnZUSUdI3jaqBfC8v8NPaUGRLD\n0CRjMIyfeSBGG+FQl/D8DuKEZKb5xK8H0Lhi7nUR5eX6e+dl3Ftk1HDRwn3dI+LJ\nwvxia9YSTcTr544Ym48g3xAYXUSvC5XATVbzHYRcDwgN9zrO/wn4oEkHAEF0oYFO\ncib8lMgasSiZtppTBkAbwKytLUSjsLZZ3YfTBNVwUYom1+k2riEV92pjdEAQhv+y\n91j8PJvrYuICmMNYp/4Sg8i1b6KYqNC+CYXJh5Uo4e9QtyLXv2PtZ+XB8Knmf8rz\ne3j1mEN5z4pT71SJx34bGCqnIxCvrpB6MDrPdtxWCh05R/38ljO8RTvt/JMWeP4g\niWLrf7APJG6PJ0Fbm0nyZ0eGVZ6BIAY6C8Fm1ZXtmOBwCiBK4YZCYl6TebAnoFC7\nOlhOywmh0vq6Y+MErmdmBRIwxZ3BH9UtYQBqrTR3f37GV36Z3cIFao18lnW5ZBa9\nFRLvxOINKGqZ12v6/99vH9L7wwrJBMWHtkZbZTpFZXEYPghIOQQS9KUAWwpHK3BB\nR+L8gjp+GdZYvjTv+d03\n=i+9Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T22:15:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_ev