45e800b2d76d90acbecd26a307fd3844baf99e10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/3f133b8c10ab29a9d1fa9c2d58157db62c566bad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:34:47Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:34:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: derive the courseware loaded gate and sequence ids from queries (#2071)\n\nAdds useIsCourseLoaded — the course bridge''s composite collapsed to a\nboolean, since every remaining consumer (nav hooks, breadcrumbs, the\nteardown''s redirect logic) gates on exactly \"loaded\"; the denied/failed\ndistinctions live in TabPage, which takes the raw queries — and\nuseSequenceIds, replacing sequenceIdsSelector with the same gate + flatMap\nover the section models (useModels'' shallowEqual + useMemo preserve the\nmemoization createSelector provided). useSequenceNavigationMetadata and\nUnitNavigationEffortEstimate convert; courseware/data/selectors.js is\ndeleted (its other consumers converted in the route-ids layer); the\ncontainer''s inline copy remains until the teardown.\n\nAlso defaults useSequenceNavigationMetadata''s entranceExamData destructure\n(= {}): it throws on the empty coursewareMeta model, a landmine the\nalways-set slice courseId kept buried and route-sourced ids reach.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e16ef25f1e960f941b7f7c40e587b5531fa2ab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/2e16ef25f1e960f941b7f7c40e587b5531fa2ab8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/3f133b8c10ab29a9d1fa9c2d58157db62c566bad","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e16ef25f1e960f941b7f7c40e587b5531fa2ab8\nparent 760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1789763687 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789763687 -0400\n\nrefactor: derive the courseware loaded gate and sequence ids from queries (#2071)\n\nAdds useIsCourseLoaded — the course bridge''s composite collapsed to a\nboolean, since every remaining consumer (nav hooks, breadcrumbs, the\nteardown''s redirect logic) gates on exactly \"loaded\"; the denied/failed\ndistinctions live in TabPage, which takes the raw queries — and\nuseSequenceIds, replacing sequenceIdsSelector with the same gate + flatMap\nover the section models (useModels'' shallowEqual + useMemo preserve the\nmemoization createSelector provided). useSequenceNavigationMetadata and\nUnitNavigationEffortEstimate convert; courseware/data/selectors.js is\ndeleted (its other consumers converted in the route-ids layer); the\ncontainer''s inline copy remains until the teardown.\n\nAlso defaults useSequenceNavigationMetadata''s entranceExamData destructure\n(= {}): it throws on the empty coursewareMeta model, a landmine the\nalways-set slice courseId kept buried and route-sourced ids reach.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqraBnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADx8QAERyYTx8jkP5YRIBIfMYx9Qh\n54VDa88+/NwXz75eZZzYH+w0TR56axSJVv4ctzJVklypeDDuc/cC9viHmEnKqD8e\nopVM0GxrWeqlSBN3shCPPw85Yjs3yzJyjKlS/hAc+AQbB7CNFx1EvN/6Dyl36NYf\nS3yWfqMB++NMfdjRzXnp7ZaIkArEFr/dNrYgA+wkD2gtGKUDLh7JPGSb5oRHoSQl\n3i24sxhYwNCnkv2A3/zKQ8u2aOCvxUAjsS6yUJkhcG6N1s+mSPUxw4dK7iuvKtv7\nGJGd1X8hjxBKTjXxlqoUgcJ5HW9Neoq+28PQxUnlpn6rnymCrVaT73oyfwd0aiRc\n5P8M3EBkzcDlM00aSPvX6qipz4WtROQ7epsUMmSy41/LVZwhbHf3MqnuDcXDa5Fj\nOhck/HE+YV4XjOghXmEUz/pTb0QmCnsd0fpUx/KXr4QLtZBE4FwOV+lXHYW3dtit\nA6dmOcTeR7RLINvvBv1ItHrqCnADRND/gGDAGKGOr6ovEs2ZNSzoAZd3Olu3RjI+\n0z/n+KYo7CPPs0oNuNl2puc7EUWN+POEeC4JA73+fZ4BVoVI6//lPbheyPdX3IHg\nkd2FbQ0B14ZlZJRm3Ww+lE1KzQsCaGfNQiv0cWRINJWaX12Rns7tb8TZtr8cGVC4\nphbmXug4xkJPMcFvGXM4\n=dV9w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:34:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/3f133b8c10ab29a9d1fa9c2d58157db62c566bad","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDNmMTMzYjhjMTBhYjI5YTlkMWZhOWMyZDU4MTU3ZGI2MmM1NjZiYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe","sha":"760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe"}],"sha":"3f133b8c10ab29a9d1fa9c2d58157db62c566bad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/3f133b8c10ab29a9d1fa9c2d58157db62c566bad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:17:02Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:17:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: derive sequence status from the sequence query (#2070)\n\nuseSequenceMetadata absorbs the route-derived preview flag (every caller\npassed pathname.startsWith(''/preview''), threaded down from the container),\nand the sequence-status readers — Sequence, both sequence-alerts hooks, and\nSequenceNavigation (whose courseId also moves to useParams) — consume the\nquery directly instead of the Redux sequenceStatus/sequenceMightBeUnit\nmirrors, gating on isPending/isSuccess/isError. The Redux status-string\nvocabulary is dropped rather than ported, matching the converted\ncourse-home readers; the 422-means-a-unit translation becomes the exported\nsequenceMightBeUnit predicate. The bridge keeps writing the slice for the\nremaining readers until the teardown layer.\n\nAlso fixes a latent Rules-of-Hooks violation this surfaced:\nSequenceNavigation called GetCourseExitNavigation (which reads models via\nhooks) inside renderNextButton, which only runs once the sequence has\nloaded — harmless while the status never flipped within a mounted life,\nbut a hook-order error once it derives from the query. The call is hoisted\nto the component top level.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d6eb2721a8db079639c0e787167c39c843f8f02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/5d6eb2721a8db079639c0e787167c39c843f8f02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d6eb2721a8db079639c0e787167c39c843f8f02\nparent e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1789762622 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789762622 -0400\n\nrefactor: derive sequence status from the sequence query (#2070)\n\nuseSequenceMetadata absorbs the route-derived preview flag (every caller\npassed pathname.startsWith(''/preview''), threaded down from the container),\nand the sequence-status readers — Sequence, both sequence-alerts hooks, and\nSequenceNavigation (whose courseId also moves to useParams) — consume the\nquery directly instead of the Redux sequenceStatus/sequenceMightBeUnit\nmirrors, gating on isPending/isSuccess/isError. The Redux status-string\nvocabulary is dropped rather than ported, matching the converted\ncourse-home readers; the 422-means-a-unit translation becomes the exported\nsequenceMightBeUnit predicate. The bridge keeps writing the slice for the\nremaining readers until the teardown layer.\n\nAlso fixes a latent Rules-of-Hooks violation this surfaced:\nSequenceNavigation called GetCourseExitNavigation (which reads models via\nhooks) inside renderNextButton, which only runs once the sequence has\nloaded — harmless while the status never flipped within a mounted life,\nbut a hook-order error once it derives from the query. The call is hoisted\nto the component top level.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZw+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArz4QAJ4kjy9UF0zWNMdFDKvjURFK\nozRqlrMcqvtMuNGEuBwoBugTdZCuAsGIQitaW59nYn6IXGuSs7dPwEbIQuZHSAfw\nEOsLGdDZ9N5RZNDmunynmiYza4AJVpzQG/4oiTvaQMMUnRV/5+HBY5bsa5FJkKfw\nohS1bT0zPfU2NDaCiOixJW1jL3DTcizVFFKZ3NxfyLRPUW6fU5sE0HXfIy4Jy9t6\n5fIueXsac6EsjnABr+CkkXodlA0WO+ikwoiZ67me91NjTCjB22a3cGaxuNsKi/KJ\n42CpcavGA8izhsJh77zy03Vwf4aqmlL9Qp+X+TIpr7O3F+rbum8epKQjM1M/HhzZ\nHgISRp3yWX8UKd9wzDQ/uvv2pOwiGgF9xHHlBEDDMCdu6w+a19qohSW2+Yzg7LXB\nekM6vD1vp/oPsL7WQL8jIUzBLXGNkmxitNMn9uz6xJ0jfNP0pJykURXbDaL/FwaP\nFD+Q036AozRYeVjqSQJeO03EvKEbsYXg6kb0fj6IY5S1XDtJwCaIm2qR4n37FgDC\nq3PKn+1kZdQYRM65rHjZrAAUlaWY9gauNnJkgJBwLUjOopPLv1/XXGEb3Tigtn77\n0o/3JfQf4+SaUOh+cQB+uclMol2YI29qTlHqmIF4AJx+D/gsIVJ8b73mAWOysN2c\n5ZJloElwHOqjnu1nqfwD\n=9CgE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:17:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe","node_id":"C_kwDOCvycV9oAKDc2MDQzMmE5ZWVjMTNhZTMyZGE5ZWQwN2IxNzhlNjU0NDZhOGIwZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commit/e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24","sha":"e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24"}],"sha":"760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/760432a9eec13ae32da9ed07b178e65446a8b0fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112954497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-smith-tcril","id":112954497,"login":"brian-smith-tcril","node_id":"U_kgDOBruMgQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-smith-tcril","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/commits/e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:09:10Z","email":"112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brian Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:09:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: read courseware route ids from useParams, not the Redux slice (#2069)\n\nThe courseware slice''s courseId/sequenceId are written only by the\nstatusBridge hooks, which dispatch the route params verbatim — so the\nreaders that consume just those id mirrors can read the route directly.\nConverts useIFrameBehavior, the outline-sidebar hook (also dropping its\nunread sequenceStatus return), UnitButton, useContextId (whose dead\ncourseHome fallback goes), and the course-exit readers (CourseCelebration,\nCourseInProgress, CourseNonPassing, CatalogSuggestion, UpgradeFootnote,\nCourseRecommendations). Status reads are untouched; the bridge keeps\nwriting the slice for them until the teardown layer.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e09ea283a60b46a56c9f9f3bdc97db09c89311b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/trees/3e09ea283a60b46a56c9f9f3bdc97db09c89311b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-learning/git/commits/e097ceb4a09dec6b00921f45383ae61c8613ca24","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e09ea283a60b46a56c9f9f3bdc97db09c89311b\nparent d0996516f9226145da3c8bb8ae54091facb7217e\nauthor Brian Smith <112954497+brian-smith-tcril@users.noreply.github.com> 1789762150 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789762150 -0400\n\nrefactor: read courseware route ids from useParams, not the Redux slice (#2069)\n\nThe courseware slice''s courseId/sequenceId are written only by the\nstatusBridge hooks, which dispatch the route params verbatim — so the\nreaders that consume just those id mirrors can read the route directly.\nConverts useIFrameBehavior, the outline-sidebar hook (also dropping its\nunread sequenceStatus return), UnitButton, useContextId (whose dead\ncourseHome fallback goes), and the course-exit readers (CourseCelebration,\nCourseInProgress, CourseNonPassing, CatalogSuggestion, UpgradeFootnote,\nCourseRecommendations). Status reads are untouched; the bridge keeps\nwriting the slice for them until the teardown layer.\n\nPart of #1976.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZpmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf/gQAKHKkIynmjkeVQCY997CB53s\nvN8S6QA9QbAcTUa4ikF/U4hzN+5dZOjnY4zC0nqBVIGKPnaxFAToPvpLQkei6DJR\nwkmiCtEnX6uzHTkfJ4OXaoyWklxVJpxrhLQobLkEXxJHM/fhry7aTjgM0dYgMUNT\n1VWwlQ7Z0kCPlOpdgcAMJN2UAkOCjyrq+oaJF+gO3ahltmoP9s007F6uA88PDgnw\nUKt5/KTYJK1IWLmSRqaPFGZzyAWIazGnrnHUHH9f4sLdVh9jTl0S+gcjemEV9ppl\nNqQ2MQM1pzSWZD4gNII3sqFZvwjAUUy+zvPmZ6+CTOSRjlqor5kpbPb8ZmlIbBcL\nhnPj5A9fwN9ubcurw8u2xz4vSEJi0MJBPhawMH79oBD0f4EJ7AVrdMLijxeSKUHB\nFATmuLvNepk32OJFDK7ObQVIZ7FC8twJAZyjp8juRNGkfj6wxJu7F1OvZxfXULT8\n13ngqRWTCnGhOriCXbwCzldwxJWDsjiymxzRD8brAoJyoLzpwDRgw8IACkfAsUa6\nPB01T6w07ClYZxwUgABIysceoy5AA5ENI8B+JuyrNyNS+tK54V/P4CsfEBgfCxj9\nGj5zpmXWykgY2wOzaaeqZd