ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/0bb05b0e894e20fa001b249041ff601cf62d423a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:51:28Z","email":"40372497+williamjstanton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"William Stanton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:51:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(expandable): Expand accessibility guidance for AI codegen (#4174)\n\nExpands Expandable Storybook docs so AI codegen (and humans) can compose an accessible disclosure or accordion without duplicating built-in ARIA.\n\nThe Accessibility section now matches the Dialog / FormField / Checkbox pattern: minimum structure aligned to **Basic Example**, built-in `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` / `display: none` behavior, a three-way composition choice (single disclosure, accordion via Hoisted Model, navigation list), heading-level prompts, a requirements table, and anti-patterns. Usage no longer restates those a11y rules; the first example is titled **Basic Example**.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nCo-authored-by: William Stanton <william.stanton@workday.com>\nCo-authored-by: @cursoragent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebc6c703241a89c39a1099e024b76495ee3119f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/trees/ebc6c703241a89c39a1099e024b76495ee3119f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/commits/0bb05b0e894e20fa001b249041ff601cf62d423a","verification":{"payload":"tree ebc6c703241a89c39a1099e024b76495ee3119f9\nparent 8743b8d9f111efb6d11b7a8e2c5d233d311dd35b\nauthor William Stanton <40372497+williamjstanton@users.noreply.github.com> 1790884288 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790884288 -0600\n\ndocs(expandable): Expand accessibility guidance for AI codegen (#4174)\n\nExpands Expandable Storybook docs so AI codegen (and humans) can compose an accessible disclosure or accordion without duplicating built-in ARIA.\n\nThe Accessibility section now matches the Dialog / FormField / Checkbox pattern: minimum structure aligned to **Basic Example**, built-in `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` / `display: none` behavior, a three-way composition choice (single disclosure, accordion via Hoisted Model, navigation list), heading-level prompts, a requirements table, and anti-patterns. Usage no longer restates those a11y rules; the first example is titled **Basic Example**.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nCo-authored-by: William Stanton <william.stanton@workday.com>\nCo-authored-by: @cursoragent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvrnACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA92AQAGCyW4duJkfm7fwpqdOhoJoe\nCJnb9vFqRMz5A+I9u6KVQUxpD9X5ksh3RKgpNNUrdAMuv9zp6mhRGkiEVu/MW9sA\nlOM6hAjdvtjX2K52t7Cm448jsvzRr5aA8dLotOHGmo9BhbakF5KSORTp6MUK4VeM\n74cifvIN04NCE2/3/cnUV499VLda9ATTUwGZ86+Ijql0BJ2S8h/5bWlt82Re9+zZ\nN4zv/0XGTsPqLtcaJ4Tx7Hixo+HsiVH7n1LLMD+uS7HDRsra7naDFVkYIWykFHDC\nYuLk5K0DcAGUju3e8WbJerGF/ix9m4OQdOqTdbGrwau+bs/DowsLr6KY8oRFtyHp\ncDR4++jv/Wvc8b+GCInY3+G2Ff3KMQkz2loGoBn3ZL2HyU9SeHzaPTT66YWO2f08\n3rReMpQxZHc/cwQeyEHkt95Vc54uX21a84P6EMA+a4a2tXe8K2R9nLLavalNGmze\nXRRGXMLZE0W94BjdxblhYRlq3TE5O3BQL007cdVkWbNtL85hWE5Gwa9FJfCl4G7y\nbDGgJs1113M4MltkYEPRxrVBLUUjw+6/WMx9mdErgmZVFsLsA/ap43F4eyLH0G2W\nujADTzboeHLedgumnBNwNRW9Rqw79uYyKtmsf1lIHfGKjqocGKG/NM4GTe2k6N6N\n8jcTgzJhgOmeKnVovOVy\n=Fc1e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T19:51:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.