mmit/945e2de7e77180c089e101727dcfa3c04019759e","node_id":"C_kwDOCwpuNtoAKDk0NWUyZGU3ZTc3MTgwYzA4OWUxMDE3MjdkY2ZhM2MwNDAxOTc1OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/commit/b03bc7c747476d1832220c0cd8f8f36eb3973913","sha":"b03bc7c747476d1832220c0cd8f8f36eb3973913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/b03bc7c747476d1832220c0cd8f8f36eb3973913"}],"sha":"945e2de7e77180c089e101727dcfa3c04019759e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/945e2de7e77180c089e101727dcfa3c04019759e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7966550?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mannycarrera4","id":7966550,"login":"mannycarrera4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NjY1NTA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mannycarrera4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/b03bc7c747476d1832220c0cd8f8f36eb3973913/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:36:54Z","email":"mannycarrera4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Manuel Carrera"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:36:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: Add Agents Skills (#4136)\n\nFixes: https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/issues/4134\n\nAdds a set of consumer-facing agent skills under [`skills/`](skills/) to help AI coding agents (Cursor, Claude, etc.) build UI correctly with Canvas Kit — choosing the right token, applying styles the supported way, avoiding deprecated exports, meeting accessibility requirements, picking the right component for a use case, and building custom compound components with the existing factories. Also adds a `sana-canvas-kit-version` skill so other skills stop guessing which release''s rules apply, and a `sana-canvas-kit-review` skill for a report-only compliance pass over a diff.\n\nThis skill set targets the **current generation**: Canvas Kit v16 + `@workday/canvas-tokens-web` 4.4 (Sana Canvas theme). It intentionally does not cover maintainer-only concerns (`system.legacy.*` in `modules/**/lib/**`, `cornerShapeStencil`, Chromatic class twins, publishing) — those stay in `STYLE.md`/`AGENTS.md` for now, with a maintainer-focused pack called out as a possible future addition.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nRelease Note:\nAdds/updates Cursor & Claude agent skills under `skills/` for Canvas Kit consumers (tokens, styling, accessibility, component selection, design principles, migration, version detection, and a review checklist). No runtime code changes; these are editor/agent-only assets.\n\nCo-authored-by: manuel.carrera <manuel.carrera@workday.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d77bdb9f16a124bc3cfb86cdcc930fd39fb230b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/trees/3d77bdb9f16a124bc3cfb86cdcc930fd39fb230b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/commits/b03bc7c747476d1832220c0cd8f8f36eb3973913","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d77bdb9f16a124bc3cfb86cdcc930fd39fb230b\nparent ecd8756a79137742567e511e64bb7f1fa14f659c\nauthor Manuel Carrera <mannycarrera4@users.noreply.github.com> 1789418214 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789418214 -0600\n\nchore: Add Agents Skills (#4136)\n\nFixes: https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/issues/4134\n\nAdds a set of consumer-facing agent skills under [`skills/`](skills/) to help AI coding agents (Cursor, Claude, etc.) build UI correctly with Canvas Kit — choosing the right token, applying styles the supported way, avoiding deprecated exports, meeting accessibility requirements, picking the right component for a use case, and building custom compound components with the existing factories. Also adds a `sana-canvas-kit-version` skill so other skills stop guessing which release''s rules apply, and a `sana-canvas-kit-review` skill for a report-only compliance pass over a diff.\n\nThis skill set targets the **current generation**: Canvas Kit v16 + `@workday/canvas-tokens-web` 4.4 (Sana Canvas theme). It intentionally does not cover maintainer-only concerns (`system.legacy.*` in `modules/**/lib/**`, `cornerShapeStencil`, Chromatic class twins, publishing) — those stay in `STYLE.md`/`AGENTS.md` for now, with a maintainer-focused pack called out as a possible future addition.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nRelease Note:\nAdds/updates Cursor & Claude agent skills under `skills/` for Canvas Kit consumers (tokens, styling, accessibility, component selection, design principles, migration, version detection, and a review checklist). No runtime code changes; these are editor/agent-only assets.\n\nCo-authored-by: manuel.carrera <manuel.carrera@workday.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqFrmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiIEQAJynaLujibJfB+J5ZQR3jjKe\nGS94qGBT5CiJd+K94FO8xf+MNF0ivV39y8e/z4jHnfe6KJbmgDvJBPU7gRDC8jg3\nfq8Eh+jki9W5pE1/Gvd74AJBCVk6qaAUTDaMfp5cHSYJXRKRmkej2/D/fUSn5xjT\npmmbwDMeR7k+gEnKLSUOkmQFxFCIOVnnCnvc990ivo2VsM1hHfvcX1ELZAAT7nyR\n2tOLtbIo1erib9OvRgzNaEtjWHosxSmEGCWIBYwi8o77qnlVusSmT76DHrDqFmjc\nYB6CRQjYOLoHFIpCNH8UgjJh8QxfgCp932d4f8hSYSRf7/U+14cSuxIUvnYmzqyG\nEu5u/3XTZ+emuZZtYxjLhdhDpk4s23XsATQ9rFY24DGpbs9tWLyLoTCTLv3r8M3S\nk4VepPCrwIQyeuSNvDR9peKQMxpeiXSo1bh3hWEQXPK4MKOMrZn8nZpG8mV+gS+v\nwxck7Kt/hp39KWY+bHB73Ulbm2Ywc