ef4d151e1b552d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40372497?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/williamjstanton","id":40372497,"login":"williamjstanton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzcyNDk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjstanton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/79d455e9eda00102b89fa7f0dbf335d7c4d5ba3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:04:43Z","email":"40372497+williamjstanton@users.noreply.github.com","name":"William Stanton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:04:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(table): Expand accessibility guidance and table pattern guides` (#4159)\n\nTable is a styled native HTML table with no model or built-in sort/filter/select/expand behavior. Teams and AI codegen were inventing ARIA (or collapsing every advanced pattern onto one page) instead of following researched Canvas Kit table patterns.\n\nThis PR:\n\n- Adds a codegen-oriented **Accessibility** section on the Table docs page (`modules/react/table/stories/Table.mdx`): minimum structure, built-in native semantics, requirements (caption vs `aria-labelledby`, `scope`, overflow `tabIndex`), and anti-patterns.\n- Splits the old `TablesAdvanced` examples into **Guides > Accessibility > Table Patterns** (Overview plus Expandable Rows, Nested Rows, Selectable Rows, Filterable/Sortable Column Headers, With Form Fields).\n- Adds a **Nested Rows** example: hierarchy as extra `<tr>`s in one table (not a `colspan` panel and not a nested `<table>`).\n- Updates selectable-row checkboxes so each control has a shared “Select Row” name plus `aria-describedby` to the row header.\n- Removes the unused Inline Portals testing example and updates MCP + `AGENTS.md` links to the new table doc paths.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nCo-authored-by: William Stanton <william.stanton@workday.com>\nCo-authored-by: @cursoragent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"d48a3c8c5b9b678e562ce7fed21656f558ef2c8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/trees/d48a3c8c5b9b678e562ce7fed21656f558ef2c8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/commits/79d455e9eda00102b89fa7f0dbf335d7c4d5ba3d","verification":{"payload":"tree d48a3c8c5b9b678e562ce7fed21656f558ef2c8f\nparent dd1a615f55e73a45836ac2ef7056dc1fb95ba1cd\nauthor William Stanton <40372497+williamjstanton@users.noreply.github.com> 1788361483 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788361483 -0600\n\ndocs(table): Expand accessibility guidance and table pattern guides` (#4159)\n\nTable is a styled native HTML table with no model or built-in sort/filter/select/expand behavior. Teams and AI codegen were inventing ARIA (or collapsing every advanced pattern onto one page) instead of following researched Canvas Kit table patterns.\n\nThis PR:\n\n- Adds a codegen-oriented **Accessibility** section on the Table docs page (`modules/react/table/stories/Table.mdx`): minimum structure, built-in native semantics, requirements (caption vs `aria-labelledby`, `scope`, overflow `tabIndex`), and anti-patterns.\n- Splits the old `TablesAdvanced` examples into **Guides > Accessibility > Table Patterns** (Overview plus Expandable Rows, Nested Rows, Selectable Rows, Filterable/Sortable Column Headers, With Form Fields).\n- Adds a **Nested Rows** example: hierarchy as extra `<tr>`s in one table (not a `colspan` panel and not a nested `<table>`).\n- Updates selectable-row checkboxes so each control has a shared “Select Row” name plus `aria-describedby` to the row header.\n- Removes the unused Inline Portals testing example and updates MCP + `AGENTS.md` links to the new table doc paths.\n\n[category:Documentation]\n\nCo-authored-by: William Stanton <william.stanton@workday.com>\nCo-authored-by: @cursoragent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmDsLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZnYQAH8ls6WOBJYoEP5YDVPbKihN\nARyQSAzCBdHtWXLenlgGwVNVsJiUE6u/PSraQbEvXJCxV2NeFPazu2qnVDl++FUL\nd3VjW0BRfUSgL9/bheXV5QLtjL6c8TEXOxngmI7Es9qEfkanL80f4AkhmNx02R3G\nXqtTNE53GYKBjZNN8iovKCGsj4Jg/Fs6+f+ECWPsUtnjTmM5mDK2t8P517z+IGHh\n/P3zTbSAAeD9SVZMwBrBYnLBFNHZ3dC7WGfK4qNlXLJnjgpLzM4hTpCb/Xof2A+V\nD51r6wbxNOY2+Y0MklcIUwQdLdBw2WomDSq2cx508BflQRGCFkClvQ82N7bfpI19\nx8U69k3XUqOGQWFkV0X7IowvXHc8U7eTbvHP50ZZvW6DB1sRKYT3qn5TIWVo9yF+\n0U/81jSUwLBlpuf0pRSJXCc7nRd7wqix8KT0Iqv/eBJN7rGda5qRALEVeZ5VChCt\nqMMoxALBEQaPfl8Giphthip263d9bz/mH1Tue3jnYTpbHXsAdaFgXQe+cAv5eQSe\nq84MGhKNw5agGD1ITXBoyjGADJ2Tj+B2NO06kqRy0VcBrpkCtK7ToF8grNpkhRsI\n05I9/vZT62jHI318pFbADV1Qh+rHsN9pahBt147TDznLaYb65Jn6+oBt/i6PJ9it\n5y6YGxZ2ASNzJiTnOCt/\n=sagi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T15:04:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","n