","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/commit/6c40cc2093133da6a7f19d441f890edbb1da9f40","sha":"6c40cc2093133da6a7f19d441f890edbb1da9f40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/6c40cc2093133da6a7f19d441f890edbb1da9f40"}],"sha":"19b3f139f43842cf3d23a14afd175ef177471536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/19b3f139f43842cf3d23a14afd175ef177471536"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4818182?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alanbsmith","id":4818182,"login":"alanbsmith","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTgxODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alanbsmith","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/commits/6c40cc2093133da6a7f19d441f890edbb1da9f40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:07:44Z","email":"a.bax.smith@gmail.com","name":"Alan B Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:07:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: Fix npm publish failures (#4150)\n\nFixes: #4149\n\nRelease publishes have been failing intermittently when `canvas-kit-actions/release@v2` runs `lerna publish from-package`. Most packages land on npm, but the job exits non-zero and leaves a partial version set behind.\n\nIn [the failing run](https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/actions/runs/32310458799/job/96252223881), `@workday/canvas-kit-codemod` and `@workday/canvas-kit-preview-react` failed with `TLOG_CREATE_ENTRY_ERROR` (Sigstore transparency-log 409) while other `16.0.7` packages published successfully. npm trusted publishing signs each package with provenance; concurrent Lerna publishes can race on Sigstore writes, npm treats the 409 as fatal, and Lerna does not roll back packages that already landed.\n\nThis PR makes publishing more reliable and recoverable:\n\n- **Serialize publishes** — set `command.publish.concurrency: 1` in `lerna.json` to reduce Sigstore races.\n- **Retry + verify** — add `utils/publish-packages.mjs`, which checks the registry for missing workspace versions, runs `lerna publish from-package` serially, retries transient tlog/network errors, and fails only if versions are still missing.\n- **Automatic catch-up** — patch/minor/major release workflows run the script on failure (`if: failure()`). `from-package` is idempotent, so this finishes the set without bumping again.\n- **Manual recovery** — add a `complete-unpublished` workflow dispatch option on **Publish to npm** for finishing a partial publish without a new version bump.\n- **Canary parity** — canary publishes use `--concurrency 1` and the same retry path.\n\n**Follow-up after merge:** merge with `[skip release]` so master does not cut `16.0.8`, then run **Publish to npm → complete-unpublished** on `master` to finish the incomplete `16.0.7` set. Do not re-run the failed release job — that would bump versions.\n\n[category:Infrastructure]\n\nRelease Note:\nRelease and canary CI now recover from partial npm publishes caused by Sigstore transparency-log 409s during trusted publishing. A new **complete-unpublished** workflow dispatch option can finish missing packages without bumping versions.","tree":{"sha":"cc07e2c018aecca9cb1c6d2b3ec1503fe6596765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/trees/cc07e2c018aecca9cb1c6d2b3ec1503fe6596765"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Workday/canvas-kit/git/commits/6c40cc2093133da6a7f19d441f890edbb1da9f40","verification":{"payload":"tree cc07e2c018aecca9cb1c6d2b3ec1503fe6596765\nparent 8e142ad29f6e653c452102cbdb2b340e704476ec\nauthor Alan B Smith <a.bax.smith@gmail.com> 1787256464 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787256464 -0600\n\nchore: Fix npm publish failures (#4150)\n\nFixes: #4149\n\nRelease publishes have been failing intermittently when `canvas-kit-actions/release@v2` runs `lerna publish from-package`. Most packages land on npm, but the job exits non-zero and leaves a partial version set behind.\n\nIn [the failing run](https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit/actions/runs/32310458799/job/96252223881), `@workday/canvas-kit-codemod` and `@workday/canvas-kit-preview-react` failed with `TLOG_CREATE_ENTRY_ERROR` (Sigstore transparency-log 409) while other `16.0.7` packages published successfully. npm trusted publishing signs each package with provenance; concurrent Lerna publishes can race on Sigstore writes, npm treats the 409 as fatal, and Lerna does not roll back packages that already landed.\n\nThis PR makes publishing more reliable and recoverable:\n\n- **Serialize publishes** — set `command.publish.concurrency: 1` in `lerna.json` to reduce Sigstore races.\n- **Retry + verify** — add `utils/publish-packages.mjs`, which checks the registry for missing workspace versions, runs `lerna publish from-package` serially, retries transient tlog/network errors, and fails only if versions are still missing.\n- **Automatic catch-up** — patch/minor/major release workflows run the script on failure (`if: failure()`). `from-package` is idempotent, so this finishes the set without bumping again.\n- **Manual recovery** — add a `complete-unpublished` workflow dispatch option on **Publish to npm** for finishing a partial publish without a new version bump.\n- **Canary parity** — canary publishes use `--concurrency 1` and the same retry path.\n\n**Follow-up after merge:** merge with `[skip release]` so master does not cut `16.0.8`, then run **Publish to npm → complete-unpublished** on `master` to finish the incomplete `16.0.7` set. Do not re-run the failed release job — that would bump versions.\n\n[category:Infrastructure]\n\nRelease Note:\nRelease and canary CI now recover from partial npm publishes caused by Sigstore transparency-log 409s during trusted publishing. A new **complete-unpublished** workflow dispatch option can finish missing packages without bumping versions.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh16QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7wsQAJ9zG7/rWdJlJWpbE4mqVXzW\nMrdJC3bbSFqj/L4tjle41MaSVk9KHSifCBOpO8XfnQncM/WO5YoGTAv83euMaBjb\nPF/4oNj+FecZvJ7ZbUPqwI+SwPsRq1Z6qkV90OdQ3V5GncveSuue5wG8glNUm7RW\nNoUKE3/FEwM9YGK7bESMkeEyYU7NQ7rSwFtXsXNw7ku/1LbNU/rREVA11On3JE4a\nNyyo38+bJpnmzJuoXQ8PaHobBtCJsRFQ4h2AnClvPU7pqjSLyD0Gic3qXgBWAFOW\nWQgo+pxsi7fgrnfG7/60OIXJFDWxNqLvr9OkRC/ZERU2F1y0XUB2kdBOqgh0+HxS\ngIRNT4i4Ar+vq3Xy8c7GTUFXCImVMSkEEs8iBKIH1kQV4C/tfadCGzdzJRutTKJC\n791kZ85yaLF2wwOE+y9Oz+7NTPI5A2qIvyb+MpF7ayhQZerZksdwJj9RSxCx/fgL\nHc5rUehXQN8887wQjW6N1VDYHt6IAdlxWDAmVpeuGlEjrJVOh0j3fKh8ZBXDcuDI\nvEm9vm4waYnEMJrW+f66E52XMGgAquW88LslUEEnEnXrL0a+6sDDckd+aBmCQ8FI\n+92tDsVUya2bfAQKkIL5j8cTuNyNZ+k9V2zAam18xHybDpjkpUVeztWbKaO9kcMp\nvn/EGXdRVmpEXTu6lleW\n=heh0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:07:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organiza